owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/4da36739ad05ac6982e7367592b31e997c88aae3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:37:47Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:37:47Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"docs: make PLAN and ROADMAP report what actually happened\n\nThe risk table still claimed ''~15 skills'' at 25, and ''reuse rather than copy''\nwhile grilling was a verbatim same-name fork. Two mitigations the demo had\nalready falsified — tokens as single source, QA catching drift — were listed\nas if they held. Give each row a current-state column, add the two failure\nmodes the demo exposed (self-certifying QA, all-green gates), and record how\neach is now enforced.\n\nROADMAP separates ''SKILL.md written'' from ''actually run against the demo'',\nsince Phase 2 was checked off on the former. site-wayfinder, conversion-audit\nand copy-pass are honestly still unrun. Phase 3 gets an entry condition:\nconverge the 25 entry points before adding more.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f9913d7f8ebbaef3a4aa5c715ffcd3fa55e624d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/trees/4f9913d7f8ebbaef3a4aa5c715ffcd3fa55e624d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/commits/4da36739ad05ac6982e7367592b31e997c88aae3","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f9913d7f8ebbaef3a4aa5c715ffcd3fa55e624d\nparent e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785303467 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785303467 +0000\n\ndocs: make PLAN and ROADMAP report what actually happened\n\nThe risk table still claimed ''~15 skills'' at 25, and ''reuse rather than copy''\nwhile grilling was a verbatim same-name fork. Two mitigations the demo had\nalready falsified — tokens as single source, QA catching drift — were listed\nas if they held. Give each row a current-state column, add the two failure\nmodes the demo exposed (self-certifying QA, all-green gates), and record how\neach is now enforced.\n\nROADMAP separates ''SKILL.md written'' from ''actually run against the demo'',\nsince Phase 2 was checked off on the former. site-wayfinder, conversion-audit\nand copy-pass are honestly still unrun. Phase 3 gets an entry condition:\nconverge the 25 entry points before adding more.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLLCk0weNibKgMn+GKM53GFlOHW6Gh+w2RfUDpnUTxc0On8DJJPX7VP6YWKKSrVXRH\nPPaKRo9KiX2GUCvJw9vwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T05:39:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Alfred-Lau/skills/commit/4da36739ad05ac6982e7367592b31e997c88aae3","node_id":"C_kwDOTmwWq9oAKDRkYTM2NzM5YWQwNWFjNjk4MmU3MzY3NTkyYjMxZTk5N2M4OGFhZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Alfred-Lau/skills/commit/e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9","sha":"e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9"}],"sha":"4da36739ad05ac6982e7367592b31e997c88aae3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/4da36739ad05ac6982e7367592b31e997c88aae3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:36:51Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:36:51Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"feat: add pnpm verify and wire it into CI\n\nEvery defect this repo shipped so far was mechanically detectable and got past\na prose checklist anyway: a hex value outside tokens.css, three artifacts\ndisagreeing on breakpoints, a template link that breaks once copied, a\nsummarised design-rules copy. Prompt-level checks cannot enforce those; 13\ndependency-free assertions can.\n\nVerified by fault injection — reintroducing each defect fixed in this branch\nfails exactly the intended check. Writing the script also surfaced two real\nproblems: --measure and --page were in tokens.css but undocumented in\nTOKENS.md.\n\nCI runs the consistency checks with no install step, then builds the demo and\nasserts og.png is reproducible from tokens.css.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>","tree":{"sha":"12b91779a76619f73725f692345ce6477a97c03b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/trees/12b91779a76619f73725f692345ce6477a97c03b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/commits/e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9","verification":{"payload":"tree 12b91779a76619f73725f692345ce6477a97c03b\nparent 9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785303411 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785303411 +0000\n\nfeat: add pnpm verify and wire it into CI\n\nEvery defect this repo shipped so far was mechanically detectable and got past\na prose checklist anyway: a hex value outside tokens.css, three artifacts\ndisagreeing on breakpoints, a template link that breaks once copied, a\nsummarised design-rules copy. Prompt-level checks cannot enforce those; 13\ndependency-free assertions can.\n\nVerified by fault injection — reintroducing each defect fixed in this branch\nfails exactly the intended check. Writing the script also surfaced two real\nproblems: --measure and --page were in tokens.css but undocumented in\nTOKENS.md.\n\nCI runs the consistency checks with no install step, then builds the demo and\nasserts og.png is reproducible from tokens.css.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKNZI9BcpHiPjA98h6BUSgTviWk2k+2UuJjjJe51TemSV0puA6dLCMAqM+eRiykKZH\n2BwSXRqY8wvBNr5gsHDQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T05:39:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Alfred-Lau/skills/commit/e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9","node_id":"C_kwDOTmwWq9oAKGUxYjhhN2Q5MmRiNzhjZTNkMjUzODBkYjVlOGUxOWI1ZWZiNDdjYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Alfred-Lau/skills/commit/9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563","sha":"9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563"}],"sha":"e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/e1b8a7d92db78ce3d25380db5e8e19b5efb47cc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:34:05Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:34:05Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(demo): grade the ship gate honestly and run the quality passes for real\n\nSHIP.md had 16 rows and 16 passes, including a missing og:image recorded as\npass and a 404 that was actually n/a, and it stood in for a11y/perf/seo with\nthree one-line claims and no artifacts. An all-green first gate on a new site\nmeans the gate was not run.\n\nRun the three passes properly and land them under docs/site/qa/. They found\nreal defects: .flow-index rendered at 2.84:1 against a 4.5:1 requirement\n(fixed here at 65% ink, 5.24:1), the served HTML carries no page content, and\na third-party font stylesheet blocks the LCP element. Generate a real\n1200x630 og.png from tokens.css so that row can pass on evidence, and record\ncanonical/sitemap/absolute-OG as n/a blocked on a deploy origin rather than\nas passes. Outcome is now ''ready for demo review, not ready for public\nlaunch'' with six ordered open items.\n\nAlso restore the demo''s design-rules.md as a verbatim copy — the summarised\nversion had dropped the ''not only abstract gradients'' qualifier the hero\nleans on — and move that deviation into DIRECTION.md''s Rule exceptions table\nwhere it needs a retirement condition.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>","tree":{"sha":"adf1b7d9f90544c8760569b798069b94573001dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/trees/adf1b7d9f90544c8760569b798069b94573001dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/commits/9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563","verification":{"payload":"tree adf1b7d9f90544c8760569b798069b94573001dc\nparent 4efce5ddd1c8204af61905c8072e80044dc1cb17\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785303245 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785303245 +0000\n\nfix(demo): grade the ship gate honestly and run the quality passes for real\n\nSHIP.md had 16 rows and 16 passes, including a missing og:image recorded as\npass and a 404 that was actually n/a, and it stood in for a11y/perf/seo with\nthree one-line claims and no artifacts. An all-green first gate on a new site\nmeans the gate was not run.\n\nRun the three passes properly and land them under docs/site/qa/. They found\nreal defects: .flow-index rendered at 2.84:1 against a 4.5:1 requirement\n(fixed here at 65% ink, 5.24:1), the served HTML carries no page content, and\na third-party font stylesheet blocks the LCP element. Generate a real\n1200x630 og.png from tokens.css so that row can pass on evidence, and record\ncanonical/sitemap/absolute-OG as n/a blocked on a deploy origin rather than\nas passes. Outcome is now ''ready for demo review, not ready for public\nlaunch'' with six ordered open items.\n\nAlso restore the demo''s design-rules.md as a verbatim copy — the summarised\nversion had dropped the ''not only abstract gradients'' qualifier the hero\nleans on — and move that deviation into DIRECTION.md''s Rule exceptions table\nwhere it needs a retirement condition.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBLhEBcgcMPGxBvfkUSf+F3REP0OvBtnjKS0/9nc2fZrHZ7t84mOnKFKuR4uNfvY/8\nTllqnd1TbT9pB2IE/LqQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T05:39:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Alfred-Lau/skills/commit/9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563","node_id":"C_kwDOTmwWq9oAKDk2OTRjYmE5ODYyZmUxZTFkMjUxYjFkZWNhYjc1NGYwOTk2NDg1NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Alfred-Lau/skills/commit/4efce5ddd1c8204af61905c8072e80044dc1cb17","sha":"4efce5ddd1c8204af61905c8072e80044dc1cb17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/4efce5ddd1c8204af61905c8072e80044dc1cb17"}],"sha":"9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/9694cba9862fe1e1d251b1decab754f099648563"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/commits/4efce5ddd1c8204af61905c8072e80044dc1cb17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:28:31Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T05:28:31Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(demo): restore the token single source and separate breakpoints from QA viewports\n\nThe demo asserted ''uses tokens, no ad-hoc colors/fonts'' while App.css carried\nfive raw hex values and repeated a system monospace stack three times, and\nthree artifacts disagreed on breakpoints (TOKENS 640/880/1120, page-spec\n390/880/1280, CSS 639/640/880) with TOKENS'' sm and lg used nowhere.\n\nTokenize the missing values (ink-deep, moss, lime-bright, font-mono) and mix\nthe alpha variants from their base tokens. Declare in TOKENS.md only the two\nwidths the CSS actually breaks at, and note the 1120 cap is a layout ceiling.\nRename the page-spec''s table to verification viewports, one per band, so QA\nlooks at widths that exercise distinct layouts instead of inventing thresholds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>","tree":{"sha":"50926d329c0475105e5288a1b4ab645fbdc343ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/trees/50926d329c0475105e5288a1b4ab645fbdc343ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alfred-Lau/skills/git/commits/4efce5ddd1c8204af61905c8072e80044dc1cb17","verification":{"payload":"tree 50926d329c0475105e5288a1b4ab645fbdc343ad\nparent 6aff71fcb16376ce1b9d6a4dad8aa6906cac71d2\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785302911 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1785302911 +0000\n\nfix(demo): restore the token single source and separate breakpoints from QA viewports\n\nThe demo asserted ''uses tokens, no ad-hoc colors/fonts'' while App.css carried\nfive raw hex values and repeated a system monospace stack three times, and\nthree artifacts disagreed on breakpoints (TOKENS 640/880/1120, page-spec\n390/880/1280, CSS 639/640/880) with TOKENS'' sm and lg used nowhere.\n\nTokenize the missing values (ink-deep, moss, lime-bright, font-mono) and mix\nthe alpha variants from their base tokens. Declare in TOKENS.md only the two\nwidths the CSS actually breaks at, and note the 1120 cap is a layout ceiling.\nRename the page-spec''s table to verification viewports, one per band, so QA\nlooks at widths that exercise distinct layouts instead of inventing thresholds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Alfred榆关 <jian.liu@icloud.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGM