ern\nchapters rather than new files, per this domain''s own convention:\n- Reverse a String, Valid Palindrome (arrays-two-pointers-and-sliding-window.md)\n- Find All Duplicates, First Unique Character (hashing-patterns-and-frequency-maps.md)\n- LRU Cache, promoted from a prose-only pointer to a full worked Problem\n  with real HashMap+doubly-linked-list code (design-style-coding-problems.md)\n- Top K Frequent Elements via O(n) bucket sort, contrasted against the\n  existing O(n log k) heap approach (heaps-top-k-and-k-way-merge.md)\n\nAll four practice suites re-verified: 16/16, 16/16, 28/28, 12/12.\n\nTwo more genuine Q&A gaps closed: wait()/sleep()/join() in\ndeadlock-race-conditions-and-thread-diagnostics.md, and a \"works in\nstaging, fails in production\" systematic-troubleshooting scenario in\ntwelve-factor-config.md.\n\nThree stale question-bank indices fixed (content already existed and was\ncorrect, the index never picked it up): comparator-composition-and-pitfalls.md\nin 02-java-language-core.md, microservices-patterns-with-spring-boot.md in\n05-spring.md (plus a cross-domain link to 17-architecture.md), and the new\nwait/sleep/join question in 02-java-concurrency.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ac9c6bebbf412a17c31409015de4fc2cb6fb0a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/8ac9c6bebbf412a17c31409015de4fc2cb6fb0a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/b0f07cead7bffd213b2f375a7a543d0e0fdb259f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ac9c6bebbf412a17c31409015de4fc2cb6fb0a7\nparent 012358a7ea61b72cac34515eec781f11af896aa2\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790520644 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790520644 -0600\n\nfeat: apply Coding Interview Standard to 6 exercises; close wait/sleep/join and staging-vs-prod gaps; fix 3 stale question-bank indices (#156)\n\nUser shared a generic \"Honeywell Java Developer\" interview checklist and\nasked whether the Q&A section covered it, plus asked for the repo''s own\nCoding Interview Standard (recognition signal, clarifying question,\nbrute-force, optimized, pseudocode, compiling code, complexity, edge\ncases) applied to its 8 named coding exercises. Audited via subagent\nagainst all 50 checklist items, checking actual file contents.\n\nSix exercises got the full Standard, added to their existing pattern\nchapters rather than new files, per this domain''s own convention:\n- Reverse a String, Valid Palindrome (arrays-two-pointers-and-sliding-window.md)\n- Find All Duplicates, First Unique Character (hashing-patterns-and-frequency-maps.md)\n- LRU Cache, promoted from a prose-only pointer to a full worked Problem\n  with real HashMap+doubly-linked-list code (design-style-coding-problems.md)\n- Top K Frequent Elements via O(n) bucket sort, contrasted against the\n  existing O(n log k) heap approach (heaps-top-k-and-k-way-merge.md)\n\nAll four practice suites re-verified: 16/16, 16/16, 28/28, 12/12.\n\nTwo more genuine Q&A gaps closed: wait()/sleep()/join() in\ndeadlock-race-conditions-and-thread-diagnostics.md, and a \"works in\nstaging, fails in production\" systematic-troubleshooting scenario in\ntwelve-factor-config.md.\n\nThree stale question-bank indices fixed (content already existed and was\ncorrect, the index never picked it up): comparator-composition-and-pitfalls.md\nin 02-java-language-core.md, microservices-patterns-with-spring-boot.md in\n05-spring.md (plus a cross-domain link to 17-architecture.md), and the new\nwait/sleep/join question in 02-java-concurrency.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquS1FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy+0QAKIDImSIDTx7gZ8J/7fD/Pkm\n5oOrA8u/Ga48glkJ+qDJYf53t+Lx/FwX/kGK/35/PwFxuPZUwPE2sk4lDcirqmmI\nWXv9ie5H6cwUz45KfpWp9tJdZYwf3azx+TLNRw/Atmg2qXg8k4OCMmEacC8iEXWW\noWD3q3yEQ7eEGG8P6c