nagement) and asked for each explained per seniority level.\n\nAudited via grep: every concept was already taught in this domain''s prose,\nseveral in real depth -- but none of the twenty existed as an actual,\nanswerable interview question with a Junior baseline through a Staff\nextension, and this domain''s existing Interview Questions sections skip\nstraight to intermediate/advanced scenarios everywhere.\n\nAlso found two narrower gaps this new chapter closes directly: IoC was\nnamed as a topic tag but never defined in body text anywhere; only 2 of\nSpring''s 6 real bean scopes were ever named together. Fixed a real\ncross-link gap too -- Spring Profiles content lives entirely in\n15-cloud/twelve-factor-config.md with no related: link from\nspring-framework-vs-spring-boot.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"09d9a91fae213f73460aaadbb700e001638b1138","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/09d9a91fae213f73460aaadbb700e001638b1138"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/981aecc95fc804742b31f838860df1b6e338c6c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 09d9a91fae213f73460aaadbb700e001638b1138\nparent fee908bee2d263d4a9cdf2162573c2d6f14b08e4\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790481361 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790481361 -0600\n\nfeat: add Spring and Spring Boot Fundamentals chapter (T-2213) (#154)\n\nUser shared a widely-circulated 20-question \"Spring Fundamentals\" interview\nchecklist (IoC, DI, constructor vs. field injection, beans, bean lifecycle,\nbean scopes, stereotype annotations, @RestController vs. @Controller,\n@Autowired internals, ambiguous-bean resolution, @Primary/@Qualifier,\n@Configuration/@Bean, component scanning, @SpringBootApplication,\nauto-configuration, @EnableAutoConfiguration, starters, profiles, config\nmanagement) and asked for each explained per seniority level.\n\n