:"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/fee908bee2d263d4a9cdf2162573c2d6f14b08e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:34:12Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:34:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: add real Spring Boot wiring example to Clean/Hexagonal Architecture (#153)\n\nUser shared a social-media infographic showing Clean Architecture wired\nwith real Spring Boot code (@Service/@Repository implementing a\ndomain-owned port) and asked whether this repo covers it.\nclean-hexagonal-architecture.md (T-901) already teaches ports/adapters/\ndependency inversion in depth, deliberately framework-agnostic (a\nStripe/PaymentGateway example) -- but 05-spring/ only had three one-line\ncross-references, no worked example of wiring the pattern with Spring''s\nown annotations and DI container.\n\nClosed in place, no new chapter: the existing chapter (1.0 -> 1.1) gains\na \"Wiring this with Spring Boot\" section (a domain-owned port, a\n@Service use case depending only on it, and a @Repository adapter over\nSpring Data JPA), plus a new anti-pattern (injecting JpaRepository<T,\nID> directly as if it were the domain''s own port). Matching cheat-sheet\npitfall and flashcard added to the existing decks.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7bf046ecdb2205c017a61acfd0a70bce1742d382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/7bf046ecdb2205c017a61acfd0a70bce1742d382"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/fee908bee2d263d4a9cdf2162573c2d6f14b08e4","verification":{"payload":"tree 7bf046ecdb2205c017a61acfd0a70bce1742d382\nparent a46d7f86920100d8722ae758c6dcd9348d264c51\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790480052 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790480052 -0600\n\nfix: add real Spring Boot wiring example to Clean/Hexagonal Architecture (#153)\n\nUser shared a social-media infographic showing Clean Architecture wired\nwith real Spring Boot code (@Service/@Repository implementing a\ndomain-owned port) and asked whether this repo covers it.\nclean-hexagonal-architecture.md (T-901) already teaches ports/adapters/\ndependency inversion in depth, deliberately framework-agnostic (a\nStripe/PaymentGateway example) -- but 05-spring/ only had three one-line\ncross-references, no worked example of wiring the pattern with Spring''s\nown annotations and DI container.\n\nClosed in place, no new chapter: the existing chapter (1.0 -> 1.1) gains\na \"Wiring this with Spring Boot\" section (a domain-owned port, a\n@Service use case depending only on it, and a @Repository adapter over\nSpring Data JPA), plus a new anti-pattern (injecting JpaRepository<T,\nID> directly as if it were the domain''s own port). Matching cheat-sheet\npitfall and flashcard added to the existing decks.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquI60CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm8oQAIusgTdhSZWcT09NvgaMKmhc\nMahN60O4xSIqPYu2Ke28OnvpxrfKSNP4zIpJyinbc8JHx5cRV499h7PIT5b0kpXk\nWd8lszVoqoVjnfQd+2nYv+CJ9WbokLDDGbxSgcL39wtSfud7syfjTzjuQVlrW4px\nfbJNE4bqPMqBVFl7F6bL3jk+ew3J6AHVQpyAji6+hnUfBImxgw+o4wFDsSxP8QSq\nK0bgrN6F9D+GEZdlXM4osyRfe4dsWxb9fg6WC3FL+UHv3FUiqlXCU+HLB31aU1mQ\nezD+2zEofPUxHtxFnLIbn9PZS7j2w/4jxicQ99XChKUVBa6okoZuTWbIy3iLn31j\nSnmorNp3PqSvwLEWxqeadAwWtC/GKwQ3nP1tGeCIQNu3kxUA849aykQOHdCGVAQT\n9KKNk50im8sVMLj1r09mKfRPR5i0GG8W+tqHIImrvHbLtG