rs.githubusercontent.com/u/13798190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres","id":13798190,"login":"JuanMelendres","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzk4MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/a46d7f86920100d8722ae758c6dcd9348d264c51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:35:12Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:35:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: close Kafka message lifecycle gap (serialization step + end-to-end diagram) (#152)\n\nUser shared a social-media infographic covering the full Kafka\nproducer-to-consumer lifecycle (9 steps). Every stage already has real\ndepth across 3 chapters in 09-messaging-event-driven, but two narrow\ngaps existed: serialization (record-to-bytes, before partitioning) had\nzero coverage anywhere, and no diagram tied all 9 stages into one\nsequence -- each chapter only diagrams its own concern.\n\nClosed in place, no new chapter: producer-semantics-and-partition-keys.md\n(1.0 -> 1.1) gains a serialization section explaining Serializer<K>/\nSerializer<V> and that DefaultPartitioner hashes the key''s serialized\nbytes, not the key object. kafka-architecture-fundamentals.md (1.0 ->\n1.1) gains an end-to-end sequenceDiagram cross-linking each stage to\nits real depth elsewhere. Both diagrams verified rendering against the\nreal mermaid@10 pinned in mkdocs.yml before shipping.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"827506274d27121a5c76cda678ea180dd36d4225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/827506274d27121a5c76cda678ea180dd36d4225"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/a46d7f86920100d8722ae758c6dcd9348d264c51","verification":{"payload":"tree 827506274d27121a5c76cda678ea180dd36d4225\nparent d31d8035471bacdd0865775004cf4c2d382b21a4\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790202912 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790202912 -0600\n\nfix: close Kafka message lifecycle gap (serialization step + end-to-end diagram) (#152)\n\nUser shared a social-media infographic covering the full Kafka\nproducer-to-consumer lifecycle (9 steps). Every stage already has real\ndepth across 3 chapters in 09-messaging-event-driven, but two narrow\ngaps existed: serialization (record-to-bytes, before partitioning) had\nzero coverage anywhere, and no diagram tied all 9 stages into one\nsequence -- each chapter only diagrams its own concern.\n\nClosed in place, no new chapter: producer-semantics-and-partition-keys.md\n(1.0 -> 1.1) gains a serialization section explaining Serializer<K>/\nSerializer<V> and that DefaultPartitioner hashes the key''s serialized\nbytes, not the key object. kafka-architecture-fundamentals.md (1.0 ->\n1.1) gains an end-to-end sequenceDiagram cross-linking each stage to\nits real depth elsewhere. Both diagrams verified rendering against the\nreal mermaid@10 pinned in mkdocs.yml before shipping.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","