iew_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/8eeadfa4403901ab1bfd0e18a625e4901e8099eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:02:42Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:02:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add Project Ownership Narrative chapter + Project Deep-Dive mock round (T-1605) (#150)\n\nUser audited a Java-developer job-posting checklist (Java 8-21, Spring\nBoot/Cloud, microservices, REST, SQL/NoSQL, Kafka, Docker/Kubernetes,\nAWS/Azure/GCP, CI/CD) against the repo -- all confirmed already covered.\nThe checklist''s own tip named a real gap: no chapter taught narrating a\nproject''s full lifecycle (design/develop/deploy/support) as one story.\n\nAdds project-ownership-narrative.md (T-1605): a four-phase structure,\nwith the same representative example project narrated at Junior, Mid,\nSenior, and Staff scope per explicit user request, plus a scope-\nescalation table. Adds a matching mock-interview round that runs\nagainst the candidate''s own real project. Also fixes a stale mock-\ninterview count in syllabus/20-interview-preparation/INDEX.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fdb95116f522e8c87b4f2b77bf7a66885fad683","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/9fdb95116f522e8c87b4f2b77bf7a66885fad683"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/8eeadfa4403901ab1bfd0e18a625e4901e8099eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fdb95116f522e8c87b4f2b77bf7a66885fad683\nparent 329c08d9cbe62cfd690cffbf63de0d6f7f18f1f8\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790200962 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790200962 -0600\n\nfeat: add Project Ownership Narrative chapter + Project Deep-Dive mock round (T-1605) (#150)\n\nU