ly@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add System Design Patterns Recognition and Quick-Reference chapter (T-2427) (#148)\n\nUser asked for real examples and visual examples for 11-system-design''s\nexisting patterns. Rather than duplicating any of the domain''s 9 already-\ndeep chapters, adds a recognition/routing chapter mirroring 03-data-\nstructures-algorithms''s T-2120 precedent: a signal-to-pattern table, one\nnew example plus one compact Mermaid diagram per pattern (8 total), and\na decision framework for the three most commonly confused overlapping\npattern pairs (caching vs. read replica, rate limiting vs. circuit\nbreaker, idempotency vs. message deduplication).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ed915e4d789af5c89f662f7bcdc284e72c19fee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/5ed915e4d789af5c89f662f7bcdc284e72c19fee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/edf55f3aa2a18bff8110a4f395f574ec6236ba9b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ed915e4d789af5c89f662f7bcdc284e72c19fee\nparent e677521d5c7e7a0aec95c928c7b0993454bfba4e\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790105299 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790105299 -0600\n\nfeat: add System Design Patterns Recognition and Quick-Reference chapter (T-2427) (#148)\n\nUser asked for real examples and visual examples for 11-system-design''s\nexisting patterns. Rather than duplicating any of the domain''s 9 already-\ndeep chapters, adds a recognition/routing chapter mirroring 03-data-\nstructures-algorithms''s T-2120 precedent: a signal-to-pattern table, one\nnew example plus one compact Mermaid diagram per pattern (8 total), and\na decision framework for the three most commonly confused overlapping\npattern pairs (caching vs. read replica, rate limiting vs. circuit\nbreaker, idempotency vs. message deduplication).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude So