},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commit/4f08cb9df500b1f4c9c154291be8bceec3f3a1c1","node_id":"C_kwDOTnPgT9oAKDRmMDhjYjlkZjUwMGIxZjRjOWMxNTQyOTFiZThiY2VlYzNmM2ExYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commit/63eb2ce1ac2096c6d853ddd6366914c4f83fade4","sha":"63eb2ce1ac2096c6d853ddd6366914c4f83fade4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/63eb2ce1ac2096c6d853ddd6366914c4f83fade4"}],"sha":"4f08cb9df500b1f4c9c154291be8bceec3f3a1c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/4f08cb9df500b1f4c9c154291be8bceec3f3a1c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13798190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres","id":13798190,"login":"JuanMelendres","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzk4MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/63eb2ce1ac2096c6d853ddd6366914c4f83fade4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:40:01Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:40:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: close domain events vs. integration events gap in 17-architecture (#88)\n\ncqrs-read-write-separation.md and ddd-tactical-design-aggregates.md\nuse \"domain event\" extensively, and 09-messaging-event-driven/\nevent-driven-architecture-integration-styles.md covers publishing\nevents across service boundaries -- but none of the three ever named\nthe specific, commonly-made mistake at their intersection: treating a\ndomain event''s internal shape as if it were the public contract\nexternal consumers depend on.\n\nAdds Domain Events vs. Integration Events: Contract Boundaries and\nTranslation (T-2426), backed by a real, fully deterministic Java demo\n(practice/java/architecture/domain-events-vs-integration-events/, no\ntiming or randomness -- every run byte-identical):\n\n- Publishing a domain event directly as the wire message works fine\n  for a NotificationConsumer reading its \"total\" field -- until a\n  real, well-motivated internal refactor happens (double total ->\n  BigDecimal grandTotal), at which point the same consumer genuinely\n  breaks: \"Consumer expected field \\\"total\\\" but it was not present\".\n- The same consumer, reading a translated OrderCompletedIntegrationEvent''s\n  stable \"totalAmount\" field, shows 49.99 before and after the\n  identical refactor -- unaffected, because IntegrationEventTranslator\n  absorbed the internal change (and deliberately drops an internal-only\n  loyaltyPointsEarned field from the public contract).\n\nCross-links added: cqrs-read-write-separation.md (1.1 -> 1.2),\nddd-tactical-design-aggregates.md (1.0 -> 1.1), and\nevent-driven-architecture-integration-styles.md (1.1 -> 1.2) updated\nin place with related: links and body cross-references naming this\nchapter''s real evidence. New cheat sheet and flashcard deck (3 cards).\nDomain INDEX.md, overview INDEX.md, and changelog.md updated (9 -> 10\nchapters). validate.py: errors 0, warnings 13 (baseline preserved).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57a52d450aa1302587523b40fbd60177dba03ce3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/57a52d450aa1302587523b40fbd60177dba03ce3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/63eb2ce1ac2096c6d853ddd6366914c4f83fade4","verification":{"payload":"tree 57a52d450aa1302587523b40fbd60177dba03ce3\nparent 2993402b9bfbc253fe97fb2f6f4b2f94bc0d0884\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790098801 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790098801 -0600\n\nfeat: close domain events vs. integration events gap in 17-architecture (#88)\n\ncqrs-read-write-separation.md and ddd-tactical-design-aggregates.md\nuse \"domain event\" extensively, and 09-messaging-event-driven/\nevent-driven-architecture-integration-styles.md covers publishing\nevents across service boundaries -- but none of the three ever named\nthe specific, commonly-made mistake at their intersection: treating a\ndomain event''s internal shape as if it were the public contract\nexternal consumers depend on.\n\nAdds Domain Events vs. Integration Events: Contract Boundaries and\nTranslation (T-2426), backed by a real, fully deterministic Java demo\n(practice/java/architecture/domain-events-vs-integration-events/, no\ntiming or randomness -- every run byte-identical):\n\n- Publishing a domain event directly as the wire message works fine\n  for a NotificationConsumer reading its \"total\" field -- until a\n  real, well-motivated internal refactor happens (double total ->\n  BigDecimal grandTotal), at which point the same consumer genuinely\n  breaks: \"Consumer expected field \\\"total\\\" but it was not present\".\n- The same consumer, reading a translated OrderCompletedIntegrationEvent''s\n  stable \"totalAmount\" field, shows 49.99 before and after the\n  identical refactor -- unaffected, because IntegrationEventTranslator\n  absorbed the internal change (and deliberately drops an internal-only\n  loyaltyPointsEarned field from the public contract).\n\nCross-links added: cqrs-read-write-separation.md (1.1 -> 1.2),\nddd-tactical-design-aggregates.md (1.0 -> 1.1), and\nevent-driven-architecture-integration-styles.md (1.1 -> 1.2) updated\nin place with related: links and body cross-references naming this\nchapter''s real evidence. New cheat sheet and flashcard deck (3 cards).\nDomain INDEX.md, overview INDEX.md, and changelog.md updated (9 -> 10\nchapters). validate.py: errors 0, warnings 13 (baseline preserved).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsr1xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu/wQAA38Ks06VfEqWVc8VyS27S5m\nSY4qcCfpzX4L1tGy6hxotnuhE76iKv91Azq02FGmPcOqbQN+YRzas9aDMAsoR878\nyIaO+5KR+fddSuQUpHFEB8brx+kbwGkHS+tb8WJ0Ry/rEjaROWrs+RdJf4wdqqeh\nAdgfM65x16Uj7XHEpSfFyzfOwGjxr99h/SEK5jdeoR0m4wCfjHTvQSpnMZUY/5DH\nhBu0gSlxcwUzuNgYxJgJP0DLS4yC7eC2fYYX/dJuRLC0rkya8QJ7qzCJTMAoo