,"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres","id":13798190,"login":"JuanMelendres","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzk4MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/ccf2631118d5ae99820c6868d0ef63bb516f03e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:13:22Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:13:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add timed whiteboard practice tool (six-phase countdown) (#97)\n\nSecond practice-layer follow-up, same post-audit review as the\ninteractive canvas (#96) -- this one is the kinesthetic/time-pressure\nhalf. system-design-method-and-estimation.md''s own cheat sheet states\nreal per-phase minute ranges (Clarify 2-3, Estimate 3-5, API 2-3, Data\n3-5, Architecture 10-15, Bottlenecks 5-10) and calls running out of time\nbefore Bottlenecks a scored gap, but there was no way to rehearse against\na real, ticking clock.\n\ndocs/javascripts/whiteboard-timer.js (new, vanilla JS, no dependency): a\nreal six-phase countdown using those exact ranges. Two presets load the\nchapter''s own lower-bound (25 min) or upper-bound (41 min) pace exactly;\nany phase''s minutes can be hand-edited. Auto-advances with a beep on each\ntransition, Pause/Resume, Reset. No-op on every page except the one\nembedding it.\n\narchitecture-atlas/timed-whiteboard-practice.md (new): same \"not a full\nAtlas entry\" framing as the canvas tool, recommends pairing the two.\nCross-linked from system-design-method-and-estimation.md''s cheat-sheet\ntable and from the canvas tool.\n\nVerified real via a headless-Chromium harness: ran a full session with\n~1-second phase durations start to finish (6/6 segments done, 6 beeps\nfired, confirmed via a spied AudioContext.createOscillator count),\nconfirmed Pause genuinely freezes the clock and Resume continues it, and\nconfirmed both presets set the chapter''s exact minute values. Caught and\nfixed a real off-by-one during verification: the initial tick logic\nadvanced a phase one second late (`< 0` instead of `<= 0`) -- fixed and\nre-verified before this commit. Same scope limitation as the canvas tool:\nnot verified inside the live Material/mkdocs theme (not installed here).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50f1d232f4ea4c2413b968442e5dc5d369955d01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/50f1d232f4ea4c2413b968442e5dc5d369955d01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/ccf2631118d5ae99820c6868d0ef63bb516f03e5","verification":{"payload":"tree 50f1d232f4ea4c2413b968442e5dc5d369955d01\nparent 6ce0f3d6dccb951cbe6706b5b90ebb0d2b80346f\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790086402 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790086402 -0600\n\nfeat: add timed whiteboard practice tool (six-phase countdown) (#97)\n\nSecond practice-layer follow-up, same post-audit review as the\ninteractive canvas (#96) -- this one is the kinesthetic/time-pressure\nhalf. system-design-method-and-estimation.md''s own cheat sheet states\nreal per-phase minute ranges (Clarify 2-3, Estimate 3-5, API 2-3, Data\n3-5, Architecture 10-15, Bottlenecks 5-10) and calls running out of time\nbefore Bottlenecks a scored gap, but there was no way to rehearse against\na real, ticking clock.\n\ndocs/javascripts/whiteboard-timer.js (new, vanilla JS, no dependency): a\nreal six-phase countdown using those exact ranges. Two presets load the\nchapter''s own lower-bound (25 min) or upper-bound (41 min) pace exactly;\nany phase''s minutes can be hand-edited. Auto-advances with a beep on each\ntransition, Pause/Resume, Reset. No-op on every page except the one\nembedding it.\n\narchitecture-atlas/timed-whiteboard-practice.md (new): same \"not a full\nAtlas entry\" framing as the canvas tool, recommends pairing the two.\nCross-linked from system-design-method-and-estimation.md''s cheat-sheet\ntable and from the canvas tool.\n\nVerified real via a headless-Chromium harness: ran a full session with\n~1-second phase durations start to finish (6/6 segments done, 6 beeps\nfired, confirmed via a spied AudioContext.createOscillator count),\nconfirmed Pause genuinely freezes the clock and Resume continues it, and\nconfirmed both presets set the chapter''s exact minute values. Caught and\nfixed a real off-by-one during verification: the initial tick logic\nadvanced a phase one second late (`< 0` instead of `<= 0`) -- fixed and\nre-verified before this commit. Same scope limitation as the canvas tool:\nnot verified inside the live Material/mkdocs theme (not installed here).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqso0CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhXoQAGuJ9SbTKcrfZ8+/c/pzR0pv\n7ZRGFBw5CIB/Ew67PhBYTZfyXruyODmhq+bXQU9BsA1Zz1jYovpjZmscro6GqbqO\ngvFLEay8Ie5M/4XHicOn1UohHwwb9Sp5TcAZOY+TuxDYty0G25Ocg+AgVZ9k25RM\nMz5xUJD6+pxYba1bh7Sgyca2vRPXp3/r9t9CyVZhLxQ6bo0lCFGBhyx+F1JJ1h8V\n/Ng3QDKy6W3YqPGsionq0buY6Pm5diT1Yz9f3JYQx1MY07SbSAaDqus8Tm6+eoBM\nqES8f9SEWhYCVcRfNDwJXgGMHwQD4yRcgaHy3YCEVsAscOFwbGZ0+1JLCmWJ8SFf\nxnI5OAsh4Hp8sYCUDqItnbwPepomVSuafc41SM/HAJ0qZh13atLtRC6hJJmTgeNu\nX3y1OnyR4dK9iVSwMct8q3AssjnxYZjkOBwL90DNGRC8fv3bGMaUz93ztFmDdnuL\nO9gngVaue+gR