190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres","id":13798190,"login":"JuanMelendres","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzk4MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/6ce0f3d6dccb951cbe6706b5b90ebb0d2b80346f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:11:28Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:11:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add interactive system design canvas practice tool (#96)\n\narchitecture-atlas/ diagrams are all static -- no way to actually place\nand rearrange system-design components short of physical paper, despite\nsystem-design-method-and-estimation.md explicitly teaching a Whiteboard\nExplanation meant to be drawn, not just read. Adds a real, vanilla-JS\ndrag-and-connect canvas (docs/javascripts/design-canvas.js): add\ncomponents from a palette, drag to reposition, double-click to rename,\nconnect-mode + two clicks to draw a connection, export the layout as a\nreal PNG. Layout persists per reader per page via localStorage, matching\nthe existing checklist-progress.js pattern. No-op on every page except\nthe one embedding it.\n\nExplicitly labeled a practice tool, not an Architecture Atlas Standard\nentry (doesn''t follow the 15-element reference template) -- lives at\narchitecture-atlas/interactive-system-design-canvas.md with its own\n\"Practice Tools\" section in the README, kept separate from the Entries\nreference table and its case-study count.\n\nVerified real via a headless-Chromium harness (Playwright, reusing the\ndependency already installed for practice/frontend/service-workers-and-pwa/)\ndriving the actual widget markup and script: adding components, dragging\n(position genuinely changed), connecting (a real SVG edge appeared),\nrenaming, exporting a real downloaded PNG (valid signature, 16,555 bytes),\ndeleting a component (its connection was removed with it), reloading\n(layout survived via localStorage), and clearing. Not verified inside the\nlive Material/mkdocs theme -- mkdocs/mkdocs-material aren''t installed in\nthis environment, so only the widget''s own DOM/script/CSS logic is\nconfirmed working, not theme-level rendering.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afe8456b7e9e228d4075c7613942f3ca9fc16a79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/afe8456b7e9e228d4075c7613942f3ca9fc16a79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/6ce0f3d6dccb951cbe6706b5b90ebb0d2b80346f","verification":{"payload":"tree afe8456b7e9e228d4075c7613942f3ca9fc16a79\nparent 9f3e18c598dae6e86443ead7cfe178b21d7dd2be\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790086288 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790086288 -0600\n\nfeat: add interactive system design canvas practice tool (#96)\n\narchitecture-atlas/ diagrams are all static -- no way to actually place\nand rearrange system-design components short of physical paper, despite\nsystem-design-method-and-estimation.md explicitly teaching a Whiteboard\nExplanation meant to be drawn, not just read. Adds a real, vanilla-JS\ndrag-and-connect canvas (docs/javascripts/design-canvas.js): add\ncomponents from a palette, drag to reposition, double-click to rename,\nconnect-mode + two clicks to draw a connection, export the layout as a\nreal PNG. Layout persists per reader per page via localStorage, matching\nthe existing checklist-progress.js pattern. No-op on every page except\nthe one embedding it.\n\nExplicitly labeled a practice tool, not an Architecture Atlas Standard\nentry (doesn''t follow the 15-element reference template) -- lives at\narchitecture-atlas/interactive-system-design-canvas.md with its own\n\"Practice Tools\" section in the README, kept separate from the Entries\nreference table and its case-study count.\n\nVerified real via a headless-Chromium harness (Playwright, reusing the\ndependency already installed for practice/frontend/service-workers-and-pwa/)\ndriving the actual widget markup and script: adding components, dragging\n(position genuinely changed), connecting (a real SVG edge appeared),\nrenaming, exporting a real downloaded PNG (valid signature, 16,555 bytes),\ndeleting a component (its connection was removed with it), reloading\n(layout survived via localStorage), and clearing. Not verified inside the\nlive Material/mkdocs theme -- mkdocs/mkdocs-material aren''t installed in\nthis environment, so only the widget''s own DOM/script/CSS logic is\nconfirmed working, not theme-level rendering.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsoyQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS48QAIJeJ4rrGabQ+xXW+xCiPMEF\nDN8N0go00wSkdj+1ufkjUnM6lYtilALtgjFw+6d8FLHC4VFNKIRCxx34qh3w356f\ndQv8xAGnvQLs12CPETTcTlhghJI1sXAJHSGyJAt1Q7DiVdWaaqh1DxtvSuAeSR5h\nz0wy8Il7IJQRPnOos2hq00+SC4A4eTHWLWKcB8DEiZnGPQSPetDqgF5Ca5tF6gOi\nUGQ+ptrfw8G2x1dOsGYC8NZuuRXB66xmG4kb+JU3EEaU3Fs/LGSsYErIbzriHEoi\nt7USpHPs6gGT/0g7A2zCsH2LAMxmnU2Eswl4bQlxVHzTEN2Q+oDC