ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JuanMelendres","id":13798190,"login":"JuanMelendres","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzk4MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JuanMelendres","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/commits/df5e5e7911759b7994bbc0f9d425fdec96e8c671/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T22:45:58Z","email":"juan.mele97@gmail.com","name":"Juan Antonio Melendres Villa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T22:45:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: close prompt injection gap in 22-ai-llm-engineering (#94)\n\nllm-api-integration-fundamentals.md already names prompt injection\nexplicitly -- \"a real, documented risk category, not a hypothetical\"\n-- but never explains or demonstrates it, and no chapter anywhere in\nthe repository does either.\n\nAdds Prompt Injection and Agentic Security: Attack Vectors and\nDefenses (T-2306), backed by a real, fully deterministic Java demo\n(practice/java/prompt-injection-and-agentic-security/, no live LLM\ncall, no timing or randomness -- every run byte-identical):\n\n- SearchTool returns a real, attacker-controlled payload embedded in\n  an otherwise-legitimate result -- a genuine indirect prompt\n  injection payload, not a description of one.\n- UnsafeAgent re-parses tool output for embedded directives, the real\n  documented anti-pattern that makes indirect injection work: a user\n  asking only \"What is the capital of France?\" ends with a wiped\n  database (Database wiped: true).\n- SafeAgent receives the identical poisoned payload but never\n  re-parses tool output for instructions -- the structural fix, not a\n  filter (Database wiped: false).\n- SensitiveTools.wipeDatabase is gated behind a real, separately-\n  obtained human-approval flag, proven bidirectional: genuinely\n  blocked without approval, genuinely allowed with it.\n\nCross-links added: llm-api-integration-fundamentals.md (T-2300,\n1.0 -> 1.1) and agentic-workflows-and-tool-orchestration.md (T-2304,\n1.0 -> 1.1) updated in place with related: links and body\ncross-references naming this chapter''s real evidence explicitly. New\nstandalone cheat sheet and flashcard deck (3 cards), matching this\ndomain''s own convention. Domain INDEX.md, overview INDEX.md, and\nchangelog.md updated (6 -> 7 chapters).\n\nvalidate.py: errors 0, warnings 13 (baseline preserved).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03411ecd222dd8ab03eec895fe16f6df5bca1ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/trees/03411ecd222dd8ab03eec895fe16f6df5bca1ad9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuanMelendres/cracking-code-interviews/git/commits/df5e5e7911759b7994bbc0f9d425fdec96e8c671","verification":{"payload":"tree 03411ecd222dd8ab03eec895fe16f6df5bca1ad9\nparent dd118681cc09bcbbf622f9ee6f4e34894ed599c1\nauthor Juan Antonio Melendres Villa <juan.mele97@gmail.com> 1790030758 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790030758 -0600\n\nfeat: close prompt injection gap in 22-ai-llm-engineering (#94)\n\nllm-api-integration-fundamentals.md already names prompt injection\nexplicitly -- \"a real, documented risk category, not a hypothetical\"\n-- but never explains or demonstrates it, and no chapter anywhere in\nthe repository does either.\n\nAdds Prompt Injection and Agentic Security: Attack Vectors and\nDefenses (T-2306), backed by a real, fully deterministic Java demo\n(practice/java/prompt-injection-and-agentic-security/, no live LLM\ncall, no timing or randomness -- every run byte-identical):\n\n- SearchTool returns a real, attacker-controlled payload embedded in\n  an otherwise-legitimate result -- a genuine indirect prompt\n  injection payload, not a description of one.\n- UnsafeAgent re-parses tool output for embedded directives, the real\n  documented anti-pattern that makes indirect injection work: a user\n  asking only \"What is the capital of France?\" ends with a wiped\n  database (Database wiped: true).\n- SafeAgent receives the identical poisoned payload but never\n  re-parses tool output for instructions -- the structural fix, not a\n  filter (Database wiped: false).\n- SensitiveTools.wipeDatabase is gated behind a real, separately-\n  obtained human-approval flag, proven bidirectional: genuinely\n  blocked without approval, genuinely allowed with it.\n\nCross-links added: llm-api-integration-fundamentals.md (T-2300,\n1.0 -> 1.1) and agentic-workflows-and-tool-orchestration.md (T-2304,\n1.0 -> 1.1) updated in place with related: links and body\ncross-references naming this chapter''s real evidence explicitly. New\nstandalone cheat sheet and flashcard deck (3 cards), matching this\ndomain''s own convention. Domain INDEX.md, overview INDEX.md, and\nchangelog.md updated (6 -> 7 chapters).\n\nvalidate.py: errors 0, warnings 13 (baseline preserved).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsbOmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApWoQAJs4srIR8jzJv7cwdebtR9Oo\nCWS79eyE1b1czf9ZHRGdhNNqabJeAEnsIUO+JJyuxBbLNiBLkUcIc6DnaDwvc2hr\nOaauDpc58Ui997HBMF/zDOJ/N5OCz2rcn02tc9IHyi0JkdBp57qnTqIGgS1V5ZcI\nQHSU33+UWc4Ms0j/0S/1woqblUnDCji2