ived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/5b10869a2bd01aaff70a2e2c95889798c194f232","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDViMTA4NjlhMmJkMDFhYWZmNzBhMmUyYzk1ODg5Nzk4YzE5NGYyMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/b6a4c635eefaf6ff51d9c922c3ccde2c810ee079","sha":"b6a4c635eefaf6ff51d9c922c3ccde2c810ee079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b6a4c635eefaf6ff51d9c922c3ccde2c810ee079"}],"sha":"5b10869a2bd01aaff70a2e2c95889798c194f232","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/5b10869a2bd01aaff70a2e2c95889798c194f232"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b6a4c635eefaf6ff51d9c922c3ccde2c810ee079/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T17:23:22Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T17:23:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflow): rename the trigger step through the dedicated mutation (#23450)\n\n## Bug\n\nRenaming the **trigger** step from the workflow side panel fails with:\n\n> Updating a workflowVersion through the generic mutation is restricted.\nsteps, trigger, status, position, workflowId and coreWorkflowVersionId\ncannot be changed...\n\nRenaming a **regular** step works, which is why this is easy to miss:\nonly the trigger branch is broken.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is a regression from #23207. That PR added the server-side denylist\non `updateOneWorkflowVersion` and switched\n`useUpdateWorkflowVersionTrigger` to the dedicated\n`updateWorkflowVersionTrigger` mutation, but missed the call site in\n`SidePanelWorkflowStepInfo`, which still did:\n\n```ts\nif (isTrigger) {\n  await updateOneWorkflowVersion({          // generic mutation, sends `trigger`\n    updateOneRecordInput: { trigger: { ...stepDefinition.definition, name: title } },\n  });\n} else {\n  await updateWorkflowVersionStep({ ... }); // dedicated, unaffected\n}\n```\n\nThe observed request confirms it: `UpdateOneWorkflowVersion` with\n`input.trigger`.\n\n## Fix\n\nRoute the trigger branch through `updateTrigger`, which already resolves\nthe draft version, calls the dedicated mutation, marks the step for\nrecomputation and updates the cache.\n\n`useUpdateWorkflowVersionTrigger` now accepts an **optional**\n`instanceId`. This matters here: the side panel computes the visualizer\ninstance id explicitly (it already passes it to\n`useGetUpdatableWorkflowVersionOrThrow`), and without it the hook would\nresolve the updatable version from a different component instance. Being\noptional, the four existing callers are unaffected.\n\nAlso removes the now-redundant `getUpdatableWorkflowVersion()` call on\nthe trigger path, so a rename no longer risks resolving the draft twice.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `nx typecheck twenty-front` green\n- `oxfmt` + `oxlint --type-aware` green on both changed files\n- `useUpdateWorkflowVersionTrigger` unit tests green (2/2)\n- Not yet clicked through locally; the reporter hit this on a dev\ninstance and can confirm the rename now succeeds\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23450?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"480a34f823a712ab4739f26833881e08aacbed6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/480a34f823a712ab4739f26833881e08aacbed6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/b6a4c635eefaf6ff51d9c922c3ccde2c810ee079","verification":{"payload":"tree 480a34f823a712ab4739f26833881e08aacbed6c\nparent 9acc5c192fe94d619f0e1dcbb7282eae9344b265\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1785259402 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785259402 +0000\n\nfix(workflow): rename the trigger step through the dedicated mutation (#23450)\n\n## Bug\n\nRenaming the **trigger** step from the workflow side panel fails with:\n\n> Updating a workflowVersion through the generic mutation is restricted.\nsteps, trigger, status, position, workflowId and coreWorkflowVersionId\ncannot be changed...\n\nRenaming a **regular** step works, which is why this is easy to miss:\nonly the trigger branch is broken.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is a regression from #23207. That PR added the server-side denylist\non `updateOneWorkflowVersion` and switched\n`useUpdateWorkflowVersionTrigger` to the dedicated\n`updateWorkflowVersionTrigger` mutation, but missed the call site in\n`SidePanelWorkflowStepInfo`, which still did:\n\n```ts\nif (isTrigger) {\n  await updateOneWorkflowVersion({          // generic mutation, sends `trigger`\n    updateOneRecordInput: { trigger: { ...stepDefinition.definition, name: title } },\n  });\n} else {\n  await updateWorkflowVersionStep({ ... }); // dedicated, unaffected\n}\n```\n\nThe observed request confirms it: `UpdateOneWorkflowVersion` with\n`input.trigger`.\n\n## Fix\n\nRoute the trigger branch through `updateTrigger`, which already resolves\nthe draft version, calls the dedicated mutation, marks the step for\nrecomputation and updates the cache.\n\n`useUpdateWorkflowVersionTrigger` now accepts an **optional**\n`instanceId`. This matters here: the side panel computes the visualizer\ninstance id explicitly (it already passes it to\n`useGetUpdatableWorkflowVersionOrThrow`), and without it the hook would\nresolve the updatable version from a different component instance. Being\noptional, the four existing callers are unaffected.\n\nAlso removes the now-redundant `getUpdatableWorkflowVersion()` call on\nthe trigger path, so a rename no longer risks resolving the draft twice.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `nx typecheck twenty-front` green\n- `oxfmt` + `oxlint --type-aware` green on both changed files\n- `useUpdateWorkflowVersionTrigger` unit tests green (2/2)\n- Not yet clicked through locally; the reporter hit this on a dev\ninstance and can confirm the rename now succeeds\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23450?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaOWaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+mkQAFE/Bj6E4bXqzSKQmcLYSY22\nRwKPfiqxW8y7qYnNTjc78L/BC9T6yH7op/QsEwYallk124orriMEj+AAsOidC2o9\ncnoCAfWZ1n5ugLArn4ZjvtaBTUU3ivu/L7dDWwxvOxRZEIhOT7VZsJwG0sjP/5Q0\n9UoLp2v+V6LEtpGTiQVbjeW7rbF5uJPajre7POXjtFJ8IamrNVCBNKk2DrGEKB6z\n3+T54OHQvkXSiT7WcNy8gNAklykEtDckMsKTBMb8LOlBdubTgba944he5Btk52Yi\nYEKmmuQBPVXSEJ3IPbsQ7Awx6AYnLZ7hribzFxitBI1cbQHRS8ntgtbaVKXkpykw\nBOaZgZSKhEKzgyXwil8wsLucrNPOLmuKpjyWI8skCxJA6csJuVWf4vm+qRZ7nTj4\nF3bQYxYVgru2sBrNGLdhIH0UHkq1Xv6r4qwanGuwKG7kEd16g5QZouyEGEKs+s3U\nYf4TEnvOU3g5QW20dymxvlEsceAwKg13IpBQwgHTe7rHStTDZaBgssBOu4t3ZsYq\n3IQYNXncpn/kg04z9O4UOpBxMBWY34hwj+TDRr4g6hRLBvgltKJIc9fiLA8rQEgF\ntlflHxu7ACjuc2xuA/nzYMSCGI2mF4iG6JaN4mHD4T1iEOvGDuepeYDWeiRygOhK\nP8nh5hw6/3MuzUIDDUOu\n=zRtE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/r