s://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:59:33Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:59:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Unify remote element style declarations (#23263)\n\nFront components run in a Web Worker with a fake DOM. Until now the\nworker had a hand-rolled `style` object for remote elements and the host\nhad its own separate CSS-string parser: two implementations of the same\nparsing that kept drifting apart (several review rounds fixed edge cases\nin one copy but not the other).\n\nWhat changed:\n- One shared `createStyleProxy` now backs `element.style` in the worker,\nand one shared `parseCssDeclarations` feeds both the worker proxy and\nthe host''s `parseCssString`. Most of the diff is existing logic split\nout of `installStylePropertyOnRemoteElements` into small single-purpose\nutils (`splitCssDeclarations`, `stripImportantPriorityFromCssValue`,\n`normalizeCssPropertyName`, `formatCssValue`, ...), not new behavior.\n- `!important` is stripped from values instead of tracked. Nothing ever\nread priorities back, and the host applies styles through React inline\nstyles, which cannot express `!important`. Rendering note: `color: red\n!important` used to reach React as an invalid value (property silently\nnot applied); it now applies, without the priority.\n- Style writes flush to the host synchronously, exactly as on main.\n- The parser handles quotes, escapes and parentheses; CSS comments\ninside hand-written `cssText` are not supported.\n\nThis shared proxy is also the base for the worker `getComputedStyle`\nstub in the geometry PR. Second of three PRs splitting the geometry\nmirror work.","tree":{"sha":"6a9a5feb443187cdeba722da3ffc0ed2df349ddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/6a9a5feb443187cdeba722da3ffc0ed2df349ddf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a9a5feb443187cdeba722da3ffc0ed2df349ddf\nparent 64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1785243573 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785243573 +0000\n\nUnify remote element style declarations (#23263)\n\nFront components run in a Web Worker with a fake DOM. Until now the\nworker had a hand-rolled `style` object for remote elements and the host\nhad its own separate CSS-string parser: two implementations of the same\nparsing that kept drifting apart (several review rounds fixed edge cases\nin one copy but not the other).\n\nWhat changed:\n- One shared `createStyleProxy` now backs `element.style` in the worker,\nand one shared `parseCssDeclarations` feeds both the worker proxy and\nthe host''s `parseCssString`. Most of the diff is existing logic split\nout of `installStylePropertyOnRemoteElements` into small single-purpose\nutils (`splitCssDeclarations`, `stripImportantPriorityFromCssValue`,\n`normalizeCssPropertyName`, `formatCssValue`, ...), not new behavior.\n- `!important` is stripped from values instead of tracked. Nothing ever\nread priorities back, and the host applies styles through React inline\nstyles, which cannot express `!important`. Rendering note: `color: red\n!important` used to reach React as an invalid value (property silently\nnot applied); it now applies, without the priority.\n- Style writes flush to the host synchronously, exactly as on main.\n- The parser handles quotes, escapes and parentheses; CSS comments\ninside hand-written `cssText` are not supported.\n\nThis shared proxy is also the base for the worker `getComputedStyle`\nstub in the geometry PR. Second of three PRs splitting the geometry\nmirror work.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaKfGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJEEQAIc5Y+LO78s2W2un6dFfftlH\nRjqqyZ83vLDA6U+37T2+kxFFgrGLTdwLZemtSBW+gdD5WrYyJ/PrC1vVvKiLWEU+\nTpYo1+vEK84MJ/2pYLkgxyjFAVdFjaDKbyLN9p+o72IMws+KDhTMsluneZ9Pfy+X\n1IeJmIWgPnJaA5TKa5QWdemdxEf6SgRJ8YpGJ4fJyUPckfIxI/bYbWfZM1exD+0s\nH322tmkphA6bhTjAJrL2IRkdGbXP0tRtBLvkdSSNwIXTbpbHVAuWzC+kVbCdqc0I\nfMlSBgOAydUeYOhUA+4zWtmGnhAKBW71mDP5INz8Y5LxeqY7nh6UN2/5inRwXaXl\nf516+y+SQbwL0ax26CtDrXPl2Pac3kOiAuba87o87IzFccBUuzSNw84pxVdYHb9G\nOl/JUswgBwIRdpsp/JpDJFwK44r+5N0XIfIMDN3XFeiOmtAYKJHuyd8MuheuCGz3\na8hFMHIJNk3S/okJFuN1KC7uKsvdxyAO0fpOab8tNUGJQgVfAMLR2IdI99P7xmrY\n3uYM2KtddgZspxuqzh7ix8R7E/pYKtByy+MPRhEooBm/9nYBIJyqjPVamMpDNadZ\nmKibwKFfqQntaPZisN19h50HEl5uXBmidAr5e4WAYaZB4n7Ii8fLQzveOo8CYCwy\n+LfBTZCL9kI8pW64ieNg\n=KJYT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKGI4ZTJhNmU5MTBjMzllMWUxM2ZhZTA1ZDdmYzM4ZjVkOTJmNTAxNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed","sha":"64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed"}],"sha":"b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:43:55Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:43:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix numeric controlled input values in front components (#23421)\n\nA front component rendering a numeric input never showed its value\nbecause the caret-preserving path only accepted strings:\n- controlled: `<input type=\"number\" value={42}>` was rejected by the\nvalue sync guard, so nothing was written to the host element\n- uncontrolled: `defaultValue={42}` was dropped from the initial value\nseeding\n\nNumeric values are now stringified in both places. Also adds a test\nasserting `createCaretPreservingElement` forwards its ref to the\nrendered element.\n\nThe controlled case and the ref test were flagged by cubic on #23264","tree":{"sha":"11d55f3bd91f92b321ca8b7f302b9a33b83f9084","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/11d55f3bd91f92b321ca8b7f302b9a33b83f9084"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed","verification":{"payload":"tree 11d55f3bd91f92b321ca8b7f302b9a33b83f9084\nparent 4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1785242635 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785242635 +0000\n\nFix numeric controlled input values in front components (#23421)\n\nA front component rendering a numeric input never showed its value\nbecause the caret-preserving path only accepted strings:\n- controlled: `<input type=\"number\" value={42}>` was rejected by the\nvalue sync guard, so nothing was written to the host element\n- uncontrolled: `defaultValue={42}` was dropped from the initial value\nseeding\n\nNumeric values are now stringified in both places. Also adds a test\nasserting `createCaretPreservingElement` forwards its ref to the\nrendered element.\n\nThe controlled case and the ref test were flagged by cubic on #23264","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaKQcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJEIQAJSUZjlxrE6aGygnF6bUm/XP\nvhROLkGtn5tQyzUAMZM+3ZdVg6HIxdpPiEWllkjE9wODIQL981cJOgQqHmfd924Q\nrO4wKB1/UV2RfXtIYrg6DvQ3sizvSoeUZM1GiMxacltbRRKwVRqEjetVbALN7Mfn\nM5DsrxOZUKKuhcb2YcbRQ8iCnpGoEXizIN3bf8VIqjRXk6mitmpfnGRxVlwletE9\nqHKE9TU4pYtzRp2rTwAffwuo6RVBlr+Nrb2BMwqQgbXo7SknWD77jWWdDxBCMaNh\npzEun7alfkVQ64TGnhXGWsJAdzF5GObxY/H4G7Ynl9gH8duWoywlYZqfJCyK7XQy\nlHgH4rPqa44XEeQK3nO38fX7Lw9qrO6CuplE60InEQLE96XbCeur+J41vRDY7hXv\na8h0rPVwo0MvIJFNhc1bLNayM72RGSdnDduM+0LvYCVui77KcGqtlrIvwp/fZEYC\na2Rm9vTTvcPs97Srj1qqAJ+Z+1tsWx6pMIZ4gE40zZKICQQHJTdEAM1zg6kUXw6a\nKfw87Ajq7nTwVieJt/P9OkthVbQA2pGu0dzV7b4BM2JJEne63ZCdDwJTI2riYIca\nXCPuVl89LaZ4YLGkA1/juePnSG13Dy13DrNUmJpqqZoD1j2dA5jPOx/8WH7Ckxir\nc//jUqrgRK/BkTYy/tJO\n=b8Uw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDY0MDAxNTkxZjI5ZmZmY2UzN2Q4OTM1ODc4YzMxNTNkNjA1NGM5ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272","sha":"4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272"}],"sha":"64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:32:16Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:32:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflow): keep Limit and Offset when changing the Search Records object (#23423)\n\nFixes the second bug reported in #23387.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn the Search Records action, changing the Object silently reset `Limit`\nto `1`. A user who had set `Limit = 100` and then switched object (or\nswitched away and back) ended up with a step that returns exactly one\narbitrary record, with no indication beyond a small `1` in the side\npanel.\n\nReproduced on `main` against a local instance, checking the persisted\ndraft version:\n\n```json\n{ \"limit\": 1, \"offset\": 0, \"objectName\": \"person\" }\n```\n\n`handleOptionClick` rebuilt the entire form as `{ objectNameSingular,\nlimit: 1, offset: 0 }`, discarding whatever the user had entered. `1` is\nthe server-side default for a newly created `FIND_RECORDS` step, so this\nwas effectively a revert-to-creation-default on every object change.\n\n## Change\n\nCarry `limit` and `offset` over instead of hardcoding them. `filter` and\n`orderBy` are still dropped by omission, which is correct: they\nreference fields of the previous object.\n\n## Test\n\nAdded `KeepsLimitAndOffsetWhenObjectChanges` to the existing story file.\nIt switches the object and asserts `onActionUpdate` receives `{\nobjectName: ''company'', limit: 100, offset: 20 }`.\n\nConfirmed the test is not vacuous: reverting the fix makes it fail with\nexactly the reported symptom (`limit: 100 -> 1`, `offset: 20 -> 0`).\n\n## Not addressed here\n\nThe headline bug in #23387 (filters made only of value-less operators\nnever persisting) does not reproduce on `main`. I ran the reporter''s\nsteps with `Is in past` OR `Is today (UTC)` and both rules plus the `OR`\ngroup were written to the draft version correctly. Persistence hangs off\n`useUpsertRecordFilter`, which fires the advanced-filter `onUpdate` on\nevery upsert, so operand changes save just as value changes do. The\nreporter is on ~v2.18.x and did not re-test on a recent release.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23423?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"87c165399de1a447170e4aaadfc3b36e95156af2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/87c165399de1a447170e4aaadfc3b36e95156af2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272","verification":{"payload":"tree 87c165399de1a447170e4aaadfc3b36e95156af2\nparent 11447bd96f0100e90d99c221a6b7c7af10ccba2b\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1785241936 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785241936 +0000\n\nfix(workflow): keep Limit and Offset when changing the Search Records object (#23423)\n\nFixes the second bug reported in #23387.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn the Search Records action, changing the Object silently reset `Limit`\nto `1`. A user who had set `Limit = 100` and then switched object (or\nswitched away and back) ended up with a step that returns exactly one\narbitrary record, with no indication beyond a small `1` in the side\npanel.\n\nReproduced on `main` against a local instance, checking the persisted\ndraft version:\n\n```json\n{ \"limit\": 1, \"offset\": 0, \"objectName\": \"person\" }\n```\n\n`handleOptionClick` rebuilt the entire form as `{ objectNameSingular,\nlimit: 1, offset: 0 }`, discarding whatever the user had entered. `1` is\nthe server-side default for a newly created `FIND_RECORDS` step, so this\nwas effectively a revert-to-creation-default on every object change.\n\n## Change\n\nCarry `limit` and `offset` over instead of hardcoding them. `filter` and\n`orderBy` are still dropped by omission, which is correct: they\nreference fields of the previous object.\n\n## Test\n\nAdded `KeepsLimitAndOffsetWhenObjectChanges` to the existing story file.\nIt switches the object and asserts `onActionUpdate` receives `{\nobjectName: ''company'', limit: 100, offset: 20 }`.\n\nConfirmed the test is not vacuous: reverting the fix makes it fail with\nexactly the reported symptom (`limit: 100 -> 1`, `offset: 20 -> 0`).\n\n## Not addressed here\n\nThe headline bug in #23387 (filters made only of value-less operators\nnever persisting) does not reproduce on `main`. I ran the reporter''s\nsteps with `Is in past` OR `Is today (UTC)` and both rules plus the `OR`\ngroup were written to the draft version correctly. Persistence hangs off\n`useUpsertRecordFilter`, which fires the advanced-filter `onUpdate` on\nevery upsert, so operand changes save just as value changes do. The\nreporter is on ~v2.18.x and did not re-test on a recent release.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23423?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaKFfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/AgQACn54NcPvEuUApDW1iqDADyL\nvivEqxZukc1WejDH2EX3SeIq9nmG/F1xGZIjvyAwEYBr7zFq1G78dglDgaai6J1M\nv+ApMUdEH/LnUzAAZx/dd2EEq00E/YfY3Aq7MdzKsdFiTKQFrep3t7v81XE4fRAl\nMoe1mnclgeP4KMKFXjtbcmtftOQnMxyP6AFxnnL2HLc6dTDprjbvXNivT6W+T6r0\nWCJ+Vh2zA27j7rA2kfw8qirCMizY2vcKCjqIuxnZEwVx0eRZMGPJaoSkciphGubE\nsQg4W8y6EjI58ov3pq+VLpjVTNRsj5YNFW3rerJoZS78KHhoSru3qAgh2fYf7KjD\nksHY16Vj96jdPAIWmJACZ8upfgY3cEyI7EkJcQ1WiMyKuW99HCGyET9PTGiiN3iO\np3c+tEfOExS7WbcMgyqwenWw6eApJm9exImm+QAHpKSmfay8STsb7K47nW3WyKE5\nj3qy72u94ZVSQ95B1LZaKflfr2EBy7FECw/DjtoHJmIe58pVwlFgzTxkAYf7+Xe4\nTBCZV4Kbk/8x+6TV+ORwZ4BndAQ0Es19MyiglHvWutd9dDyp38LqLx1MJAi+Siy7\nuuo7ZSzb+yP7LkhE9tKg6qVVFN+nPzjYJ+9Syx/1LZPkzfkjtHpMBz0995iKonmE\nnAyDXpjoCSB6ALgvTEt9\n=2atS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDRjOTA0YWE0NGM0NDA3NWQyNmJhYTk1YzY4NDQ4MTYxOGQ3YWIyNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/11447bd96f0100e90d99c221a6b7c7af10ccba2b","sha":"11447bd96f0100e90d99c221a6b7c7af10ccba2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/11447bd96f0100e90d99c221a6b7c7af10ccba2b"}],"sha":"4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/4c904aa44c44075d26baa95c684481618d7ab272"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/11447bd96f0100e90d99c221a6b7c7af10ccba2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:27:26Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:27:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make add-select-option work on record detail pages (#23420)\n\nFixes #23339\n\nFollow-up to #23410, which fixed the neighbouring issue (#23341) for\nusers *without* the `DATA_MODEL` permission.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn #23339 the reporter added a multiselect field to Person and then\nfound the inline \"create option\" prompt unresponsive. They clearly have\n`DATA_MODEL` permission, since they just created the field, so the\npermission check isn''t what''s blocking them.\n\nThe blocker is the *other* precondition. Both hooks read the object name\nfrom the router:\n\n```ts\nconst { objectNamePlural } = useParams();\n```\n\n`objectNamePlural` only exists on record index routes\n(`/objects/:objectNamePlural`). Record **detail** pages are\n`/object/:objectNameSingular/:objectRecordId`, so on a record page the\nparam is `undefined` and:\n\n- `useCanAddSelectOption` returns false via\n`isNonEmptyString(objectNamePlural)`\n- `useAddSelectOption` bails out at `if (!fieldName ||\n!objectNamePlural) return;`\n\nSo the action was dead on record pages for **every** user, admins\nincluded, and the navigation target it needed was never reachable from\nthere.\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve the field and its object from `fieldMetadataId`, which\n`FieldDefinition` already carries, instead of reading the object name\noff the URL:\n\n```ts\nconst { fieldMetadataItem, objectMetadataItem } =\n  useFieldMetadataItemById(fieldMetadataId);\n```\n\nThis drops the route dependency entirely, so the action behaves the same\nwherever the field is rendered, and `canAddSelectOption` now reflects\nonly the real permission check.\n\nIt also lets both hooks take a single `fieldMetadataId` argument:\n`fieldMetadataItem.name` is the same value the callers were previously\npassing as `fieldName`, so that parameter is no longer needed. Resolving\nboth values from one id means the guard and the action can''t disagree\nabout which field they''re describing.\n\n`useFieldMetadataItemById` is used rather than\n`useFieldMetadataItemByIdOrThrow` because a lookup miss should disable\nthe prompt, not crash the field input.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nOn the code the reporter was running (immediately before #23410), as an\n**admin** with full `DATA_MODEL`, on a company record page, typing a\nvalue matching no option:\n\n- `Add \"…\" to options` renders\n- clicking it does nothing — URL unchanged, no navigation\n- pressing <kbd>Enter</kbd> does nothing either\n\nwhich matches #23339 exactly, including the note about the Enter\nkeypress.\n\nAfter #23410 the same root cause shows up differently: the prompt is no\nlonger rendered at all on record pages, since the guard it''s now gated\non is false there. Still broken, just silent.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified manually on a local instance, swapping only these files between\nthree states and re-running the identical steps on the same cell.\n\n| code state | user | route | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| before #23410 | Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt shown, click\nand Enter both do nothing |\n| current main | Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt not shown,\naction unreachable |\n| **this PR** | Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt shown, navigates\nto `/settings/objects/companies/workPolicy?newOption=…` |\n| **this PR** | Admin | `/objects/tasks` (`Status`, single select) |\nstill works, navigates to `/settings/objects/tasks/status?newOption=…` |\n| **this PR** | Member (no `DATA_MODEL`) | `/object/company/:id` |\nprompt not shown |\n\nThe settings form opens with the typed value prefilled alongside the\nexisting options, so the end-to-end flow works from a record page for\nthe first time.\n\nThe Member row confirms #23341 stays fixed: dropping the route\ndependency doesn''t weaken the permission gate. The single-select row\ncovers `SelectFieldInput`, which takes the same change.\n\n`nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-front` and `nx typecheck twenty-front`\nboth pass.","tree":{"sha":"28304e9c7bbea02824d64194b63bd01dfdb5b53a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/28304e9c7bbea02824d64194b63bd01dfdb5b53a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/11447bd96f0100e90d99c221a6b7c7af10ccba2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 28304e9c7bbea02824d64194b63bd01dfdb5b53a\nparent 7b46c3ed3184e4f9b3785da2d66ad51a0a6f965a\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1785241646 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785241646 +0000\n\nfix: make add-select-option work on record detail pages (#23420)\n\nFixes #23339\n\nFollow-up to #23410, which fixed the neighbouring issue (#23341) for\nusers *without* the `DATA_MODEL` permission.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn #23339 the reporter added a multiselect field to Person and then\nfound the inline \"create option\" prompt unresponsive. They clearly have\n`DATA_MODEL` permission, since they just created the field, so the\npermission check isn''t what''s blocking them.\n\nThe blocker is the *other* precondition. Both hooks read the object name\nfrom the router:\n\n```ts\nconst { objectNamePlural } = useParams();\n```\n\n`objectNamePlural` only exists on record index routes\n(`/objects/:objectNamePlural`). Record **detail** pages are\n`/object/:objectNameSingular/:objectRecordId`, so on a record page the\nparam is `undefined` and:\n\n- `useCanAddSelectOption` returns false via\n`isNonEmptyString(objectNamePlural)`\n- `useAddSelectOption` bails out at `if (!fieldName ||\n!objectNamePlural) return;`\n\nSo the action was dead on record pages for **every** user, admins\nincluded, and the navigation target it needed was never reachable from\nthere.\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve the field and its object from `fieldMetadataId`, which\n`FieldDefinition` already carries, instead of reading the object name\noff the URL:\n\n```ts\nconst { fieldMetadataItem, objectMetadataItem } =\n  useFieldMetadataItemById(fieldMetadataId);\n```\n\nThis drops the route dependency entirely, so the action behaves the same\nwherever the field is rendered, and `canAddSelectOption` now reflects\nonly the real permission check.\n\nIt also lets both hooks take a single `fieldMetadataId` argument:\n`fieldMetadataItem.name` is the same value the callers were previously\npassing as `fieldName`, so that parameter is no longer needed. Resolving\nboth values from one id means the guard and the action can''t disagree\nabout which field they''re describing.\n\n`useFieldMetadataItemById` is used rather than\n`useFieldMetadataItemByIdOrThrow` because a lookup miss should disable\nthe prompt, not crash the field input.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nOn the code the reporter was running (immediately before #23410), as an\n**admin** with full `DATA_MODEL`, on a company record page, typing a\nvalue matching no option:\n\n- `Add \"…\" to options` renders\n- clicking it does nothing — URL unchanged, no navigation\n- pressing <kbd>Enter</kbd> does nothing either\n\nwhich matches #23339 exactly, including the note about the Enter\nkeypress.\n\nAfter #23410 the same root cause shows up differently: the prompt is no\nlonger rendered at all on record pages, since the guard it''s now gated\non is false there. Still broken, just silent.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified manually on a local instance, swapping only these files between\nthree states and re-running the identical steps on the same cell.\n\n| code state | user | route | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| before #23410 | Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt shown, click\nand Enter both do nothing |\n| current main | Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt not shown,\naction unreachable |\n| **this PR** | Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt shown, navigates\nto `/settings/objects/companies/workPolicy?newOption=…` |\n| **this PR** | Admin | `/objects/tasks` (`Status`, single select) |\nstill works, navigates to `/settings/objects/tasks/status?newOption=…` |\n| **this PR** | Member (no `DATA_MODEL`) | `/object/company/:id` |\nprompt not shown |\n\nThe settings form opens with the typed value prefilled alongside the\nexisting options, so the end-to-end flow works from a record page for\nthe first time.\n\nThe Member row confirms #23341 stays fixed: dropping the route\ndependency doesn''t weaken the permission gate. The single-select row\ncovers `SelectFieldInput`, which takes the same change.\n\n`nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-front` and `nx typecheck twenty-front`\nboth pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaKA+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANOoQAHttWiDDMbZZ68UoLRX3hoCo\nxeNB1UpPuqGGHpRMuNOzE/8ShVpzonMh6uGoTG3kLQDUNeui4viEhy7dkp6AbBQb\nzxNGNW2a9blGHAP3xJUbsnc6vyn4uSGn6M0wJwlJrfMIXk3Dcg