Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/cc5ff4869dd98b07c07625e064d4f8ef278d1db5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:53:42Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:53:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: use cache for role validation (#23383)\n\n## Context\n\nRole assignment validation queried PostgreSQL only to check whether a\nrole exists and whether `canBeAssignedToUsers` is enabled. Both values\nalready exist in `flatRoleMaps`.\n\nThis validation runs when inviting users and assigning a role to a user\nworkspace.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the role repository lookup with `flatRoleMaps`\n- Resolve the role through the existing keyed flat-map helper\n- Preserve the existing role-not-found and role-not-assignable errors\n- Replace unused TypeORM module wiring with the flat entity cache module\n\n## Expected impact\n\nOn a warm workspace cache, role assignment validation uses an O(1) map\nlookup and avoids a PostgreSQL round trip. Cold caches retain the normal\nworkspace cache recomputation behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Typecheck reports no errors in the changed files\n- Existing validation outcomes and exception codes are preserved\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23383?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"7efb212f370a5abb663433782d27f9a26d375c03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/7efb212f370a5abb663433782d27f9a26d375c03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/cc5ff4869dd98b07c07625e064d4f8ef278d1db5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7efb212f370a5abb663433782d27f9a26d375c03\nparent 8481c76bfb9da0ec85ab2aaac42b7fb15590b494\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1785225222 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785225222 +0000\n\nperf: use cache for role validation (#23383)\n\n## Context\n\nRole assignment validation queried PostgreSQL only to check whether a\nrole exists and whether `canBeAssignedToUsers` is enabled. Both values\nalready exist in `flatRoleMaps`.\n\nThis validation runs when inviting users and assigning a role to a user\nworkspace.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the role repository lookup with `flatRoleMaps`\n- Resolve the role through the existing keyed flat-map helper\n- Preserve the existing role-not-found and role-not-assignable errors\n- Replace unused TypeORM module wiring with the flat entity cache module\n\n## Expected impact\n\nOn a warm workspace cache, role assignment validation uses an O(1) map\nlookup and avoids a PostgreSQL round trip. Cold caches retain the normal\nworkspace cache recomputation behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Typecheck reports no errors in the changed files\n- Existing validation outcomes and exception codes are preserved\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23383?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaGAsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnCwQAJSqovwnjVWh052DQbbbR4b+\nnrKQazyc7y/9eqjWW5HJxJ14bhRSOalW/4+xC+cn9N8tQeLyJIAnZaH6D9kRKRKu\npQzIKMuPyasKN8rWCnE3k8soZmlw/Q3NNnmKUdy7MfQwjxfk3lW7zfmgb/DGQhie\ng4SGDnZFr/wdfTzsCQ7NhOwIDJsgx/2venWLZDqiDMoSOCOgXGOW8vNZTSPTjltw\n6v4tVZC6Av89kYKwushZrZzVESbpi3ELJE87u2vkwBj3dzivV/ESGA1j7M2vMLFN\nH/tNWKYnEr5qytufEONYVsZVL11oHJ3WdJTwsraqgLV4QHAztrbnMUvZ76TNa0kU\nkjfn/vN3MUdlklhrJiKSA7QbPFd8c3QBcopiXLnTm/Wqdq9NjbhDo97Yfyz2w49Y\nn29hejMtC7iIZoMulbLpzSTwo7qxWEQFrmCHSAaWJkHMey3TgJecr/qrE0n571o2\n+NPngbGDinnyPi0gHPYKBfdsigeMSPXZBZvgv8lgSHmS4AtVeb4e5KLY7ZLbptlU\nGPRMzIE9ZXQJjekmP00MYwDWg/HaKUDcRBr1qIAEVPqpfLdj//NPsO+rNSClhM3l\n+SSmKIGO7SFwZ0Czu/OTAtQcg9ZRYAw196TP/EhnOrt21vXnMZHMY2AjVMrCsgLl\nUTwBPEOwjJSFNO0CWYqf\n=/dR6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/cc5ff4869dd98b07c07625e064d4f8ef278d1db5","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKGNjNWZmNDg2OWRkOThiMDdjMDc2MjVlMDY0ZDRmOGVmMjc4ZDFkYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/8481c76bfb9da0ec85ab2aaac42b7fb15590b494","sha":"8481c76bfb9da0ec85ab2aaac42b7fb15590b494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/8481c76bfb9da0ec85ab2aaac42b7fb15590b494"}],"sha":"cc5ff4869dd98b07c07625e064d4f8ef278d1db5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/cc5ff4869dd98b07c07625e064d4f8ef278d1db5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/8481c76bfb9da0ec85ab2aaac42b7fb15590b494/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:53:29Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:53:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: use cache for webhook reads (#23382)\n\n## Context\n\nWebhook reads queried both the webhook and application tables, then\nrebuilt the same flat webhook representation already maintained by the\nworkspace cache.\n\nThis affected REST, GraphQL, and the webhook listing tool.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Read `findAll` and `findById` from `flatWebhookMaps`\n- Keep `findById` as a keyed ID lookup\n- Preserve `findAll` ordering by `createdAt`\n- Remove unused webhook and application repository wiring\n\nThe flat webhook cache contains only active webhooks and already\nincludes the application universal identifier needed by the DTO\nconversion.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nOn a warm workspace cache, webhook reads avoid queries to both the\nwebhook and application tables. `findAll` still iterates over every\nreturned webhook, matching the original query''s result cardinality,\nwhile `findById` uses a keyed lookup.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Typecheck reports no errors in the changed files\n- `findAll` ordering and `findById` missing-record behavior are\npreserved\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23382?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"b708fb5e6cdac6184e8316a1d840f997c5e45b3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/b708fb5e6cdac6184e8316a1d840f997c5e45b3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/8481c76bfb9da0ec85ab2aaac42b7fb15590b494","verification":{"payload":"tree b708fb5e6cdac6184e8316a1d840f997c5e45b3d\nparent 30aee1dee585a893bb93404b87d429c2a14de5a3\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1785225209 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785225209 +0000\n\nperf: use cache for webhook reads (#23382)\n\n## Context\n\nWebhook reads queried both the webhook and application tables, then\nrebuilt the same flat webhook representation already maintained by the\nworkspace cache.\n\nThis affected REST, GraphQL, and the webhook listing tool.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Read `findAll` and `findById` from `flatWebhookMaps`\n- Keep `findById` as a keyed ID lookup\n- Preserve `findAll` ordering by `createdAt`\n- Remove unused webhook and application repository wiring\n\nThe flat webhook cache contains only active webhooks and already\nincludes the application universal identifier needed by the DTO\nconversion.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nOn a warm workspace cache, webhook reads avoid queries to both the\nwebhook and application tables. `findAll` still iterates over every\nreturned webhook, matching the original query''s result cardinality,\nwhile `findById` uses a keyed lookup.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Typecheck reports no errors in the changed files\n- `findAll` ordering and `findById` missing-record behavior are\npreserved\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23382?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaGAJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz4sQAH9y2oTpTmIvWzzi7yhdtlGM\nTBOaWWUTV9fT8JJ8pOoR84wuyQDbegagVFCFRou7YpIwz3CguI2ACfGkrBXYAkkk\nKID78a/qCgAVqBZ6VxKWTTfmFveoDivicNLat+qPC7SG8+3AKgJR10Q9ybnd2j96\nnCZz5hBdF0B6gzycDWoxbUOBVto4Te9+8Sp5DmWswjeva186WQBfQePa50SH090B\n5nHQFBtki2mhmWHZ9ishtIDVHg/fsAC9W0Gxj+X4JYr3Dkq/XO8fDUQNTPpbi7ZQ\nUm2K3Kub/OiIHkOIg3fOD5ZKPTquWc5liChS4xTZKLt6CD/LA9TH8viRFY5QfAH3\nZ+KNzJM8jvyS2SmusJrvgO1x6YNuyOvXizYzNMCRXV048NU+a+9MAb2HNONrb39D\nNeCf+q18iQwzk/MKDQLsbZ9+hBEJsP7MaEZ70VuDsbneQ8lnMGc5z6Xpj3dVE5Bv\nY50XJljQVt6mrHCqKKEryT1EqtWeFmrszNtSYEY6vaUqSUZcFVK8DvTiSn09a8Hc\njTDA3tfeeUDEjfmin/5gwKRGAI2z1Di4SctZDt6/eXz1SEjMEHibdCsnMTD9lmfz\nJe+yk3TfanqRkRSg+r32UCvXcncfs8h+TByOC03VJp+4AUWlfv2DNz9UAsE/TQZx\nOgk1wTLPBkL2H15sMhZW\n=Bxuu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/user