url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/3c48e27b2ea91c097f01a51b759a987c29caeeac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/79bf20515d8c83adb298582f8ef470f0ef043de4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T14:43:59Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T14:43:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(workflow): mirror version delete/restore/destroy to core transactionally (#23356)\n\nNext step in the workflowVersion -> core soft-ref migration. The\ntransactional mirror (#23243) made **content** writes (create/update)\ndrift-free. This does the same for the **lifecycle** events (delete /\nrestore / destroy), which were still handled only by the async\nbest-effort listener. It''s the prerequisite for dropping that listener.\n\n## What changed\n`delete` and `restore` already soft-delete / restore the workflow''s\nversions inside `handleWorkflowSubEntities` (twenty doesn''t cascade\nsoft-deletes, so it does each sub-entity explicitly). So the core\ndelete/recreate just sits next to the existing version write:\n\n- **delete** — after `workflowVersionRepository.softDelete({ workflowId\n})`, `deleteCoreVersionsByWorkflowIds` removes the\n`core.workflowVersion` rows (`workflowId IN (...)`).\n(`deactivateVersionOnDelete` no longer re-mirrors the deactivated\nversion — that was recreating the core row it just deleted; it only\nflips the workspace status to `DEACTIVATED` so a restore comes back\ndeactivated.)\n- **restore** — after `workflowVersionRepository.restore({ workflowId\n})`, `recreateCoreVersionsByWorkflowId` re-reads the restored versions\nand reuses the existing `upsertToCore` (which reuses the stored\n`coreWorkflowVersionId` soft-ref, so rows come back with their original\nids and current status).\n- **destroy** — version destroy isn''t done in\n`handleWorkflowSubEntities` (it happens via the generic cascade), so\nthere''s no existing place to hang the core delete. New\n`workflow.destroyOne`/`destroyMany` **post**-hooks call\n`deleteCoreVersionsByWorkflowIds` (batched `IN`) only after the destroy\ncommits, so a rejected destroy can''t remove core rows while the\nworkspace versions survive.\n\nNo new transactional wrappers or raw SQL — the delete/recreate reuse the\nexisting `WorkflowVersionCoreSyncService` methods\n(`deleteFromCore`-style delete, `upsertToCore`). The async listener\nstays as an idempotent backstop until the cron soaks zero drift.\n\n## Async listener kept as backstop\n`handleRestored` / `handleDeleted` / `handleDestroyed` stay for now.\nBoth paths are idempotent (delete-of-deleted is a no-op; upsert\nconverges), so they don''t conflict. Those handlers come out in a\nfollow-up once the consistency cron soaks zero drift - which this PR\nunblocks.\n\n## Verification\nLifecycle integration test — creates a workflow, **activates** the\nversion (the active path is where the delete re-mirror bug bit), then\nasserts the core row: present -> gone after delete -> back after restore\n(as `DEACTIVATED`, same id) -> gone after destroy. Plus the existing\n`workflow-resolver` delete/restore suite (regression, since\n`handleWorkflowSubEntities` is shared).\n\nAlso verified **live** on a running instance against the real DB: the\nfull active-version lifecycle above, plus a batched `destroyWorkflows`\non two workflows removing both core rows in one `IN` delete. `nx\ntypecheck` + oxlint + oxfmt clean.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23356?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"d974ff22914e034028b4284e3017ddb24b648d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/d974ff22914e034028b4284e3017ddb24b648d51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/79bf20515d8c83adb298582f8ef470f0ef043de4","verification":{"payload":"tree d974ff22914e034028b4284e3017ddb24b648d51\nparent 5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1785163439 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785163439 +0000\n\nfeat(workflow): mirror version delete/restore/destroy to core transactionally (#23356)\n\nNext step in the workflowVersion -> core soft-ref migration. The\ntransactional mirror (#23243) made **content** writes (create/update)\ndrift-free. This does the same for the **lifecycle** events (delete /\nrestore / destroy), which were still handled only by the async\nbest-effort listener. It''s the prerequisite for dropping that listener.\n\n## What changed\n`delete` and `restore` already soft-delete / restore the workflow''s\nversions inside `handleWorkflowSubEntities` (twenty doesn''t cascade\nsoft-deletes, so it does each sub-entity explicitly). So the core\ndelete/recreate just sits next to the existing version write:\n\n- **delete** — after `workflowVersionRepository.softDelete({ workflowId\n})`, `deleteCoreVersionsByWorkflowIds` removes the\n`core.workflowVersion` rows (`workflowId IN (...)`).\n(`deactivateVersionOnDelete` no longer re-mirrors the deactivated\nversion — that was recreating the core row it just deleted; it only\nflips the workspace status to `DEACTIVATED` so a restore comes back\ndeactivated.)\n- **restore** — after `workflowVersionRepository.restore({ workflowId\n})`, `recreateCoreVersionsByWorkflowId` re-reads the restored versions\nand reuses the existing `upsertToCore` (which reuses the stored\n`coreWorkflowVersionId` soft-ref, so rows come back with their original\nids and current status).\n- **destroy** — version destroy isn''t done in\n`handleWorkflowSubEntities` (it happens via the generic cascade), so\nthere''s no existing place to hang the core delete. New\n`workflow.destroyOne`/`destroyMany` **post**-hooks call\n`deleteCoreVersionsByWorkflowIds` (batched `IN`) only after the destroy\ncommits, so a rejected destroy can''t remove core rows while the\nworkspace versions survive.\n\nNo new transactional wrappers or raw SQL — the delete/recreate reuse the\nexisting `WorkflowVersionCoreSyncService` methods\n(`deleteFromCore`-style delete, `upsertToCore`). The async listener\nstays as an idempotent backstop until the cron soaks zero drift.\n\n## Async listener kept as backstop\n`handleRestored` / `handleDeleted` / `handleDestroyed` stay for now.\nBoth paths are idempotent (delete-of-deleted is a no-op; upsert\nconverges), so they don''t conflict. Those handlers come out in a\nfollow-up once the consistency cron soaks zero drift - which this PR\nunblocks.\n\n## Verification\nLifecycle integration test — creates a workflow, **activates** the\nversion (the active path is where the delete re-mirror bug bit), then\nasserts the core row: present -> gone after delete -> back after restore\n(as `DEACTIVATED`, same id) -> gone after destroy. Plus the existing\n`workflow-resolver` delete/restore suite (regression, since\n`handleWorkflowSubEntities` is shared).\n\nAlso verified **live** on a running instance against the real DB: the\nfull active-version lifecycle above, plus a batched `destroyWorkflows`\non two workflows removing both core rows in one `IN` delete. `nx\ntypecheck` + oxlint + oxfmt clean.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23356?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ26+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJAAQAEjakri0C/3BYW+3OeRetnDS\nrep2p5X0iaCgV1mKYPxWqIzu6lHTY72VFmddltHHhZzkNr031lsEA4SSE7eK+kV4\nIPkA7epUHxYPQaEMUeMKtCZeckKByxzHxwP0SdXSewkeNmj9xmA1c2Hp6KwXSv7y\n6YqnNFIaMk3zppuxpCtbAg8FSGck83AMlob6crnbEN5u0qca5VhBIIG0Q92rv2rw\nKwfqAyTtZsI4A3OMz1SQif9DTUE3iSiNBUC3D/4vukPe/A99MutbD9dX3J0ytN/S\nazzTsjK2G/8RdR7xPbkbHTDBMclmxJ1vYMERQEXd+BjIfT7HcgEY9wTdipfTAblR\nFfT+XQ9uSUXv3xxHjgYAIMH18qNBY5Se3vslUPILK9+EJuztTCdhuCegV90yBGPJ\nmhcPaSV6cRh9Vvy55gAIFZEC8Z6Vb4qqQYtjJsYLYzSTP5HzYSwP7DYniiAy6Ayz\n854dxa59KzdzulOwGNmfDy1hJY5CqredyFDmawELAKdbxJQaXi+GfptZL1hDs+ce\nziQHYEw98L+mqiKjod05pSvvftHtCI171c/ciiIYXqP0VWqAllNsKVwoBO4oZcq+\n+h+mo7WZBXweNqItq+7g/p1dwNwxY7Fwui1h42bpfeQtGvu4qeYONSBXN200f7hw\n6IdKZbiLH59+jlrihWP3\n=LqGw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/79bf20515d8c83adb298582f8ef470f0ef043de4","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDc5YmYyMDUxNWQ4YzgzYWRiMjk4NTgyZjhlZjQ3MGYwZWYwNDNkZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e","sha":"5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e"}],"sha":"79bf20515d8c83adb298582f8ef470f0ef043de4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/79bf20515d8c83adb298582f8ef470f0ef043de4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T14:02:55Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T14:02:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dedupe common result handlers (#23364)\n\n## Context\n\n`CommonResultGettersService` selects field handlers by mapping every\nreturned record field to the handler registered for its metadata type.\n\nHandlers are shared instances, and each handler already receives the\ncomplete field metadata list. This means that when multiple fields have\nthe same handled type, the same handler is added and executed multiple\ntimes.\n\nFor example, a record with two `FILES` fields previously produced this\nexecution list:\n\n```text\n[objectHandler, filesHandler, filesHandler]\n```\n\nEach `filesHandler` execution processes both `FILES` fields. As a\nresult, both file URLs were signed twice. With several fields of the\nsame type, this can make the work grow quadratically.\n\nThe same duplication can affect rich-text processing, including JSON\nparsing, serialization, and embedded file URL signing.\n\n## What changed\n\nField handler instances are collected in an insertion-ordered `Set`\nbefore execution:\n\n```text\n[objectHandler, filesHandler]\n```\n\nEach distinct field handler now runs once per record and continues to\nprocess every matching field.\n\n## Why this is safe\n\n- The object-specific handler still runs first.\n- Different field-handler types keep their first-seen order.\n- No field is skipped, handlers still receive the complete field\nmetadata list.\n- Requests with zero or one field for a handled type are unchanged.\n- No cache or cross-request state is introduced.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nThis removes repeated synchronous file-token signing and repeated\nrich-text transformations for records with multiple fields of the same\nhandled type. It also reduces event-loop blocking when large result sets\ncontain several file or rich-text fields.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded a regression test with two `FILES` fields. It verifies that both\nfields are processed while `signFileByIdUrl` is called exactly once per\nfile, two calls instead of the previous four.\n\nValidated with:\n\n```bash\nyarn nx jest twenty-server --runInBand --runTestsByPath src/engine/api/common/common-result-getters/__tests__/common-result-getters.service.spec.ts\n```\n\nTouched files also pass type-aware Oxlint and Oxfmt.","tree":{"sha":"f5a745a32dc2e855dbaad62d2562fd64cdfd7732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/f5a745a32dc2e855dbaad62d2562fd64cdfd7732"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e","verification":{"payload":"tree f5a745a32dc2e855dbaad62d2562fd64cdfd7732\nparent 590ae069e8aadd6a4df1738fd3a47ce7d380b250\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1785160975 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785160975 +0000\n\nDedupe common result handlers (#23364)\n\n## Context\n\n`CommonResultGettersService` selects field handlers by mapping every\nreturned record field to the handler registered for its metadata type.\n\nHandlers are shared instances, and each handler already receives the\ncomplete field metadata list. This means that when multiple fields have\nthe same handled type, the same handler is added and executed multiple\ntimes.\n\nFor example, a record with two `FILES` fields previously produced this\nexecution list:\n\n```text\n[objectHandler, filesHandler, filesHandler]\n```\n\nEach `filesHandler` execution processes both `FILES` fields. As a\nresult, both file URLs were signed twice. With several fields of the\nsame type, this can make the work grow quadratically.\n\nThe same duplication can affect rich-text processing, including JSON\nparsing, serialization, and embedded file URL signing.\n\n## What changed\n\nField handler instances are collected in an insertion-ordered `Set`\nbefore execution:\n\n```text\n[objectHandler, filesHandler]\n```\n\nEach distinct field handler now runs once per record and continues to\nprocess every matching field.\n\n## Why this is safe\n\n- The object-specific handler still runs first.\n- Different field-handler types keep their first-seen order.\n- No field is skipped, handlers still receive the complete field\nmetadata list.\n- Requests with zero or one field for a handled type are unchanged.\n- No cache or cross-request state is introduced.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nThis removes repeated synchronous file-token signing and repeated\nrich-text transformations for records with multiple fields of the same\nhandled type. It also reduces event-loop blocking when large result sets\ncontain several file or rich-text fields.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded a regression test with two `FILES` fields. It verifies that both\nfields are processed while `signFileByIdUrl` is called exactly once per\nfile, two calls instead of the previous four.\n\nValidated with:\n\n```bash\nyarn nx jest twenty-server --runInBand --runTestsByPath src/engine/api/common/common-result-getters/__tests__/common-result-getters.service.spec.ts\n```\n\nTouched files also pass type-aware Oxlint and Oxfmt.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ2UfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATsEQAJQNVpTQAGvwun8JliwFYyBg\nME0hHtDqIUXzkNO+ezK5nc9gEga/QJLsyRgFCOV0HOQtpgo6Tqos6Ho8STj1wJhm\nVFVHrREB7IgYghFoN0F+c/uCTMhRS3HG4HKFzlZ6fpcDqZ5IIylqgj5dHmNnxqNV\noU4v+nIccrsj/5Wq8WlKWt05rkMn4gHAXXQ3xmvZEgNS6RI9nEVs64FIZjCB2Mwh\nUp6I1Oi9JRnwEdfhwBGLRShCZH7zhoqtbV4kY+NlZ2g6yex5TnU1wLi34DQvPIe1\noW3U/i20Hzv5mv++KoOIAy6FFqZ8AajIQkaozV3TJ8z/tCty8nS0uvUGZzc5Pjff\nSjxnRNTgJpVWzl90AObQW/r/mpBXpAsIeraA5eIpvxuFokbL5wm17C5rMY96/axi\nLpLU3DIdZPymhPJzdqddbbGXCYsdRx3age5upA9qTTyBDVnPQ78HK8iWhCigyMPh\nX8wa/XQ/mZ64Z/gwhlwJF58W6trtI4K12L02v56cRUIauRr14WmGxllPtxNNYnbo\nytpP/eGjUIgW9nDJo6wCOoPy32hNiVl5ZXhufO10Oijeo0SxU67XROq5EBuJwrCk\n3h224hJOTvrl6cvji/6ZQCBDzhf+xKDGeRTds/ekccAGE5zJTgpGmH5I543ho43E\nQG/LfQY16gQPdq4Mxz1q\n=Ey2k\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDVjMjNkZGIxYWNkODFmYTNmMzlkMmE2MTRjYjBhNjNjMWM3Yzk3OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/590ae069e8aadd6a4df1738fd3a47ce7d380b250","sha":"590ae069e8aadd6a4df1738fd3a47ce7d380b250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/590ae069e8aadd6a4df1738fd3a47ce7d380b250"}],"sha":"5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/5c23ddb1acd81fa3f39d2a614cb0a63c1c7c978e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/590ae069e8aadd6a4df1738fd3a47ce7d380b250/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T13:51:05Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T13:51:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Support workspace member Me filter for relation fields in dashboards (#23282)\n\n<img width=\"3024\" height=\"1484\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-07-27 at 15 04\n22@2x\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a57797b7-dbe9-4748-aeff-18667f1f69bb\"\n/>\n\n\nFixes #20225\n\nWorkspace member \"Me\" filters worked for standard actor fields (Created\nby / Updated by) in dashboard widgets but not for relation fields\npointing to a workspace member (e.g. \"Account owner\"). In the\nadvanced-filter UI, picking such a relation forced a relation traversal\nand never produced a filter you could set to \"Me\".\n\nFor a many-to-one relation targeting workspaceMember, the\nrelation-target sub-menu now offers a \"filter by record\" entry that\ncreates a direct relation filter with the same \"Me\" multi-select picker\nused by view filters. Traversal (e.g. \"Account owner -> Name\") is\npreserved. No backend change is needed: the stored value matches view\nfilters and is already resolved server-side.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23282?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"70250d26c2af6e3d2b8724d41ad21243b6e6d00a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/70250d26c2af6e3d2b8724d41ad21243b6e6d00a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/590ae069e8aadd6a4df1738fd3a47ce7d380b250","verification":{"payload":"tree 70250d26c2af6e3d2b8724d41ad21243b6e6d00a\nparent 0c57d7c108332fe47bc6d2e354a69563bb5f6519\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1785160265 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785160265 +0000\n\nSupport workspace member Me filter for relation fields in dashboards (#23282)\n\n<img width=\"3024\" height=\"1484\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-07-27 at 15 04\n22@2x\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a57797b7-dbe9-4748-aeff-18667f1f69bb\"\n/>\n\n\nFixes #20225\n\nWorkspace member \"Me\" filters worked for standard actor fields (Created\nby / Updated by) in dashboard widgets but not for relation fields\npointing to a workspace member (e.g. \"Account owner\"). In the\nadvanced-filter UI, picking such a relation forced a relation traversal\nand never produced a filter you could set to \"Me\".\n\nFor a many-to-one relation targeting workspaceMember, the\nrelation-target sub-menu now offers a \"filter by record\" entry that\ncreates a direct relation filter with the same \"Me\" multi-select picker\nused by view filters. Traversal (e.g. \"Account owner -> Name\") is\npreserved. No backend change is needed: the stored value matches view\nfilters and is already resolved server-side.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23282?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ2JaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXL4QAKtC9lM4m1YnXl2EhJRjBCr7\ncJQa1nKwtlTs+FTo3INr/1kfA1q+1RrhFaCxLnpuoIsfBU0NtDtHMRy9wy+Mk+jY\nhtInzbVwymQAUPEpz6Tw0G8Ocll2ZMXWwobNzbVU87/HfpMDPcN2qT2H3V954w8/\nQy3j5DWOYT10HZUOfu2MHPi9SpsyDMh5coJUDbcYwZlEmAKfiJunZDD/M0tHb7B3\nlKiWgtVke38hqkh7gBHhnuGFxIz6F4+6xIkjUPgRHHfbspiGFEe+jULw2Xj4ou9B\nYhV5EZGdtEoWOIav1WdarmCJ8UXwo1cDHvu7cvt6TAHPFhaeRz5NLiRObBofLiIq\nhDYCU7KLYe1HSNV0cj5KBPlFui6PCQLMi2nan4fQVxI5I4TVqk3eN9Xb3bwN/Xz