2eda10ca","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDc4MDQxMTFlNmNjN2IxYWFjYTY5NTVlNWQ3OTdlMDFiMmVkYTEwY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f","sha":"56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f"}],"sha":"7804111e6cc7b1aaca6955e5d797e01b2eda10ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/7804111e6cc7b1aaca6955e5d797e01b2eda10ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:58:42Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:58:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop leaking the refresh token in the social SSO redirect URL (#23061)\n\nThe Google/Microsoft callback for a sign-in with no target workspace\nredirected to `/sign-in-up?tokenPair={...}`, putting a 60-day refresh\ntoken in a query string. Those persist in browser history, `Referer`\nheaders and access logs.\n\nIt now carries a single-use, 5-minute opaque token in the URL fragment,\nwhich the frontend exchanges over POST. Browsers never send the fragment\non the wire, so the token stays out of access logs, proxies and\n`Referer` headers entirely. Redemption claims the row with a `DELETE`\nguarded on `revokedAt`/`deletedAt` being null, so concurrent requests\ncannot each mint a refresh token and a revoked token cannot redeem.\nEnterprise SSO (OIDC/SAML) already used a POST exchange and is\nunchanged.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Browser\n  participant Server\n  participant DB\n\n  Note over Browser,Server: before, the redirect carried access + 60-day refresh in ?tokenPair\n  Browser->>Server: GET /auth/google/redirect\n  Server->>DB: store sha256(token), expires in 5 min\n  Server-->>Browser: 302 /sign-in-up#ssoExchangeToken=opaque\n  Note over Browser: fragment never sent back to any server\n  Browser->>Server: POST getAuthTokensFromSSOExchangeToken\n  Server->>DB: guarded DELETE, single-use claim\n  Server-->>Browser: access + refresh token, in the response body\n```\n\nSince the token is single-use, the refresh token is minted at redemption\ninstead of at callback, so an abandoned redirect leaves an inert expired\nhash rather than a live credential.\n\nRedemption lives in its own `SignInUpSSOExchangeTokenEffect` +\n`useRedeemSSOExchangeToken`, mirroring the existing\n`VerifyLoginTokenEffect` + `useVerifyLogin` pair, so\n`SignInUpGlobalScopeFormEffect` only loses the vulnerable branch. Like\n`useVerifyLogin`, the hook clears any stale token pair before\nexchanging. The effect reads `window.location.hash` live and strips it\nsynchronously, which doubles as the StrictMode double-invocation latch.\n\nRemaining exposure is the browser itself (history until the synchronous\nstrip, client-side scripts), same as any fragment-based OAuth response.\n`loginToken` on the workspace-targeted branch still travels as\n`/verify?loginToken=` and is replayable for 15 minutes; moving it to the\nfragment too is a separate change.\n\nA fast instance command adds a unique partial index on `(\"type\",\n\"value\")` for live SSO exchange tokens, so redemption is an index lookup\ninstead of a full scan of the shared token table and at most one row can\never match.","tree":{"sha":"079093cd836a16edf64e8c4a2bc7af999a6ac4e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/079093cd836a16edf64e8c4a2bc7af999a6ac4e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f","verification":{"payload":"tree 079093cd836a16edf64e8c4a2bc7af999a6ac4e5\nparent b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1785157122 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785157122 +0000\n\nStop leaking the refresh token in the social SSO redirect URL (#23061)\n\nThe Google/Microsoft callback for a sign-in with no target workspace\nredirected to `/sign-in-up?tokenPair={...}`, putting a 60-day refresh\ntoken in a query string. Those persist in browser history, `Referer`\nheaders and access logs.\n\nIt now carries a single-use, 5-minute opaque token in the URL fragment,\nwhich the frontend exchanges over POST. Browsers never send the fragment\non the wire, so the token stays out of access logs, proxies and\n`Referer` headers entirely. Redemption claims the row with a `DELETE`\nguarded on `revokedAt`/`deletedAt` being null, so concurrent requests\ncannot each mint a refresh token and a revoked token cannot redeem.\nEnterprise SSO (OIDC/SAML) already used a POST exchange and is\nunchanged.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Browser\n  participant Server\n  participant DB\n\n  Note over Browser,Server: before, the redirect carried access + 60-day refresh in ?tokenPair\n  Browser->>Server: GET /auth/google/redirect\n  Server->>DB: store sha256(token), expires in 5 min\n  Server-->>Browser: 302 /sign-in-up#ssoExchangeToken=opaque\n  Note over Browser: fragment never sent back to any server\n  Browser->>Server: POST getAuthTokensFromSSOExchangeToken\n  Server->>DB: guarded DELETE, single-use claim\n  Server-->>Browser: access + refresh token, in the response body\n```\n\nSince the token is single-use, the refresh token is minted at redemption\ninstead of at callback, so an abandoned redirect leaves an inert expired\nhash rather than a live credential.\n\nRedemption lives in its own `SignInUpSSOExchangeTokenEffect` +\n`useRedeemSSOExchangeToken`, mirroring the existing\n`VerifyLoginTokenEffect` + `useVerifyLogin` pair, so\n`SignInUpGlobalScopeFormEffect` only loses the vulnerable branch. Like\n`useVerifyLogin`, the hook clears any stale token pair before\nexchanging. The effect reads `window.location.hash` live and strips it\nsynchronously, which doubles as the StrictMode double-invocation latch.\n\nRemaining exposure is the browser itself (history until the synchronous\nstrip, client-side scripts), same as any fragment-based OAuth response.\n`loginToken` on the workspace-targeted branch still travels as\n`/verify?loginToken=` and is replayable for 15 minutes; moving it to the\nfragment too is a separate change.\n\nA fast instance command adds a unique partial index on `(\"type\",\n\"value\")` for live SSO exchange tokens, so redemption is an index lookup\ninstead of a full scan of the shared token table and at most one row can\never match.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ1YSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzG8QAGDqXgjLeLywqoP2fGN52VUr\nyV666rFFgmzxAB6I0mG4gGqAbuOPSz6WSG7vIiyHolqDCoiytKXXbv4VmqGK/JMs\nlynEbRoxNdQbFWA4K8WTUg+yYaM0BK/UxkYFGRcPWW/hHUcXjZZFjJjth4oitHyg\n3wluHVqAdTrtH4b1ODVFUIHQydGXRKIW2azwO0LJCYwE7ThzB34tuOFTSn6VYF8v\noYZESE0DDRSd/aPCD3lNwhKcEXorF8fjl2L94I3EHOOXRJvvEFzhxloHd79vV3bH\nq1meFnJrg4azPfiKxQjvRS9Md6AH2zOAi3Aou5wJNXN39r+zIfm/G3sNLcljYiuX\nsVs+K5F90mVoJRoEFzriK2gOG+1sBPubWcatFFMKFFqokvMS6HC2BURf3GbLv8oa\nlpc5aopPkW7OHpGt3R8nZ+V0aqhW4xqVStbQ2CKmcvl/4EJiVg1bXOpHoO/hiu0I\nL9UUq0XOFbooJzXLV/2m+hGx1+KClnDOx2i6LXngOlhOysAoMzKlsETqvBBYdonw\nZTP2yzGVnbGLdrwD+ejGBcAMS29PpruMWgPLfgLEv0Zu9MxUzsJ8yXOMoMJbN8Qz\nDH4boaJFIIQzjwRPr0iJPQcwsqSZTz9tF+9RuZReSI4D6pim9ckDawxVAKkOTVsa\nP7tWEIuN8YHw5SrECqhl\n=olyq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDU2MjQ1YTM1YWY1NDVhODIzYTNmODVhOWJiZTY0MzE3ZmE1MDZhOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b","sha":"b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b"}],"sha":"56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/56245a35af545a823a3f85a9bbe64317fa506a8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129690295?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Shinu-Cherian","id":129690295,"login":"Shinu-Cherian","node_id":"U_kgDOB7rqtw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shinu-Cherian","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:57:24Z","email":"129690295+Shinu-Cherian@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Shinu Cherian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:57:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(twenty-front): hide layout editor UI when SystemPermissionFlag.LAYOUTS is missing (#23303) (#23343)\n\n## Description\nFixes #23303.\n\nThis PR ensures that the layout editor UI and customization entry points\nare hidden and protected when a user lacks the\n`SystemPermissionFlag.LAYOUTS` permission flag.\n\n### Changes Made:\n1. **`useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode.ts`**: Added\n`useHasPermissionFlag(PermissionFlagType.LAYOUTS)` check inside\n`enterLayoutCustomizationMode` to return `false` and prevent entering\ncustomization mode if the user lacks permission.\n2. **`WorkspaceSection.tsx`**: Updated the sidebar `WorkspaceSection`\ncomponent to render the layout edit button (`IconTool`) only when\n`hasLayoutsPermission` is `true`.\n3. **`ObjectLayout.tsx`**: Disabled customize and reset layout controls\nin the Data Model Object Details settings page if the user lacks\n`LAYOUTS` permission.\n4. **`useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode.test.tsx`**: Added unit tests to\nverify that `useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode` correctly guards layout\ncustomization initialization based on permission.\n\n## Testing\n- Added unit tests for `useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode` permission\nchecks.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23343?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"8b0f6a45d72b3b0fa4171826c73fa1dc08ebd7b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/8b0f6a45d72b3b0fa4171826c73fa1dc08ebd7b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b0f6a45d72b3b0fa4171826c73fa1dc08ebd7b8\nparent 22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979\nauthor Shinu Cherian <129690295+Shinu-Cherian@users.noreply.github.com> 1785157044 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785157044 +0000\n\nfix(twenty-front): hide layout editor UI when SystemPermissionFlag.LAYOUTS is missing (#23303) (#23343)\n\n## Description\nFixes #23303.\n\nThis PR ensures that the layout editor UI and customization entry points\nare hidden and protected when a user lacks the\n`SystemPermissionFlag.LAYOUTS` permission flag.\n\n### Changes Made:\n1. **`useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode.ts`**: Added\n`useHasPermissionFlag(PermissionFlagType.LAYOUTS)` check inside\n`enterLayoutCustomizationMode` to return `false` and prevent entering\ncustomization mode if the user lacks permission.\n2. **`WorkspaceSection.tsx`**: Updated the sidebar `WorkspaceSection`\ncomponent to render the layout edit button (`IconTool`) only when\n`hasLayoutsPermission` is `true`.\n3. **`ObjectLayout.tsx`**: Disabled customize and reset layout controls\nin the Data Model Object Details settings page if the user lacks\n`LAYOUTS` permission.\n4. **`useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode.test.tsx`**: Added unit tests to\nverify that `useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode` correctly guards layout\ncustomization initialization based on permission.\n\n## Testing\n- Added unit tests for `useEnterLayoutCustomizationMode` permission\nchecks.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23343?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ1XECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjTUQAFlEPVt/Q3nKm5S+2kbz21ix\ncW2vkXx0lawHWGjhERi2nXN+RqoL/5VLNSAM37PlydNF8oomLCwgbRXfLmcCCfhT\naJ5RAdjLJA7pde0k36IoFgltnU+OJd/M2Crb1Z5IbLaLLlC+uZYUqdfNfbMk+tHG\nMpCFpJYbzrkXuP/Pmk42glpkm98wRpq+om72e2pHmsKoKt2EdVQw2ZvKjWM1HcMT\nAPtnd91kv5sGzn7vQEQ5Vbri0jcSXpnurm+//EBm+hrujsj84mOKkIP6CHFwHPMJ\nQuzU6BWr+oXITWB4pZ+hY8WHmcseqbBG50kjLEL3PbR+rsMjNB0mSOkKjDwgE7UW\nRKevj1/qxKzOlVtNBsIJFccHcBKoZfrJTUaww1yW+lKmInHHIbTEGlBQhn6F3h+6\nxNQHnChpYDa6QPwgyhXHyxuqQy03/o8Ulio4ZDv1Dl5G0iUgGDxGtvnB1028xDDl\nsDWDC94bbS6lFF6zruzmlUnQ6w0eVYanlZuYMTuO8wJnoJ7QvHbmIXIAo72/CrTz\nRld42kGoQdm3Xw8kfBPVx5LZewQFO+T5205TMH+yh7gyMV4XhrRfcVbnB0l8Ptpd\neoKkX4jZJDJObHpCetCxPfZvLMdSqSPHFXI6xSFRu3PntCaFd58yqzaqvaELrKo6\n8H7MHqdGyb3GcHcw9FHm\n=iLTB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKGI4MWNhOTkxNjIyNzAyMWJjZTM2OWJmNzkyMjU1MDQ2MTgyNzNiMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979","sha":"22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979"}],"sha":"b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/b81ca9916227021bce369bf79225504618273b1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:32:51Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:32:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix: password reset link returns FORBIDDEN for logged-in users (#21248) (#23335)\n\n## Problem\n\nFixes #21248.\n\nAfter upgrading, workspace members who open a password reset link while\na token pair still exists in local storage get a generic `You do not\nhave permission to perform this action.` (FORBIDDEN) error, blocking\naccount recovery.\n\n## Root cause\n\nEvery GraphQL request passes through\n`GraphQLHydrateRequestFromTokenMiddleware` before any resolver. If a\ntoken is present it validates it; if no token is present it\nshort-circuits and lets the request through unauthenticated.\n\nThe reset flow was only ever designed for the unauthenticated case (the\nuser is logged out, so no token exists). Two intended changes broke that\nassumption:\n\n- A token pair now persists in local storage at reset time (unified\n`accessOrWorkspaceAgnosticToken` + tokenPair moved off session cookies\ninto local storage).\n- The Apollo auth link attaches `authorization: Bearer <token>` whenever\nany token pair exists, regardless of the operation.\n\nSo the public `validatePasswordResetToken` /\n`updatePasswordViaResetToken` operations now arrive with a token that\nthe middleware rejects, producing FORBIDDEN before the resolver runs.\nNote: the `PublicEndpointGuard` / `NoPermissionGuard` on these resolvers\nboth just `return true` — they do not inspect headers and are not the\ngate. The middleware is.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a generic `skipAuthToken` operation-context flag. The auth link\nomits the `Authorization` header when a request sets it, staying\nagnostic of any specific operation or endpoint. The two public reset\noperations opt in at their call site in `PasswordReset.tsx`.\n\nThis restores the exact unauthenticated path the flow was designed for,\nregardless of whether a token pair happens to sit in local storage.\nNothing is reverted; all authenticated traffic is unaffected.\n\n## Testing\n\nRan the built frontend against a local backend, logged in so a\n`tokenPairState` was present in local storage, then opened a reset link\nand inspected the outgoing `ValidatePasswordResetToken` request:\n\n- Request headers: `accept`, `content-type`, `x-locale` only. No\n`authorization` header, despite a token pair being present.\n- With an invalid token the response is the resolver-level `Token is\ninvalid` error (it reaches the resolver) instead of the middleware''s\nFORBIDDEN.\n- With a valid token the query succeeds (`validatePasswordResetToken`\nreturns the email + `hasPassword`) and the Set/Change Password form\nrenders, so the recovery flow completes.\n\nLint and typecheck pass on the changed files.","tree":{"sha":"90b36413fd38bf84085dcadf984d0da48980dfa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/90b36413fd38bf84085dcadf984d0da48980dfa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979","verification":{"payload":"tree 90b36413fd38bf84085dcadf984d0da48980dfa7\nparent e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1785155571 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785155571 +0000\n\nFix: password reset link returns FORBIDDEN for logged-in users (#21248) (#23335)\n\n## Problem\n\nFixes #21248.\n\nAfter upgrading, workspace members who open a password reset link while\na token pair still exists in local storage get a generic `You do not\nhave permission to perform this action.` (FORBIDDEN) error, blocking\naccount recovery.\n\n## Root cause\n\nEvery GraphQL request passes through\n`GraphQLHydrateRequestFromTokenMiddleware` before any resolver. If a\ntoken is present it validates it; if no token is present it\nshort-circuits and lets the request through unauthenticated.\n\nThe reset flow was only ever designed for the unauthenticated case (the\nuser is logged out, so no token exists). Two intended changes broke that\nassumption:\n\n- A token pair now persists in local storage at reset time (unified\n`accessOrWorkspaceAgnosticToken` + tokenPair moved off session cookies\ninto local storage).\n- The Apollo auth link attaches `authorization: Bearer <token>` whenever\nany token pair exists, regardless of the operation.\n\nSo the public `validatePasswordResetToken` /\n`updatePasswordViaResetToken` operations now arrive with a token that\nthe middleware rejects, producing FORBIDDEN before the resolver runs.\nNote: the `PublicEndpointGuard` / `NoPermissionGuard` on these resolvers\nboth just `return true` — they do not inspect headers and are not the\ngate. The middleware is.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a generic `skipAuthToken` operation-context flag. The auth link\nomits the `Authorization` header when a request sets it, staying\nagnostic of any specific operation or endpoint. The two public reset\noperations opt in at their call site in `PasswordReset.tsx`.\n\nThis restores the exact unauthenticated path the flow was designed for,\nregardless of whether a token pair happens to sit in local storage.\nNothing is reverted; all authenticated traffic is unaffected.\n\n## Testing\n\nRan the built frontend against a local backend, logged in so a\n`tokenPairState` was present in local storage, then opened a reset link\nand inspected the outgoing `ValidatePasswordResetToken` request:\n\n- Request headers: `accept`, `content-type`, `x-locale` only. No\n`authorization` header, despite a token pair being present.\n- With an invalid token the response is the resolver-level `Token is\ninvalid` error (it reaches the resolver) instead of the middleware''s\nFORBIDDEN.\n- With a valid token the query succeeds (`validatePasswordResetToken`\nreturns the email + `hasPassword`) and the Set/Change Password form\nrenders, so the recovery flow completes.\n\nLint and typecheck pass on the changed files.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ1AECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKecQADBSzr2Yl4i78ZDq37IJTp7l\n/wTIdbDlVVtcIbxJyFMUMka99TGr14c8a4FvsPTdC7ihKfDn4qbwgm1BnIPT1CQ9\nmHCLyJeAK00CzJbQ/EeIHjSy/+pgObtgTM4qyykNzfGkAT6gk+9Bd4mjY5lX6o19\npZxkXnxfGmquMMavr1I9AkxN/8IUz2jzHW8yV9c0jyqxwSjfB2mN0DguOEEmwpV7\nbHte+v8d5WU3uTE78kd3ZpC30dc4mQEs+p9PUeVo5pOs0RQ1cZn1rUSGY2PGvPT1\ns8DsdAkykTSsb00256e50dwFtMdtXmHaavN933DJSMbkfgaprS20jcJgDz1z11DI\nsc2csuzmU+SdmKrfwMdRnpCe4INdjhNDIgPJ+hkN08aZ5IRSno5Ny0eW26OYRmfh\n3wEpcbmLei2SVp5SzKYQZ+LXc3pDcDVr8HdOXyEbQI+bOvYCTAIU7o34lJLXf9Sd\n4akx0/zczsgvHcAavw2+IhuJv1/pR+Ohb5qsXFGlkkV5fZoOpKRRgRNkYtgP60l7\nfF4SYeKdhnf7d+47Y4sQQhCpXggt3tUXY9fHW7+oBYijWzWCMn3Y58qkMik6Zhd+\nRN6M5eqtxvVpWZ61aK4NJUUSoWtCH/0zvsZMeQqr7qDGR+yylFMuH2Nmq8X7tA4e\nQaFKylB/9WZoDxfS3Yk2\n=fhhc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKDIyYTAxZGMxYzYwNGQ1MzVlNGIwY2EzMDI4YTA0NTJlZTQ1M2U5Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6","sha":"e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6"}],"sha":"22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/22a01dc1c604d535e4b0ca3028a0452ee453e979"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11599358?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rashad","id":11599358,"login":"rashad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTk5MzU4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:57:23Z","email":"11599358+rashad@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rashad Karanouh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:57:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"v1.4.0 — partners: auto-link partner user on workspaceMember.created (#23295)\n\n**App version:** `1.4.0` (partners app —\n`packages/twenty-apps/internal/twenty-partners`)\n\n## What\n\nAdds partner onboarding auto-linking: when a `workspaceMember` is\ncreated (invite signup), a DB-event-triggered logic function resolves\nthe partner by the member''s email and stamps `partnerUser` across the\npartner and its cascade (person, company, links, services, content,\napplications).\n\n## Key design decision — data-linking only, no role assignment\n\nThe trigger **does not** assign the Partner role. A logic function runs\nas an app **agent**, with no user session; `updateWorkspaceMemberRole`\nis guarded by `UserAuthGuard` + `AuthWorkspaceMemberId` and is\nunreachable from an agent, so the mutation silently no-ops regardless of\npermission flags. The dead role code (`ensure-partner-role` service, its\nrole query/mutation, and the role mocks) is removed so the trigger''s\nresponsibility is unambiguous: resolve partner by email → link\n`partnerUser` cascade with retry-on-partial-failure. Role assignment, if\nwanted, belongs on the invite path (`sendInvitations` accepts a\n`roleId`), not the trigger.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `on-workspace-member-created.logic-function.ts` — DB-event trigger on\n`workspaceMember.created`; skips internal (`@twenty.com`) and unmatched\nemails\n- `resolve-partner-by-email` / `link-partner-user` services + typed\n`graphql/` operations for the cascade\n- `normalize-invite-email` util\n- `partnerUserLinkedAt` field on Partner\n- Seed: one contact `Person` (with `partnerId` + email) and one\n`Company` per partner so onboarding is testable via a seeded invite\nemail; drops the `person.city` write removed in SDK 2.25 that broke\n`yarn seed`\n\n## Verification\n\n- Unit: **173/173 pass** (27 files) · `tsc --noEmit` clean · `oxlint` 0\nwarnings/0 errors\n- End-to-end: invited + signed in a seeded partner\n(`lena@act-education.example`) on the workspace subdomain; the trigger\nlinked the member to the **Act Education** partner and the self-service\n**My Profile** page rendered the linked profile (`POST\n/s/my-partner-profile → 200`)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23295?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"e20ff68577972603513fb49523b17c50eb7e3801","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/e20ff68577972603513fb49523b17c50eb7e3801"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6","verification":{"payload":"tree e20ff68577972603513fb49523b17c50eb7e3801\nparent 302f46f0ea0620f9a8a8f7769ad24409d3b62891\nauthor Rashad Karanouh <11599358+rashad@users.noreply.github.com> 1785153443 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785153443 +0000\n\nv1.4.0 — partners: auto-link partner user on workspaceMember.created (#23295)\n\n**App version:** `1.4.0` (partners app —\n`packages/twenty-apps/internal/twenty-partners`)\n\n## What\n\nAdds partner onboarding auto-linking: when a `workspaceMember` is\ncreated (invite signup), a DB-event-triggered logic function resolves\nthe partner by the member''s email and stamps `partnerUser` across the\npartner and its cascade (person, company, links, services, content,\napplications).\n\n## Key design decision — data-linking only, no role assignment\n\nThe trigger **does not** assign the Partner role. A logic function runs\nas an app **agent**, with no user session; `updateWorkspaceMemberRole`\nis guarded by `UserAuthGuard` + `AuthWorkspaceMemberId` and is\nunreachable from an agent, so the mutation silently no-ops regardless of\npermission flags. The dead role code (`ensure-partner-role` service, its\nrole query/mutation, and the role mocks) is removed so the trigger''s\nresponsibility is unambiguous: resolve partner by email → link\n`partnerUser` cascade with retry-on-partial-failure. Role assignment, if\nwanted, belongs on the invite path (`sendInvitations` accepts a\n`roleId`), not the trigger.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `on-workspace-member-created.logic-function.ts` — DB-event trigger on\n`workspaceMember.created`; skips internal (`@twenty.com`) and unmatched\nemails\n- `resolve-partner-by-email` / `link-partner-user` services + typed\n`graphql/` operations for the cascade\n- `normalize-invite-email` util\n- `partnerUserLinkedAt` field on Partner\n- Seed: one contact `Person` (with `partnerId` + email) and one\n`Company` per partner so onboarding is testable via a seeded invite\nemail; drops the `person.city` write removed in SDK 2.25 that broke\n`yarn seed`\n\n## Verification\n\n- Unit: **173/173 pass** (27 files) · `tsc --noEmit` clean · `oxlint` 0\nwarnings/0 errors\n- End-to-end: invited + signed in a seeded partner\n(`lena@act-education.example`) on the workspace subdomain; the trigger\nlinked the member to the **Act Education** partner and the self-service\n**My Profile** page rendered the linked profile (`POST\n/s/my-partner-profile → 200`)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23295?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ0ezCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA35IQABbg9Ed8BIuX47d6Xk11R86L\nw4MJ8nQwYroY+NBLA1tPJFIs4dDwcBkX4dUmsmRt7Zi2AK2ad25UU5sGtMWiXhL6\nBBpmUuFzEUu8FwtUDtyh4DfJ4cZtBbGBzjfSpHqYs7Wp87bVdhqYxlsJ02lJLe6s\nQXJUDxJATdzvrZ2PhbA4aMBini01iPN8k8MGnjAAldvzBVCpqzojEiMJ+2PDif7q\nTMWMhS13vd8EolZW1YVFfVLnbnuRPzyJzBWPQupJvyRVpmHfMnHMcqz2smTbpjTw\n6RxVQ3ZYQU15rogsnEe8WdcXrXdyPDEVd4MGhRP4RYx+W2qUBuWxEkHx6OzB2uDm\nCW0JMHvhxINXTxFdKiFFYQE71saVV1cYrZK+JwkiNMqfrTGb4DJyDLILIqfBoS2K\n1B31Rzi2Jr1eXGWeRDJZQzEnzaUiqZJJPQnYmmbzzPaPBgPn7U+rMbV5VQKpOnJr\nUM4mRp1sRCd49AYblKxwYtGindTh/9AoYUU/z8cc7xlbZQzIwrIRhVUGBb0HpogI\nrYtA1X2kU4i1UEBViDl7yo5TuV1p35i6saHe2md+1FO0PomBEpA5oo/PfFru/IDe\nr5Ypgv6j+9gTd/qL1AXxSvAQCaIH+p2+OSm3XOnhxkFX7Bqmfocs8EolrpDBQ5k/\njZPu1gIe4izp4t5VI7KA\n=yk2n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKGU2MzFjOTg2YTFiZGFjNjZjYzZkMzQ4MjlkYTU1OWU4MTZiOGUyYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/302f46f0ea0620f9a8a8f7769ad24409d3b62891","sha":"302f46f0ea0620f9a8a8f7769ad24409d3b62891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/302f46f0ea0620f9a8a8f7769ad24409d3b62891"}],"sha":"e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/e631c986a1bdac66cc6d34829da559e816b8e2c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125115953?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mabdullahabaid","id":125115953,"login":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/302f46f0ea0620f9a8a8f7769ad24409d3b62891/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:33:38Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:33:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: bump brace-expansion to 5.0.8 in app lockfiles (Dependabot) (#23346)\n\n## Summary\n\nBumps **brace-expansion -> 5.0.8** in the three app lockfiles whose copy\nsits on the 5.x line, clearing **GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg** (high, vulnerable\n`<= 5.0.7`) on those manifests:\n\n- `examples/hello-world` (`^5.0.2`)\n- `examples/postcard` (`^5.0.5`)\n- `internal/self-hosting` (`^5.0.5`)\n\nAll three are caret ranges, so a recursive `yarn up -R brace-expansion`\nlifts them with **no resolution and no `package.json` change**.\n\n## Why the fixtures are not included\n\nThis advisory declares a single vulnerable range, `<= 5.0.7`, which\nspans **every** major line - so the `brace-expansion@2.1.2` copies in\n`seed-dependencies` and `common-layer-dependencies` are flagged as well.\nBut **2.1.2 is the last 2.x release** (1.x likewise ends at 1.1.16), and\nthe only patched version is **5.0.8**. Those consumers declare `^2.0.1`\n/ `^2.0.2`, which caps below 3.0.0, so there is no in-range fix:\nclearing them would mean forcing a cross-major jump from 2.x to 5.x via\na resolution, which is a behavior risk rather than a mechanical lift.\n\nSame situation for the root alert\n([1765](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/security/dependabot/1765)),\nwhere `nx` pins `brace-expansion` 5.0.6 exact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- brace-expansion resolves to **5.0.8** in all three lockfiles.\n- `yarn install --immutable` passes in each.\n- 5.0.8 published 2026-07-23, clears the 3-day npm age gate.","tree":{"sha":"7c829e8fa3305dd1f7ce968b7600b5365a5122ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/7c829e8fa3305dd1f7ce968b7600b5365a5122ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/302f46f0ea0620f9a8a8f7769ad24409d3b62891","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c829e8fa3305dd1f7ce968b7600b5365a5122ef\nparent f834b020b668121ea36139effd855f8b3aa25cb2\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1785152018 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785152018 +0000\n\nfix: bump brace-expansion to 5.0.8 in app lockfiles (Dependabot) (#23346)\n\n## Summary\n\nBumps **brace-expansion -> 5.0.8** in the three app lockfiles whose copy\nsits on the 5.x line, clearing **GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg** (high, vulnerable\n`<= 5.0.7`) on those manifests:\n\n- `examples/hello-world` (`^5.0.2`)\n- `examples/postcard` (`^5.0.5`)\n- `internal/self-hosting` (`^5.0.5`)\n\nAll three are caret ranges, so a recursive `yarn up -R brace-expansion`\nlifts them with **no resolution and no `package.json` change**.\n\n## Why the fixtures are not included\n\nThis advisory declares a single vulnerable range, `<= 5.0.7`, which\nspans **every** major line - so the `brace-expansion@2.1.2` copies in\n`seed-dependencies` and `common-layer-dependencies` are flagged as well.\nBut **2.1.2 is the last 2.x release** (1.x likewise ends at 1.1.16), and\nthe only patched version is **5.0.8**. Those consumers declare `^2.0.1`\n/ `^2.0.2`, which caps below 3.0.0, so there is no in-range fix:\nclearing them would mean forcing a cross-major jump from 2.x to 5.x via\na resolution, which is a behavior risk rather than a mechanical lift.\n\nSame situation for the root alert\n([1765](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/security/dependabot/1765)),\nwhere `nx` pins `brace-expansion` 5.0.6 exact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- brace-expansion resolves to **5.0.8** in all three lockfiles.\n- `yarn install --immutable` passes in each.\n- 5.0.8 published 2026-07-23, clears the 3-day npm age gate.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ0IiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEuAQAAfypts8haOMqXAOYvVlsBGw\nX36CJBSe6v/T7WCMvZBLRcV8FDgf13gw6SZySzxvkd2OsAsyjFPKB3NJRk+/bEsN\nrIus/YjYAZCURBHb5la3M7Ftq7JhDX9TfZdJMO15hKoLylHbhZx8COOh2TGYRSoT\nCx5d1GdPe+g4FbWV9W43U9ZasSQg2HJssDAOmQVoU2FUaokY7jEKiVdV3BI11p5z\nkzxqaQUaasEoGitao9upIiWlaJbIS6j6PT0aqohsT8dhFLOSJiUdUk+3wE9c12R0\nhqvDNvnGRf/H6kIlNuAVozZJ7kdbVkd+gygUeDbKcFsiOr5DbQX8ySkTno8bYWhd\nRo37zOXc7T6nTN6ETwA/J1a7P5C+D9fjVjM5lUQYl+k9erqXPDMBaHZI7raLu6rY\njpuwqRAl5GEIS9om/amXjB5JAtEzR5kQ8dE1igWp+K7mKC+PT6nOeq2OcrHUqSPm\n0NWpw3CvtBJh+yhEgqnTP0qWSMPr1gQvtiGt1RvaEfERcGHNcgB2NDpZ1NXm5g4X\nPG/bPkYEYGNJp8ldHqlYxZWRlMI4HggYZ6E+3RyInt5oHTdl0sVOm6k/7iCDvBC0\nuVF9LUPaH/i31tEVH391uo6/7vt/wQuFErKw6rMlucSjV0VT11DgOCet6gSsv5Bc\nkR+b4MlPQ3m7mX/0zGLK\n=9iUu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/s