n/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/a6b36422f947469fea608faf26b21287a73a7607/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:31:20Z","email":"142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nitin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:31:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fireflies: upgrade to twenty-sdk 2.23 (#23349)\n\nFireflies was skipped by both SDK bump sweeps (#23124, #23165) and sat\non `twenty-sdk ^2.18.0` with no `engines.twenty` floor, while the rest\nof the published set moved to `2.23.0-alpha.2`.\n\n- `twenty-sdk` / `twenty-client-sdk` `^2.18.0` -> `2.23.0-alpha.2`\n- adds `engines.twenty: \">=2.23.0\"`\n\nNo source changes needed: the 2.19 identifier migration (#22601) only\naffected apps referencing a standard object''s system-field identifier,\ndefining a relation into a standard object, or calling the field-UID\nderivation helper. Fireflies does none of those.\n\nThe `engines.twenty` floor means the app integration job needs a server\nimage at 2.23+, so it may fail on version mismatch rather than an app\ndefect, as in #22601.","tree":{"sha":"73a740e94a10828020e2788adc5ddf676081a401","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/73a740e94a10828020e2788adc5ddf676081a401"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/a6b36422f947469fea608faf26b21287a73a7607","verification":{"payload":"tree 73a740e94a10828020e2788adc5ddf676081a401\nparent cdd78462b90ef370e8c8863100687e3bd107da6a\nauthor nitin <142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com> 1785148280 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785148280 +0000\n\nFireflies: upgrade to twenty-sdk 2.23 (#23349)\n\nFireflies was skipped by both SDK bump sweeps (#23124, #23165) and sat\non `twenty-sdk ^2.18.0` with no `engines.twenty` floor, while the rest\nof the published set moved to `2.23.0-alpha.2`.\n\n- `twenty-sdk` / `twenty-client-sdk` `^2.18.0` -> `2.23.0-alpha.2`\n- adds `engines.twenty: \">=2.23.0\"`\n\nNo source changes needed: the 2.19 identifier migration (#22601) only\naffected apps referencing a standard object''s system-field identifier,\ndefining a relation into a standard object, or calling the field-UID\nderivation helper. Fireflies does none of those.\n\nThe `engines.twenty` floor means the app integration job needs a server\nimage at 2.23+, so it may fail on version mismatch rather than an app\ndefect, as in #22601.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZzOICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARkcQAHva7e/OmnBIlNtqQG7Kzs8x\ntRsQDDTLluI8pqWkxMUJE7KqLeur2fEqJsSeymSJkYNUvCPQKY6FElHEXTSNckHa\ns5BCipqGVSQIJ3KORFIklWkVgxaQwWg5ll1Q6vFKuQdoBTWp6y+04pMb53Jd+Xaf\n95T7yY66WN7JmBfRl5EifY3FKTEqmhGAciVhqS6CPlyXnT2TWaww/iK3ZpbEQ0oD\ndmn2+srVia2KWZ7N7dQkT1Vg1JmG2RiiR3ggrmhwdh9wduMwfmUP4SKjFr4wgzN1\nG91Wd/1pmUY6chp45F+mc4xdiWhnF/faGZLY+UlVd+hIDpFdUsMw2Nwkv4gYEMwt\nkpfVSc/8WDQ0ZYmcIdEr9/7AXy47jkE20qPc/wuDLc8F5mC42QpZYH1lMIKTMiQ2\nCMXkhINjTCk73lhULIOSp4JjJAOg+f5NpNHfGJoYMQEO1Z582LKip4XoKGvzwzU9\nt4AZR+vENRh/xORHXLxxDu6/z4mKHCjxdPgByT2uXBnXuB7CiYNTpJrtBwAGQt6E\nUZhu3hrU08cruPZ6W41MQ2JQttUhMmaUdf85j83p3HzIv7FTChg0uGH3IzIHj3lY\nbDzhOvUgd3cdrc9DgKCTJGEzoJpyovvXdMvwITV51AgIADi2dcEyf5Fav+E+mxQt\n78MbV+6tNHfVaN1ziU8t\n=Jc31\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/a6b36422f947469fea608faf26b21287a73a7607","node_id":"C_kwDOTnk9wdoAKGE2YjM2NDIyZjk0NzQ2OWZlYTYwOGZhZjI2YjIxMjg3YTczYTc2MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ndlomoro/twenty/commit/cdd78462b90ef370e8c8863100687e3bd107da6a","sha":"cdd78462b90ef370e8c8863100687e3bd107da6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/cdd78462b90ef370e8c8863100687e3bd107da6a"}],"sha":"a6b36422f947469fea608faf26b21287a73a7607","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/a6b36422f947469fea608faf26b21287a73a7607"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/commits/cdd78462b90ef370e8c8863100687e3bd107da6a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:25:34Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:25:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: block route triggers for suspended workspaces (#23347)\n\n## Problem\n\nLogic function route triggers (app HTTP endpoints served under `/s/*`\nand public domains) kept serving traffic for suspended workspaces. A\nworkspace suspended for non-payment (`activationStatus = SUSPENDED`)\nstill served its route triggers for the entire suspension window until\nsoft-deletion removed it from domain lookup. Every other trigger path\ngates on activation status — cron triggers only process `ACTIVE`\nworkspaces — but the route trigger path had no check at all.\n\n## Fix\n\n`RouteTriggerService.getLogicFunctionWithPathParamsOrFail` now rejects\nrequests when the resolved workspace has `activationStatus = SUSPENDED`,\nthrowing a `RouteTriggerException` with a new `WORKSPACE_SUSPENDED` code\nmapped to `403 Forbidden` in the REST exception filter. Scope is\nintentionally limited to `SUSPENDED`; other non-active statuses and the\nDB event trigger path are untouched.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23347?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1460e45e8a04602979b4abbc5e386e6923216d4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/trees/1460e45e8a04602979b4abbc5e386e6923216d4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ndlomoro/twenty/git/commits/cdd78462b90ef370e8c8863100687e3bd107da6a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1460e45e8a04602979b4abbc5e386e6923216d4f\nparent 5948c167a0ccd23ba9ae77749ae861d29eb82e87\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1785147934 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785147934 +0000\n\nfix: block route triggers for suspended workspaces (#23347)\n\n## Problem\n\nLogic function route triggers (app HTTP endpoints served under `/s/*`\nand public domains) kept serving traffic for suspended workspaces. A\nworkspace suspended for non-payment (`activationStatus = SUSPENDED`)\nstill served its route triggers for the entire suspension window until\nsoft-deletion removed it from domain lookup. Every other trigger path\ngates on activation status — cron triggers only process `ACTIVE`\nworkspaces — but the route trigger path had no check at all.\n\n## Fix\n\n`RouteTriggerService.getLogicFunctionWithPathParamsOrFail` now rejects\nrequests when the resolved workspace has `activationStatus = SUSPENDED`,\nthrowing a `RouteTriggerException` with a new `WORKSPACE_SUSPENDED` code\nmapped to `403 Forbidden` in the REST exception filter. Scope is\nintentionally limited to `SUSPENDED`; other non-active statuses and the\nDB event trigger path are untouched.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23347?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZzIuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuowQAEVA6Elj08X0hlH9Xq+QjTNJ\nt30902DR+1U2MO60XxFTO9pi4BXwajbWf4X18lsdihhyCt/19vjfrYioDAWPrtNy\n0EyAeUamAdsjCG4PCc6ECJACi6AYDoK6RgsqULpekimOvt+VV7QTq+KInjZTR9FV\n3vp/KNHnblk5gK6fTM+hhZzEZtjkv70RrE6kquTt8GvY4ZEqNUlIGf30mPBUxkrg\njhJRwB4GNlg2AWRolvETXSdtJ1UkM8XJ/o4lssFofQSPyDgczRR0rGe1RFNpiexb\nB0kqkUrflG7LXW+2ePp0lUKS9PlEbWQYe41k0gRe5kYGCNr4si9eSfqImTxlTYk/\n44MTt3s9ScgYiYKyDq2fyUeG2cuR2VZuE+G4S5uBxJFjV65MTKwD2cFXD9PVgOj1\njRLu5/4/aui7gKmUvR6+C3Ay3zNEN5FyBU4XbCEHXkTokiNFf870VG3c6s57U4uv\nQddo56QeYx3lRknAt3r3xmoMHW497O6MfoG5+rwBbQlPqn2Qa6wPebYCEbJuMIld\n2AZQ00s6ujMA5Hg7gz9LPnw7vVcAvVkqW3VrNaOhHhg5ABf8IsBYSGNo3UvoG1L8\nzSx8KbO1tbMQzN1S06gYVrWX5n+lxBtvTAcDFlJ2NbaVd1nAFVnM4hOfTsMGOKfM\njdDfuG0DU1JCfR3e+mLN\n=fc8x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:16:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-fl