"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/9509c737e032ad6528ccadfce93dbe16fa434b2e","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDk1MDljNzM3ZTAzMmFkNjUyOGNjYWRmY2U5M2RiZTE2ZmE0MzRiMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124","sha":"884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124"}],"sha":"9509c737e032ad6528ccadfce93dbe16fa434b2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/9509c737e032ad6528ccadfce93dbe16fa434b2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:33:52Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:33:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Remove grey corners around navigation menu items on mobile (#23425)\n\nOn mobile, folder items in the navigation drawer were wrapped in a faint\ngrey rounded box, showing up as small grey corners around the item. It\nwas not part of any design.\n\n## Cause\n\n`NavigationDrawerItemsCollapsableContainer` renders each folder group\ninside a framer-motion div and animates its chrome through the `animate`\nobject:\n\n- collapsed group: `border: ''1px solid <2% black>''`, `borderRadius: md`,\n`backgroundColor: <2% black>`\n- expanded: `border: ''none''`, `backgroundColor: ''transparent''`\n\n`none` is not an animatable value for framer-motion, so once the\ncollapsed border had been applied it was never cleared. `borderRadius`\nwas never part of the expanded target at all, so it stuck too. The\ninline style on the group container ended up as:\n\n```\nwidth: auto; background-color: transparent; border: 1px solid color(display-p3 0 0 0 / 0.02); border-radius: var(--t-border-radius-md);\n```\n\nThe drawer starts collapsed on mobile (`isNavigationDrawerExpandedState`\ndefaults to `!isMobile`) and is expanded when the user opens it, so\nevery folder group passed through the collapsed state and kept the\nhairline box. On desktop the drawer starts expanded, which is why it\nnormally does not show there — but collapsing and re-expanding the\nsidebar reproduced the exact same leftover.\n\nOnly folders were affected: the group chrome is applied when `isGroup`\nis true, which requires more than one folder in the section.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe group background, border and radius now live in the styled component\nand are driven by an `isCollapsedGroup` prop, with a CSS transition on\nthe background. framer-motion only animates the width, which it handles\ncorrectly.\n\n## Verification\n\nRan the app locally against a seeded workspace with three folders, at\n393px width and at 1280px.\n\n- Mobile: folder rows no longer carry a border or radius; the group\ncontainer computes to `border: 0px none`, `border-radius: 0px`,\ntransparent background\n- Desktop expanded: unchanged, no chrome\n- Desktop collapsed: group pill still renders as before (1px hairline,\n16px radius, 2% black background, 24px wide)\n- Desktop collapse then re-expand: chrome is now cleared instead of\nsticking\n\nLint, format and typecheck pass on the changed file.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_018wtVx6vj3ZbHT3vijBLwMW)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23425?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"abeba454f97b3a71a8e88e04822652c43e2b137f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/abeba454f97b3a71a8e88e04822652c43e2b137f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124","verification":{"payload":"tree abeba454f97b3a71a8e88e04822652c43e2b137f\nparent 7b81d9ab83bf7a8978c7341810ac544b99b14c7f\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1785249232 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785249232 +0200\n\nRemove grey corners around navigation menu items on mobile (#23425)\n\nOn mobile, folder items in the navigation drawer were wrapped in a faint\ngrey rounded box, showing up as small grey corners around the item. It\nwas not part of any design.\n\n## Cause\n\n`NavigationDrawerItemsCollapsableContainer` renders each folder group\ninside a framer-motion div and animates its chrome through the `animate`\nobject:\n\n- collapsed group: `border: ''1px solid <2% black>''`, `borderRadius: md`,\n`backgroundColor: <2% black>`\n- expanded: `border: ''none''`, `backgroundColor: ''transparent''`\n\n`none` is not an animatable value for framer-motion, so once the\ncollapsed border had been applied it was never cleared. `borderRadius`\nwas never part of the expanded target at all, so it stuck too. The\ninline style on the group container ended up as:\n\n```\nwidth: auto; background-color: transparent; border: 1px solid color(display-p3 0 0 0 / 0.02); border-radius: var(--t-border-radius-md);\n```\n\nThe drawer starts collapsed on mobile (`isNavigationDrawerExpandedState`\ndefaults to `!isMobile`) and is expanded when the user opens it, so\nevery folder group passed through the collapsed state and kept the\nhairline box. On desktop the drawer starts expanded, which is why it\nnormally does not show there — but collapsing and re-expanding the\nsidebar reproduced the exact same leftover.\n\nOnly folders were affected: the group chrome is applied when `isGroup`\nis true, which requires more than one folder in the section.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe group background, border and radius now live in the styled component\nand are driven by an `isCollapsedGroup` prop, with a CSS transition on\nthe background. framer-motion only animates the width, which it handles\ncorrectly.\n\n## Verification\n\nRan the app locally against a seeded workspace with three folders, at\n393px width and at 1280px.\n\n- Mobile: folder rows no longer carry a border or radius; the group\ncontainer computes to `border: 0px none`, `border-radius: 0px`,\ntransparent background\n- Desktop expanded: unchanged, no chrome\n- Desktop collapsed: group pill still renders as before (1px hairline,\n16px radius, 2% black background, 24px wide)\n- Desktop collapse then re-expand: chrome is now cleared instead of\nsticking\n\nLint, format and typecheck pass on the changed file.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_018wtVx6vj3ZbHT3vijBLwMW)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23425?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaL3RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5BYQAD/5f/MSJvM+no2vD4bIlTVe\nDNV32ahP+wbAdzwer96EiHvK+m4P911TeLax0056eLfu+pdY0tChCjbRgj6+OoX+\nucRNDTyEn3tl2DkaTRVE9FQoGq7or3nM04aXfy9kErNVmLajEAORBwG+qSuP4u+/\nPJ5Ds22b7Jj4EvWEsZHywMUOsuNHZG5N+/29Vry9TQucMqHSZC4c3hmeWvZ26Agk\nS7Rp6xzGGaui+UeRgqQfbTDNHuNGI6wYYXP6xkcrH+Peydr0kVXp9Lh7zuDxkWZ8\nFQBDPTbL3IX7fp0lsemlGYyXPJkhJapHgKpmAeavH7PDm7RItE1uZ9mVGL3UOJD6\nZ6uONu6W1M85qgRo6V/qab0iMDmm2NC2WLwRA02x4vlD+hhpjeBaG3NyQYlKS8bs\nibeYy8in1J+cmoOuFQbRtM14Oa7u8rt3eCWnx3hslKd6gmFlwUUyv3ygx52VktDW\n7Fw+sAfBvJ6RVqKWa6vtLTfluXy0iJMSlG5Vuak6Yo5tH6Tkyu7cTITIAn8GkMsD\n7jWC3aFITr1fJLgcWrrBMy+j4o7whmgHxFtTto6a7q8aIat8t3808elR3E/wpBPQ\nPXoIaakQUJQ3JMkHWdZB3JQ4hEKrsxPvhHVi2mjWNZ4NAO0sbOlQfGzQNskF5Z63\n9mEH4uwgSR024h5v1CoI\n=Wtmk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDg4NGY0NzA5ODJiMzgyYTBkNWI3MWE0MzE1NzQ2MWVlYzBmOGQxMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/7b81d9ab83bf7a8978c7341810ac544b99b14c7f","sha":"7b81d9ab83bf7a8978c7341810ac544b99b14c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/7b81d9ab83bf7a8978c7341810ac544b99b14c7f"}],"sha":"884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/884f470982b382a0d5b71a43157461eec0f8d124"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142569587?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ehconitin","id":142569587,"login":"ehconitin","node_id":"U_kgDOCH9wcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/7b81d9ab83bf7a8978c7341810ac544b99b14c7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:08:39Z","email":"142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nitin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:08:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix call-recorder REC badge rendering as empty boxes (#23415)\n\n## What was wrong\n\nThe bot camera image draws a \"REC\" pill on top of the workspace logo.\nThe label used an SVG `<text>` element, and sharp resolves SVG text\nthrough the host''s fonts. The runtimes that execute app logic functions\nship no fonts, so every character fell back to an empty box: the badge\nshowed \"▯▯▯\" instead of \"REC\" in real meetings. It looked fine locally\nbecause dev machines have fonts.\n\n## The fix\n\nDraw the label as vector outlines instead of text. \"REC\" is outlined\nonce from Inter SemiBold and stored as an SVG path constant, so the\nbadge renders the same on any host with no font lookup. The pill width\nis derived from its contents instead of hardcoded, and tests fail if\n`<text>` or `font-family` ever comes back.\n\n<img width=\"2120\" height=\"1191\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-07-28 at 19 16 46\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5fa0958-35ba-48da-be9c-a6af81ec2fa0\"\n/>\n\n\n1 -- the bug on prod\n2 -- how it looks when its not bugged on prod\n3 -- this branches changes\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23415?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"b80715b9db47e2ea895f83be468c2a81c38d29af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/b80715b9db47e2ea895f83be468c2a81c38d29af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/7b81d9ab83bf7a8978c7341810ac544b99b14c7f","verification":{"payload":"tree b80715b9db47e2ea895f83be468c2a81c38d29af\nparent 1fb1232a1743c3d8148875f68ba87d470f770f20\nauthor nitin <142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com> 1785247719 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785247719 +0000\n\nFix call-recorder REC badge rendering as empty boxes (#23415)\n\n## What was wrong\n\nThe bot camera image draws a \"REC\" pill on top of the workspace logo.\nThe label used an SVG `<text>` element, and sharp resolves SVG text\nthrough the host''s fonts. The runtimes that execute app logic functions\nship no fonts, so every character fell back to an empty box: the badge\nshowed \"▯▯▯\" instead of \"REC\" in real meetings. It looked fine locally\nbecause dev machines have fonts.\n\n## The fix\n\nDraw the label as vector outlines instead of text. \"REC\" is outlined\nonce from Inter SemiBold and stored as an SVG path constant, so the\nbadge renders the same on any host with no font lookup. The pill width\nis derived from its contents instead of hardcoded, and tests fail if\n`<text>` or `font-family` ever comes back.\n\n<img width=\"2120\" height=\"1191\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-07-28 at 19 16 46\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5fa0958-35ba-48da-be9c-a6af81ec2fa0\"\n/>\n\n\n1 -- the bug on prod\n2 -- how it looks when its not bugged on prod\n3 -- this branches changes\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23415?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaLfsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWL0QAFyLzJLvVaYl+3qY3r3+yds6\n1zUyL0EeCrZ8FkwPx/TbBmXAsQKS5ttfrradADIySkul8zTpIeb0NxB/YVu5MxOO\nZQUEtM7n/VfceH353qnWqCNx6b8WcqA535f+dzZF7mYl4swgxMjbgXLhXI1HgnDL\n3OPJqKllJX87uJ3wyZ4gSVWmtG+jzmHjlW7bh6cpoCN27JdG5UeU5y/o+A/YIfWb\nQTIEUusgYrfGViH48VR63/mphjs6pAzQ97QvWs0p69BhNbUx0LWOqMclcI6q+NRm\nSVfnfmP9X9flAXjvI4gNwupve3sV2t8bVoyhtnmdZEj4mecOM328QZiqU8qlZQQ9\nXiHe+tWfkMcvmVRrNTPC68f8WBvT/RFQ8qPyNwMT4lB1DmqMe3M2tW0ybHtHmAPL\nEyvBa61uBF1xr16cEhAH8NpkXVO9QFw7V+saXWazOlzVYuDcLGs10RWAU9Xuum6F\nKH4z9yJSdh2AgvZH7UbVCp9ocDoFBdT1rUo7Mayn+4wDOUMTn7JOS0oee040vsqx\nl9T81OmHZFHMDcbhbBj5/nOKC/yuyl7CvrTV4oBexaVoMY88XJLb4G75g2b02NEE\nWt0Xq9lLCO6q4Xh6EQEqKe9rMAfdWxZNEXdJ+NhEWyFs4nwMz3u88e3Y/HF5c3M9\nhMW/TZGw37qdh0CUfLlt\n=iM+T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_