twentycrm-npt/commit/dfea3af7785e4a1355cf4919a11a61b2db3824e8","sha":"dfea3af7785e4a1355cf4919a11a61b2db3824e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/dfea3af7785e4a1355cf4919a11a61b2db3824e8"}],"sha":"902bc6db635f9c637601b5d496e039f45f6b101f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/902bc6db635f9c637601b5d496e039f45f6b101f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/dfea3af7785e4a1355cf4919a11a61b2db3824e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:21:30Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:21:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai-chat): enrich zero-output stream captures and keep client-error exceptions out of Sentry (#23426)\n\n## What & why\n\nTwo related fixes that clean up Sentry reporting for the AI chat flow.\n\n### 1. Enriched zero-output stream captures\n\nThe AI chat stream''s rejection handler previously skipped only\n`AbortError` and captured everything else to Sentry as-is. Two problems:\n\n- The SDK''s bare `NoOutputGeneratedError` carries no troubleshooting\ncontext, so the Sentry issues were unactionable (no model, provider,\nworkspace, or conversation size).\n- Expected interruptions (user abort, `STREAM_INTERRUPTED`) still\ngenerated noise.\n\nThe rejection handler now handles three cases inline:\n\n- `AbortError` and `STREAM_INTERRUPTED` are expected interruptions and\nare not captured.\n- `NoOutputGeneratedError` is replaced with a single error whose message\ncarries the full context as plain JSON: model, provider, workspace,\nthread, stream, turn, message count, conversation size, elapsed time,\nand the underlying stream error - recorded via a new `onError` handler,\nwhich also keeps stream-level errors visible in the worker logs.\n- Anything else is captured unchanged.\n\nThe stable message prefix and single capture site keep zero-output\nevents grouped separately from raw provider errors in Sentry.\n\n### 2. Keep client-error domain exceptions out of Sentry\n\n`BILLING_CREDITS_EXHAUSTED` (a 402, i.e. an expected \"user out of\ncredits\" condition) was landing in Sentry. Root cause: `CustomException`\ncarries no HTTP status, so the worker/BullMQ path hands the raw\nexception to `shouldCaptureException`, which can''t tell a 4xx client\nerror from a 5xx server error and captures everything. The GraphQL/REST\nedges convert exceptions first, but background jobs bypass those\nconverters.\n\nFix, mirroring how `HttpException.getStatus()` already works:\n\n- `CustomException` gains an intrinsic `statusCode`.\n- `shouldCaptureException` skips a `CustomException` whose `statusCode <\n500`, as a branch symmetric to the existing `HttpException` check. This\ncovers every path, including the worker.\n- `BillingException` populates `statusCode` from the existing\n`getBillingExceptionStatusCode` mapping, so credits-exhausted (402)\nstays out of Sentry while the 500-mapped billing codes are still\ncaptured.\n\nExceptions that don''t set `statusCode` default to undefined and are\ncaptured exactly as before, so other domains are unaffected until they\nopt in.\n\n## Tests\n\n- ai-chat unit suite passes (13 suites, 76 tests).\n- Existing billing exception handler tests pass.\n- `typecheck` passes.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23426?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"895fae27187fa0379a55b3a74fe4c040daa2025d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/895fae27187fa0379a55b3a74fe4c040daa2025d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/dfea3af7785e4a1355cf4919a11a61b2db3824e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 895fae27187fa0379a55b3a74fe4c040daa2025d\nparent ceb699c43f0fc98ec9399a10f75216ea0905ec0d\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1785244890 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785244890 +0000\n\nfix(ai-chat): enrich zero-output stream captures and keep client-error exceptions out of Sentry (#23426)\n\n## What & why\n\nTwo related fixes that clean up Sentry reporting for the AI chat flow.\n\n### 1. Enriched zero-output stream captures\n\nThe AI chat stream''s rejection handler previously skipped only\n`AbortError` and captured everything else to Sentry as-is. Two problems:\n\n- The SDK''s bare `NoOutputGeneratedError` carries no troubleshooting\ncontext, so the Sentry issues were unactionable (no model, provider,\nworkspace, or conversation size).\n- Expected interruptions (user abort, `STREAM_INTERRUPTED`) still\ngenerated noise.\n\nThe rejection handler now handles three cases inline:\n\n- `AbortError` and `STREAM_INTERRUPTED` are expected interruptions and\nare not captured.\n- `NoOutputGeneratedError` is replaced with a single error whose message\ncarries the full context as plain JSON: model, provider, workspace,\nthread, stream, turn, message count, conversation size, elapsed time,\nand the underlying stream error - recorded via a new `onError` handler,\nwhich also keeps stream-level errors visible in the worker logs.\n- Anything else is captured unchanged.\n\nThe stable message prefix and single capture site keep zero-output\nevents grouped separately from raw provider errors in Sentry.\n\n### 2. Keep client-error domain exceptions out of Sentry\n\n`BILLING_CREDITS_EXHAUSTED` (a 402, i.e. an expected \"user out of\ncredits\" condition) was landing in Sentry. Root cause: `CustomException`\ncarries no HTTP status, so the worker/BullMQ path hands the raw\nexception to `shouldCaptureException`, which can''t tell a 4xx client\nerror from a 5xx server error and captures everything. The GraphQL/REST\nedges convert exceptions first, but background jobs bypass those\nconverters.\n\nFix, mirroring how `HttpException.getStatus()` already works:\n\n- `CustomException` gains an intrinsic `statusCode`.\n- `shouldCaptureException` skips a `CustomException` whose `statusCode <\n500`, as a branch symmetric to the existing `HttpException` check. This\ncovers every path, including the worker.\n- `BillingException` populates `statusCode` from the existing\n`getBillingExceptionStatusCode` mapping, so credits-exhausted (402)\nstays out of Sentry while the 500-mapped billing codes are still\ncaptured.\n\nExceptions that don''t set `statusCode` default to undefined and are\ncaptured exactly as before, so other domains are unaffected until they\nopt in.\n\n## Tests\n\n- ai-chat unit suite passes (13 suites, 76 tests).\n- Existing billing exception handler tests pass.\n- `typecheck` passes.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23426?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaKzrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzzsQAKdjSr3qyS/6WGpNubbo98pI\nF3TE2WRDHWR2PKx/IOLnQdDlGvJlyOr/obGK0LWAacTgFkeKLfVL6d53wMePvfyt\nkxbeWvpFCNcllnh56RfC8ZB0xI1+oOhnk9uUTEfP0SDRizf08Yy7byEplI8cfDhb\nI9v1CjPS10vpEgk7ikVZczlhj9McKcDiGWgLw8TeoHSJzYAfTbo7fKK+f7G708E4\nJnOPmtAq/WWK0UwIuNvD2gj8J73MJAUcP2qAnCEWM+p/h5F4te12f5Qm6M5Ryi8L\n9eCbph5r2GLFZOGFjBp50KoptB/ZAKrbZo/dGH2pLyOiAR0lMMK87MqoEbM2ypJ+\noSzmB4AHu6XUcw1q8bhnsCtVnIwGBlXMgHLoUa83orJAhy8yaWCjjRBcNoD+tB5p\n7rPZqRFHiFVq/6LVL/gXOenB1XPDB9kpnO41z3MnQ8wXyXkTioeNwZHF/z1DfUDj\n0DRi+jW1GnPYqTdGh8OVwt4aK5OUkHqW5XFdS0p/ihH8P6/5WX3/i9U4vadzn6Me\nUg7RV+SXoGD9IbxLcpna1TcdqwQGajg41sEiq40yC3kAqjxFvENRk5jE5UVXwbVR\nF6Wz01gfwLmjpw1Br6SDmjuAt6B1uAAbbykez0U3ZSuYEaAJguDtDtDhwlftZ03X\n4pBHr4gKym28mJ50NxLj\n=8fG/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/othe