_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/ceb699c43f0fc98ec9399a10f75216ea0905ec0d","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGNlYjY5OWM0M2YwZmM5OGVjOTM5OWExMGY3NTIxNmVhMDkwNWVjMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155","sha":"b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155"}],"sha":"ceb699c43f0fc98ec9399a10f75216ea0905ec0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/ceb699c43f0fc98ec9399a10f75216ea0905ec0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:59:33Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:59:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Unify remote element style declarations (#23263)\n\nFront components run in a Web Worker with a fake DOM. Until now the\nworker had a hand-rolled `style` object for remote elements and the host\nhad its own separate CSS-string parser: two implementations of the same\nparsing that kept drifting apart (several review rounds fixed edge cases\nin one copy but not the other).\n\nWhat changed:\n- One shared `createStyleProxy` now backs `element.style` in the worker,\nand one shared `parseCssDeclarations` feeds both the worker proxy and\nthe host''s `parseCssString`. Most of the diff is existing logic split\nout of `installStylePropertyOnRemoteElements` into small single-purpose\nutils (`splitCssDeclarations`, `stripImportantPriorityFromCssValue`,\n`normalizeCssPropertyName`, `formatCssValue`, ...), not new behavior.\n- `!important` is stripped from values instead of tracked. Nothing ever\nread priorities back, and the host applies styles through React inline\nstyles, which cannot express `!important`. Rendering note: `color: red\n!important` used to reach React as an invalid value (property silently\nnot applied); it now applies, without the priority.\n- Style writes flush to the host synchronously, exactly as on main.\n- The parser handles quotes, escapes and parentheses; CSS comments\ninside hand-written `cssText` are not supported.\n\nThis shared proxy is also the base for the worker `getComputedStyle`\nstub in the geometry PR. Second of three PRs splitting the geometry\nmirror work.","tree":{"sha":"6a9a5feb443187cdeba722da3ffc0ed2df349ddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/6a9a5feb443187cdeba722da3ffc0ed2df349ddf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/b8e2a6e910c39e1e13fae05d7fc38f5d92f50155","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a9a5feb443187cdeba722da3ffc0ed2df349ddf\nparent 64001591f29fffce37d8935878c3153d6054c9ed\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1785243573 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785243573 +0000\n\nUnify remote element style declarations (#23263)\n\nFront components run in a Web Worker with a fake DOM. Until now the\nworker had a hand-rolled `style` object for remote elements and the host\nhad its own separate CSS-string parser: two implementations of the same\nparsing that kept drifting apart (several review rounds fixed edge cases\nin one copy but not the other).\n\nWhat changed:\n- One shared `createStyleProxy` now backs `element.style` in the worker,\nand one shared `parseCssDeclarations` feeds both the worker proxy and\nthe host''s `parseCssString`. Most of the diff is existing logic split\nout of `installStylePropertyOnRemoteElements` into small single-purpose\nutils (`splitCssDeclarations`, `stripImportantPriorityFromCssValue`,\n`normalizeCssPropertyName`, `formatCssValue`, ...), not new behavior.\n- `!important` is stripped from values instead of tracked. Nothing ever\nread priorities back, and the host applies styles through React inline\nstyles, which cannot express `!important`. Rendering note: `color: red\n!important` used to reach React as an invalid value (property silently\nnot applied); it now applies, without the priority.\n- Style writes flush to the host synchronously, exactly as on main.\n- The parser handles quotes, escapes and parentheses; CSS comments\ninside hand-written `cssText` are not supported.\n\nThis shared proxy is also the base for the worker `getComputedStyle`\nstub in the geometry PR. Second of three PRs splitting the geometry\nmirror work.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----