s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/7b46c3ed3184e4f9b3785da2d66ad51a0a6f965a","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDdiNDZjM2VkMzE4NGU0ZjliMzc4NWRhMmQ2NmFkNTFhMGE2Zjk2NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae","sha":"6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae"}],"sha":"7b46c3ed3184e4f9b3785da2d66ad51a0a6f965a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/7b46c3ed3184e4f9b3785da2d66ad51a0a6f965a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81605929?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulrahmancodes","id":81605929,"login":"abdulrahmancodes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjA1OTI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:53:31Z","email":"81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:53:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai-agent): use a non-workflow base system prompt for programmatic agent runs (#23394)\n\n`AgentAsyncExecutorService` hardcoded `WORKFLOW_SYSTEM_PROMPTS.BASE`, so\nevery caller was told \"You are executing as part of a workflow\nautomation\" and \"your output may be used by downstream workflow nodes\".\nThat is only true for the workflow AI-agent action. The `runAgent` API\n(used by apps such as the call recorder) and agent evaluations got the\nsame framing, which does not describe how they run or where their output\ngoes.\n\nThe executor no longer asserts its own execution context: `executeAgent`\nnow takes a required `baseSystemPrompt` and each caller supplies its\nown.\n\n- Workflow AI-agent action passes `WORKFLOW_SYSTEM_PROMPTS.BASE`\n(unchanged behavior)\n- `runAgent` and evaluations pass the new `AGENT_RUN_BASE_SYSTEM_PROMPT`\n\nThe param is required rather than defaulted so every call site states\nits context and no future caller silently inherits the wrong one.\n\nPrompt constants are also split one export per file, with the shared\ntool-usage guidance extracted into `TOOL_USAGE_STRATEGY` so both bases\ncompose it.\n\nNo GraphQL schema, SDK, or database changes.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23394?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"5e33e0f5d6ff4acadbfce6ae8f2849cd6846fdeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/5e33e0f5d6ff4acadbfce6ae8f2849cd6846fdeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e33e0f5d6ff4acadbfce6ae8f2849cd6846fdeb\nparent 3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21\nauthor Abdul Rahman <81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1785239611 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785239611 +0000\n\nfix(ai-agent): use a non-workflow base system prompt for programmatic agent runs (#23394)\n\n`AgentAsyncExecutorService` hardcoded `WORKFLOW_SYSTEM_PROMPTS.BASE`, so\nevery caller was told \"You are executing as part of a workflow\nautomation\" and \"your output may be used by downstream workflow nodes\".\nThat is only true for the workflow AI-agent action. The `runAgent` API\n(used by apps such as the call recorder) and agent evaluations got the\nsame framing, which does not describe how they run or where their output\ngoes.\n\nThe executor no longer asserts its own execution context: `executeAgent`\nnow takes a required `baseSystemPrompt` and each caller supplies its\nown.\n\n- Workflow AI-agent action passes `WORKFLOW_SYSTEM_PROMPTS.BASE`\n(unchanged behavior)\n- `runAgent` and evaluations pass the new `AGENT_RUN_BASE_SYSTEM_PROMPT`\n\nThe param is required rather than defaulted so every call site states\nits context and no future caller silently inherits the wrong one.\n\nPrompt constants are also split one export per file, with the shared\ntool-usage guidance extracted into `TOOL_USAGE_STRATEGY` so both bases\ncompose it.\n\nNo GraphQL schema, SDK, or database changes.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23394?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaJhLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVOYQAKI22LpyDdj4LrBS+nOcemew\nfAwVLX7YaQCMDjH88LRa9T7vbw6oHNgAAjywBfjJjyPGXLPh23EZUDoKx222jltF\nTgpSCbmv+je6vXYbkDMw2JfFfvW2oPnbd/PRgx1VKoarw6vzticGjcg9AbGXQLD0\nZ0nZEEkdwQDWbe+RBcR3Osrvnc6tSscdsMyNO4ZJOowpwq9nNidFWmPmqungKIBS\npKn9S7+IESOdh9KmTOvnuQ3Tky2d+kyuUj5CohUYhEOCr4pAyTX9gW+HAuCr107i\nZyzN3vOXuf5V3HZCJG4CLcxJC3+rxcio+glalLGkLZTJ8yVBx6n5HMZxRS6wOcxl\nXdSh658yXD7zKrZAY8h2189lnvt4E9r93pdhzAVi65s1A7zpLvVGfwzlKQDoGR3x\nO5f3UV8710sqCX4CkuMlypIejNYDtAzqgo3AVUq+3BW/3HCR8QC1E7JjNbFRzqqJ\n0AWLk61MRf0mMLoG3BrY4fshAodfLR31CfrsAnqkAB2jL2Q7G/YIP3n3V7eiB7R+\nbfhGvYB12vum4/TYxVHZBG7P283yev7XUwsHl0yUtcpyc9IHUrImNaiObTmsou6c\nO0CNLAG44IwU8U2yj2iwZZqbtsl7eg5ZG1y4T88LFVgekE8alPo5sf+5BtM4EGXA\nCDDR+AgpZs6f9xCSgZhB\n=jDNc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDZjNjZkNGM4NjI5ZWQyMjY3OGVkZmFjYTk4NTAxZTZiN2VmNjkyYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21","sha":"3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21"}],"sha":"6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/6c66d4c8629ed22678edfaca98501e6b7ef692ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:47:07Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:47:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(page-layout): let the column surface win over the solo presentation (#23412)\n\n## Why\n\nIn the side panel and on mobile, a tab holding a single widget renders\nwith no gutter at all: the field list sits flush against the panel\nborder. Regression from #23109.\n\n`getWidgetCardVariant` checked the derived presentation before the\nsurface:\n\n```ts\nif (presentation === ''solo'') return ''solo'';\nconst isSideColumnContext = isInPinnedTab || isMobile || isInSidePanel;\n```\n\nSo a single-widget tab resolved to `''solo''` even in the side panel or on\nmobile, and `''solo''` has no branch in `WidgetCard`''s padding switch, so\nit falls through to `0`. The same widget used to match `variant ===\n''side-column'' && !isEditable` and get `spacing[3]` (12px).\n\nThe pinned left panel escaped this only because `PageLayoutLeftPanel`\nhardcodes `presentation: ''stack''` — the rule was already there (\"the\npinned left panel is always a column, a surface rule not a widget\nrule\"), just applied at one call site instead of being the rule.\n\n## Why only the Home tab looks broken\n\nEvery widget that used to live on a `CANVAS` tab carries its own gutter,\nso losing the card padding costs them nothing:\n\n| Widget | Own horizontal padding |\n|---|---|\n| Timeline | `spacing[6]` |\n| Notes | `spacing[6]` |\n| Files | `spacing[6]` |\n| Tasks | `spacing[6]` |\n| **Fields** | **none** |\n\n`Fields` was the only widget on a `VERTICAL_LIST` tab, so it was the\nonly one relying on the card for its gutter, and the only one that ends\nup flush.\n\n## What\n\nResolve the surface first: a column surface (pinned panel, side panel,\nmobile) is always a column of cards, whatever the tab presentation is.\nSolo stays a main-tab-area concept.\n\nHeader visibility is untouched: `showHeader` keys off `presentation`,\nnot the variant, so a solo tab still shows no bare title row. The\n`Fields` widget does not regain the header it lost in #23109.\n\n## Measured\n\nSide panel, custom object whose Home tab holds a single Fields widget\n(1600x1000, panel at x=1200):\n\n| | Card padding | First label x |\n|---|---|---|\n| main | `0px` | 1221 |\n| this PR | `12px` | 1233 |\n\n12px restored, matching what the pinned left panel gives the same\nwidget.\n\n## Trade-off worth a second opinion\n\nIn the side panel and on mobile, the activity widgets now resolve to\n`''side-column''` instead of `''solo''`, so they pick up the card''s 12px on\ntop of their own 24px, i.e. 36px instead of 24px. Nothing overlaps or\nclips, but it is a visible change on those tabs. If you would rather\nkeep them at 24px, the follow-up is to drop the intrinsic `spacing[6]`\nfrom the activity cards and let the surface own the gutter everywhere.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `getWidgetCardVariant` tests extended: `''side-column''` now wins over\n`''solo''` for each of `isInPinnedTab` / `isMobile` / `isInSidePanel`. 13\ntests pass.\n- 88 suites / 620 tests across `page-layout/widgets` pass.\n- `lint:diff-with-main twenty-front` clean.\n- Verified against a local stack: side panel on a single-widget Home\ntab, before and after.","tree":{"sha":"e5235fcb8dc3f53be6070b3f9a0473a8a2de2f16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/e5235fcb8dc3f53be6070b3f9a0473a8a2de2f16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21","verification":{"payload":"tree e5235fcb8dc3f53be6070b3f9a0473a8a2de2f16\nparent 38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1785239227 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785239227 +0200\n\nfix(page-layout): let the column surface win over the solo presentation (#23412)\n\n## Why\n\nIn the side panel and on mobile, a tab holding a single widget renders\nwith no gutter at all: the field list sits flush against the panel\nborder. Regression from #23109.\n\n`getWidgetCardVariant` checked the derived presentation before the\nsurface:\n\n```ts\nif (presentation === ''solo'') return ''solo'';\nconst isSideColumnContext = isInPinnedTab || isMobile || isInSidePanel;\n```\n\nSo a single-widget tab resolved to `''solo''` even in the side panel or on\nmobile, and `''solo''` has no branch in `WidgetCard`''s padding switch, so\nit falls through to `0`. The same widget used to match `variant ===\n''side-column'' && !isEditable` and get `spacing[3]` (12px).\n\nThe pinned left panel escaped this only because `PageLayoutLeftPanel`\nhardcodes `presentation: ''stack''` — the rule was already there (\"the\npinned left panel is always a column, a surface rule not a widget\nrule\"), just applied at one call site instead of being the rule.\n\n## Why only the Home tab looks broken\n\nEvery widget that used to live on a `CANVAS` tab carries its own gutter,\nso losing the card padding costs them nothing:\n\n| Widget | Own horizontal padding |\n|---|---|\n| Timeline | `spacing[6]` |\n| Notes | `spacing[6]` |\n| Files | `spacing[6]` |\n| Tasks | `spacing[6]` |\n| **Fields** | **none** |\n\n`Fields` was the only widget on a `VERTICAL_LIST` tab, so it was the\nonly one relying on the card for its gutter, and the only one that ends\nup flush.\n\n## What\n\nResolve the surface first: a column surface (pinned panel, side panel,\nmobile) is always a column of cards, whatever the tab presentation is.\nSolo stays a main-tab-area concept.\n\nHeader visibility is untouched: `showHeader` keys off `presentation`,\nnot the variant, so a solo tab still shows no bare title row. The\n`Fields` widget does not regain the header it lost in #23109.\n\n## Measured\n\nSide panel, custom object whose Home tab holds a single Fields widget\n(1600x1000, panel at x=1200):\n\n| | Card padding | First label x |\n|---|---|---|\n| main | `0px` | 1221 |\n| this PR | `12px` | 1233 |\n\n12px restored, matching what the pinned left panel gives the same\nwidget.\n\n## Trade-off worth a second opinion\n\nIn the side panel and on mobile, the activity widgets now resolve to\n`''side-column''` instead of `''solo''`, so they pick up the card''s 12px on\ntop of their own 24px, i.e. 36px instead of 24px. Nothing overlaps or\nclips, but it is a visible change on those tabs. If you would rather\nkeep them at 24px, the follow-up is to drop the intrinsic `spacing[6]`\nfrom the activity cards and let the surface own the gutter everywhere.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `getWidgetCardVariant` tests extended: `''side-column''` now wins over\n`''solo''` for each of `isInPinnedTab` / `isMobile` / `isInSidePanel`. 13\ntests pass.\n- 88 suites / 620 tests across `page-layout/widgets` pass.\n- `lint:diff-with-main twenty-front` clean.\n- Verified against a local stack: side panel on a single-widget Home\ntab, before and after.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaJa7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPaoQAAkZGgL/ynIx2LifOPExY03N\nG1T2Ov5dpuDJm4C9HG5zOyupyr3UolSYGwBMFiqEMQV2ufHHtiXnudDFovAx5qIw\nbjuAv975DfQkpD3qjQesMMGJWf12jFynuPcAP7qLUVP8xmRujYW9ewOj+y6U1MDZ\n+5CtverE16wwT9aD/qpquWN7O0eH1rc6CeXN1IE8IlmexzuEkgm0B7f9IE+f7/Ky\nJvZlPmA+ne2SftP1HedY+N96Cy62jXIJ9Xt3Lj4bzFjsQlvB/izj9YNA71QPD8K7\n64WJNmWVBHaJbhhO1X9eBpIyaD3DHVZTB65ZulU4rfLl2/kF/OuVoOuoznSvUu0v\n5CoCDZW0hINj9MqoA/yyfpX4CliUOIQincHZWZozzrDWqEqYG/uB6u/eSDPWSGEh\nat58digxhtJwb9d/VhpDvn+jCTSvPF/indhxk20Q0jp/X6psxM2NVRpBRyrWWRLa\nBl8ckSz4Xc0L1QK45Dz7oJ8ZCRXbAg0BRXTZE2mkl/KSccQ23fMyixWq4n+WbElb\nnDWHEIOGqBpV37u1zWeDOY9UMTTE3Dq5BJYF3aNnVSmyTYb5M6GqirKNBK4xwY7X\nU6TJ/LRtNw9+ZqjYmoz0C9XRQel1ErJU/qAdL2l8Ny+UdCjhwFm72yH+dgVZuXBu\nXiYEHiUlRfG0ys5gIYt0\n=cZXl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDNmMDIzNmI1OTBkZDM3MmI3NTg1NTllYzU3OGU1YmRhNWViZDlhMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a","sha":"38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a"}],"sha":"3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/3f0236b590dd372b758559ec578e5bda5ebd9a21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:33:12Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:33:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: hide add-select-option prompt for users without data model permission (#23410)\n\nFixes #23341\n\n## Problem\n\nA user whose role lacks the `DATA_MODEL` permission flag still saw the\n`Add \"…\" to options` prompt when typing a value that matched no option\nin a multiselect. Clicking it did nothing.\n\n`MultiSelectInput` renders `AddSelectOptionMenuItem` based purely on\nwhether the callback exists:\n\n```tsx\n{onAddSelectOption && searchFilter && filteredOptionsInDropDown.length === 0 && (\n```\n\n`MultiSelectFieldInput` always passed a callback, and did the permission\ncheck *inside* it:\n\n```tsx\nconst handleAddSelectOption = (optionName: string) => {\n  if (!canAddSelectOption) {\n    return;\n  }\n  addSelectOption(optionName);\n};\n```\n\nSo the guard suppressed the click but not the render, which is exactly\nthe reported symptom: the prompt is visible and inert.\n\n## Fix\n\nGate at the prop instead of inside the handler, so the menu item is\nnever rendered when the action is unavailable:\n\n```tsx\nonAddSelectOption={canAddSelectOption ? addSelectOption : undefined}\n```\n\nThe wrapper is now redundant and removed; `addSelectOption` already has\nthe matching `(optionName: string) => void` signature.\n\n`SelectFieldInput` had the byte-identical bug (`SelectInput` gates on\n`onAddSelectOption &&` the same way), so it gets the same change.\n\n## Note on scope\n\n`useCanAddSelectOption` requires `objectNamePlural` from the route in\naddition to the permission flag:\n\n```ts\nconst canAddSelectOption =\n  userHasPermissionToEditDataModel &&\n  isNonEmptyString(fieldName) &&\n  isNonEmptyString(objectNamePlural);\n```\n\nRecord *detail* pages (`/object/:objectNameSingular/:recordId`) have no\n`objectNamePlural`, so the prompt was dead there for **every** user,\nadmins included. This change hides it in that case too, which is the\ncorrect behavior since the click could never have worked.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified manually against a local instance, toggling the patch in and\nout on the same cell so before/after is directly comparable.\n\nCompany `Work Policy` (multiselect) in the Companies table view, typing\na string that matches no option:\n\n| user | route | before | after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Member (no `DATA_MODEL`) | `/objects/companies` | prompt shown, click\ndoes nothing | prompt hidden |\n| Admin | `/objects/companies` | prompt shown, click works | prompt\nshown, click works (navigates to\n`/settings/objects/companies/workPolicy?newOption=…`) |\n| Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt shown, click does nothing |\nprompt hidden |\n\n`nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-front` and `nx typecheck twenty-front`\nboth pass.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23410?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"3789616673bc09a1ea4952ac1962aa975c6bf6c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/3789616673bc09a1ea4952ac1962aa975c6bf6c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a","verification":{"payload":"tree 3789616673bc09a1ea4952ac1962aa975c6bf6c0\nparent 1064ae835bd97db423f73c55cdf84f8c2bcf75f8\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1785238392 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785238392 +0000\n\nfix: hide add-select-option prompt for users without data model permission (#23410)\n\nFixes #23341\n\n## Problem\n\nA user whose role lacks the `DATA_MODEL` permission flag still saw the\n`Add \"…\" to options` prompt when typing a value that matched no option\nin a multiselect. Clicking it did nothing.\n\n`MultiSelectInput` renders `AddSelectOptionMenuItem` based purely on\nwhether the callback exists:\n\n```tsx\n{onAddSelectOption && searchFilter && filteredOptionsInDropDown.length === 0 && (\n```\n\n`MultiSelectFieldInput` always passed a callback, and did the permission\ncheck *inside* it:\n\n```tsx\nconst handleAddSelectOption = (optionName: string) => {\n  if (!canAddSelectOption) {\n    return;\n  }\n  addSelectOption(optionName);\n};\n```\n\nSo the guard suppressed the click but not the render, which is exactly\nthe reported symptom: the prompt is visible and inert.\n\n## Fix\n\nGate at the prop instead of inside the handler, so the menu item is\nnever rendered when the action is unavailable:\n\n```tsx\nonAddSelectOption={canAddSelectOption ? addSelectOption : undefined}\n```\n\nThe wrapper is now redundant and removed; `addSelectOption` already has\nthe matching `(optionName: string) => void` signature.\n\n`SelectFieldInput` had the byte-identical bug (`SelectInput` gates on\n`onAddSelectOption &&` the same way), so it gets the same change.\n\n## Note on scope\n\n`useCanAddSelectOption` requires `objectNamePlural` from the route in\naddition to the permission flag:\n\n```ts\nconst canAddSelectOption =\n  userHasPermissionToEditDataModel &&\n  isNonEmptyString(fieldName) &&\n  isNonEmptyString(objectNamePlural);\n```\n\nRecord *detail* pages (`/object/:objectNameSingular/:recordId`) have no\n`objectNamePlural`, so the prompt was dead there for **every** user,\nadmins included. This change hides it in that case too, which is the\ncorrect behavior since the click could never have worked.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified manually against a local instance, toggling the patch in and\nout on the same cell so before/after is directly comparable.\n\nCompany `Work Policy` (multiselect) in the Companies table view, typing\na string that matches no option:\n\n| user | route | before | after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Member (no `DATA_MODEL`) | `/objects/companies` | prompt shown, click\ndoes nothing | prompt hidden |\n| Admin | `/objects/companies` | prompt shown, click works | prompt\nshown, click works (navigates to\n`/settings/objects/companies/workPolicy?newOption=…`) |\n| Admin | `/object/company/:id` | prompt shown, click does nothing |\nprompt hidden |\n\n`nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-front` and `nx typecheck twenty-front`\nboth pass.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23410?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaJOICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW9UQADeD/AW2TW0m76KTQttiyviT\nmf3o0hueOuOXSQDq8t0PObtZ/aqrEv79IgJXwzYwRcT6mGq6OKooLieHuR+DexP8\nf0uFIo2qpiKjgrJP9OuGmzs0pJHnsw+4X0O12gxZG6YpRDJL6bPFcAjCzXwqVyQv\nBTwZ/CBWWh8NLNkqmpZkcA+tEcqYmrRG7IMqNcslmn4DKKOWCdZb/94oEVW90RM2\noq3Ff6MQgG9jM3Tb8Zga2o1mqR753IK+9r08+Ad5oIeGwEZeTFcBxB7EIdZ5o1/B\n8KoxnThxJ/1AvjzKn62BTL5ZlK4zx2AillHl/1BuhpDy0zWMbihjFT9BmWQNlqCA\nzWjddJiIF2jpZwYB+BQsBfCsJavcGsAnnUprSTSoPi0jNOlMCnJp1DxcNFfc62vk\ndj950nNhkpuCf+OGPZyWnPHikEOTf57HK/oL3Qd1z2POPShdlB75GodlVY3qPFZJ\npbRj+iDZ1tGQ41Bfy0fR44NUbbh4K8V8q53Cm7eXmMPvwGnQo6ks0guIFq7sMpkh\n6lTfd1sJIq1UT/Eanoicx13Zm10VwC2wVgfVb/ITbi81JMEa4LzfZyePG4yXagCC\nukJbraJF6Wn5CC6HnC1w4v46biftaQ5fF7riRC1SUjw81aeN2bynD+J0rPO2J0fW\ndmwYxnrTEgzNEAqGZzLj\n=g9l/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDM4ZTlkMjMxYmNkOTM5MjMwZjU4NGVjNDlhYzlkZjViNWFjZjllMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/1064ae835bd97db423f73c55cdf84f8c2bcf75f8","sha":"1064ae835bd97db423f73c55cdf84f8c2bcf75f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/1064ae835bd97db423f73c55cdf84f8c2bcf75f8"}],"sha":"38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/38e9d231bcd939230f584ec49ac9df5b5acf9e2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/1064ae835bd97db423f73c55cdf84f8c2bcf75f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:30:19Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T11:30:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Remove ugly page card top-left rounded corner on mobile (#23414)\n\nOn mobile the main page card kept the desktop styling that makes it look\nattached to the navigation drawer: a rounded top-left corner\n(`border-radius: lg 0 0 0`) and a 1px ring box-shadow. Since the drawer\nisn''t rendered inline on mobile, the card is full-bleed and the rounded\ncorner plus hairline border look out of place.\n\nChanges in `PageCardLayout`:\n- Card: `border-radius: 0` and `box-shadow: none` below\n`MOBILE_VIEWPORT`, including the `.dark` override which would otherwise\nwin on specificity\n- Wrapper: drop the `-3px` margin-left / `4px` padding-left that\nreserved the drawer seam\n\nVerified in the running app at 390px width on both the record show page\nand the record index, in light and dark mode: no full-width element\ncarries a shadow or top-left radius anymore.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01N6LfZg7JZ2FiYiJ9QcNucj)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23414?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"223a0d474d5ad0de108997cd98de9383539b1c35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/223a0d474d5ad0de108997cd98de9383539b1c35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/1064ae835bd97db423f73c55cdf84f8c2bcf75f8","verification":{"payload":"tree 223a0d474d5ad0de108997cd98de9383539b1c35\nparent 897d29b603cff97fb8231bb41bf3e54258bbc6b6\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1785238219 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785238219 +0200\n\nRemove ugly page card top-left rounded corner on mobile (#23414)\n\nOn mobile the main page card kept the desktop styling that makes it look\nattached to the navigation drawer: a rounded top-left corner\n(`border-radius: lg 0 0 0`) and a 1px ring box-shadow. Since the drawer\nisn''t rendered inline on mobile, the card is full-bleed and the rounded\ncorner plus hairline border look out of place.\n\nChanges in `PageCardLayout`:\n- Card: `border-radius: 0` and `box-shadow: none` below\n`MOBILE_VIEWPORT`, including the `.dark` override which would otherwise\nwin on specificity\n- Wrapper: drop the `-3px` margin-left / `4px` padding-left that\nreserved the drawer seam\n\nVerified in the running app at 390px width on both the record show page\nand the record index, in light and dark mode: no full-width element\ncarries a shadow or top-left radius anymore.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01N6LfZg7JZ2FiYiJ9QcNucj)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23414?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\