os","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/fea06bdd4b5e021344482d7576c23d9abcc620c2","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGZlYTA2YmRkNGI1ZTAyMTM0NDQ4MmQ3NTc2YzIzZDlhYmNjNjIwYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef","sha":"1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef"}],"sha":"fea06bdd4b5e021344482d7576c23d9abcc620c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/fea06bdd4b5e021344482d7576c23d9abcc620c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:51:40Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:51:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(call-recorder): leave call when only recording bots remain (#23053)\n\n## Problem\n\nFixes\n[core-team-issues#2689](https://github.com/twentyhq/core-team-issues/issues/2689).\n\n`everyone_left_timeout` only fires when the bot is the sole remaining\nparticipant, and Recall counts other recording bots as participants. So\nwhen several bots share a meeting, none of them sees itself as alone.\n\nRecall does enable `bot_detection` by default, but it ships an empty\n`matches` list, so the name-based check can never classify anyone. The\nonly detector that actually runs is the behavioural one, at its default\n20 minute grace plus 10 minute timeout. A meeting left with only bots\ntherefore stays open for around 30 minutes, and two Twenty bots in the\nsame call never recognise each other at all.\n\nThis happens when several workspace members are invited to the same\nmeeting and each has the recorder preference on, or when third-party\nnotetakers stay behind after the humans leave.\n\n## What this does\n\nSends a full `automatic_leave.bot_detection` block plus\n`silence_detection`:\n\n- **`using_participant_names`** — the configured recorder name, so\nco-scheduled Twenty bots recognise each other, plus a list of common\nnotetakers. `timeout: 10`, which is Recall''s enforced minimum; their\nexample config shows `5` and the API rejects it.\n- **`using_participant_events`** — a participant that never speaks nor\nshares screen is treated as a bot.\n- **`silence_detection`** — Recall''s documented example values\n(`activate_after: 1200`, `timeout: 300`). Previously unset, so it fell\nback to Recall''s 20 + 60 minute default.\n\nBoth bot detectors activate 5 minutes after the **meeting start time**,\nnot 5 minutes after the bot joins. The bot joins early by a configurable\namount, so anchoring to join time spent the grace period before the\nmeeting existed — at a 10 minute early join, detection would have gone\nlive 5 minutes before the meeting began.\n\n`everyone_left_timeout` is unchanged and still covers the ordinary case.\n\nEffect:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Only bots remain | ~30 min | ~5 min after meeting start |\n| Someone leaves the call open after talking | ~80 min | ~25 min |\n\n## Deferred\n\nDe-duplicating bots per meeting URL, so several `callRecording`s in one\nmeeting share a single bot instead of each spawning one. `bot_detection`\nis still needed for third-party bots, so this ships first.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ehconitin <nitinkoche03@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cd0c21d23e0c7a61b90344668d7996202808ded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/5cd0c21d23e0c7a61b90344668d7996202808ded"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 5cd0c21d23e0c7a61b90344668d7996202808ded\nparent c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1785228700 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785228700 +0000\n\nfix(call-recorder): leave call when only recording bots remain (#23053)\n\n## Problem\n\nFixes\n[core-team-issues#2689](https://github.com/twentyhq/core-team-issues/issues/2689).\n\n`everyone_left_timeout` only fires when the bot is the sole remaining\nparticipant, and Recall counts other recording bots as participants. So\nwhen several bots share a meeting, none of them sees itself as alone.\n\nRecall does enable `bot_detection` by default, but it ships an empty\n`matches` list, so the name-based check can never classify anyone. The\nonly detector that actually runs is the behavioural one, at its default\n20 minute grace plus 10 minute timeout. A meeting left with only bots\ntherefore stays open for around 30 minutes, and two Twenty bots in the\nsame call never recognise each other at all.\n\nThis happens when several workspace members are invited to the same\nmeeting and each has the recorder preference on, or when third-party\nnotetakers stay behind after the humans leave.\n\n## What this does\n\nSends a full `automatic_leave.bot_detection` block plus\n`silence_detection`:\n\n- **`using_participant_names`** — the configured recorder name, so\nco-scheduled Twenty bots recognise each other, plus a list of common\nnotetakers. `timeout: 10`, which is Recall''s enforced minimum; their\nexample config shows `5` and the API rejects it.\n- **`using_participant_events`** — a participant that never speaks nor\nshares screen is treated as a bot.\n- **`silence_detection`** — Recall''s documented example values\n(`activate_after: 1200`, `timeout: 300`). Previously unset, so it fell\nback to Recall''s 20 + 60 minute default.\n\nBoth bot detectors activate 5 minutes after the **meeting start time**,\nnot 5 minutes after the bot joins. The bot joins early by a configurable\namount, so anchoring to join time spent the grace period before the\nmeeting existed — at a 10 minute early join, detection would have gone\nlive 5 minutes before the meeting began.\n\n`everyone_left_timeout` is unchanged and still covers the ordinary case.\n\nEffect:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Only bots remain | ~30 min | ~5 min after meeting start |\n| Someone leaves the call open after talking | ~80 min | ~25 min |\n\n## Deferred\n\nDe-duplicating bots per meeting URL, so several `callRecording`s in one\nmeeting share a single bot instead of each spawning one. `bot_detection`\nis still needed for third-party bots, so this ships first.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ehconitin <nitinkoche03@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaG2sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGR0QAKBuiaRSr1yviH0taSzxePCc\n2Iuw9olXnEwkMKKqaLck/rd31kuLC9b8M2HMaJwphH7WgVOlAfKZr4vctDsnQ5hF\n1OPBVp+0Pz5AsNv1pWemkkS39Mm1ROzqQnN9Rwa1mU2rfYHj