nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c"}],"sha":"1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/1f55234d0bd1abe20e5615dc5830b254a54831ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125115953?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mabdullahabaid","id":125115953,"login":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:06:23Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:06:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: lift root postcss to 8.5.23 (Dependabot) (#23396)\n\n## Summary\n\nClears the root postcss alert\n[1851](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/security/dependabot/1851):\n**GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849** (high) - path traversal in previous source map\nauto-loading (`sourceMappingURL`) leading to arbitrary `.map` file\ndisclosure, vulnerable `<= 8.5.17`.\n\nThe root lockfile carried **two** vulnerable copies, both behind exact\npins with no fixed upstream release:\n\n| Copy | Pinner | Latest release still pins |\n|---|---|---|\n| 8.5.15 | `next` (8.4.31 exact) | 16.2.12 -> 8.4.31 |\n| 8.5.14 | `@mintlify/common` (8.5.14 exact) | 1.0.1051 -> 8.5.14 |\n\nSo no parent upgrade reaches the fix. The existing `next/postcss`\nresolution moves **8.5.15 -> 8.5.23** and a matching\n**`@mintlify/common/postcss`** pin is added, placed alphabetically among\nthe other `@mintlify/*` entries. The caret consumers (`^8.4.38`,\n`^8.4.47`, `^8.5.15`) dedupe onto the same version.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The two copies **collapse into a single `postcss@8.5.23` entry**;\nnothing at or below 8.5.17 remains.\n- `yarn install --immutable` passes.\n- 8.5.23 published 2026-07-24, clears the 3-day npm age gate.\n- `//resolutions` updated with the advisory, both pinners (and their\nlatest-version evidence) and the drop condition.\n\nThe app-lockfile side of this advisory shipped separately in #23340.","tree":{"sha":"df041bff5aee16da10726014ba1d854e2ffa9fa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/df041bff5aee16da10726014ba1d854e2ffa9fa8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c","verification":{"payload":"tree df041bff5aee16da10726014ba1d854e2ffa9fa8\nparent ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1785225983 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785225983 +0000\n\nfix: lift root postcss to 8.5.23 (Dependabot) (#23396)\n\n## Summary\n\nClears the root postcss alert\n[1851](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/security/dependabot/1851):\n**GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849** (high) - path traversal in previous source map\nauto-loading (`sourceMappingURL`) leading to arbitrary `.map` file\ndisclosure, vulnerable `<= 8.5.17`.\n\nThe root lockfile carried **two** vulnerable copies, both behind exact\npins with no fixed upstream release:\n\n| Copy | Pinner | Latest release still pins |\n|---|---|---|\n| 8.5.15 | `next` (8.4.31 exact) | 16.2.12 -> 8.4.31 |\n| 8.5.14 | `@mintlify/common` (8.5.14 exact) | 1.0.1051 -> 8.5.14 |\n\nSo no parent upgrade reaches the fix. The existing `next/postcss`\nresolution moves **8.5.15 -> 8.5.23** and a matching\n**`@mintlify/common/postcss`** pin is added, placed alphabetically among\nthe other `@mintlify/*` entries. The caret consumers (`^8.4.38`,\n`^8.4.47`, `^8.5.15`) dedupe onto the same version.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The two copies **collapse into a single `postcss@8.5.23` entry**;\nnothing at or below 8.5.17 remains.\n- `yarn install --immutable` passes.\n- 8.5.23 published 2026-07-24, clears the 3-day npm age gate.\n- `//resolutions` updated with the advisory, both pinners (and their\nlatest-version evidence) and the drop condition.\n\nThe app-lockfile side of this advisory shipped separately in #23340.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaGMPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMIYQADfVB/z3IaXfo6J9FS/HexIf\nSntxLUSOTfbcO7YWCzzRO9AdxaNIiDlDoPXDUvu+UkT0TCpPUkIC2N0Yj1DjQAfW\n09DZONjgYrKUhXlK9misMqUjo7bZb48uLoxMj8R+54nWpGqTpOwjA+rJQhMRJ7gh\nlEazNZzzx27fHaTEaaaxg6WL5dR1ApVXquyj9naDEzpYJ3SIuXwyOVtT3g/Dd+kG\nHKbimEiZV1zPB+LCboLmdFjdrf+07W0fzAvWxWIreGKow8dpmo/OLdttMcga/dRb\nYiGmA9WrxpS6nM+b7x3+keZyvuoPmydqYiqXYDIbd1TjfsOGGxRofMP4VN+N3qww\nbZ+l4VDpMqwVKuAdIHGTS9y7wUCyZ1nuBDfi8ceQC6s3c4rYRCKLAnM6djse7mXh\nv/VUwdoFcrZdGJuss400wUxruvEpDjWT+ynsv6cUdPBUJEwzfbNgROLMxOvpoiTs\n1sc8DMRGxUgR1FwoF2VJGODm3L9F5vRidb+DuS9sN3VaTkCJbxMmv7MUHvkC6rLf\nkoOhnmQyJo1D59G4pw7SBco8jPA+iEdCo7zrx3rGnh7aiERj2JBDNn2P/g6QKyWv\nm5nVLBC74R1w2asYCrOQ2NXhc1dfOXATUK24lOuu4/JX3eDWZzMzBkEg0eNVylFl\nMnboDJzOmQnuHzuv4eJV\n=ddwr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGM3OTE5NjczYWZlZTM4MDE0MTE1NTlkZmI1NDcyMmRmNDZiYzg3NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4","sha":"ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4"}],"sha":"c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/c7919673afee3801411559dfb54722df46bc876c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:54:24Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:54:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: use cache for view entity lookups (#23384)\n\n## Context\n\nView child mutation guards resolve a parent view before checking access.\nThe lookup service queried PostgreSQL for a single `viewId`, even though\nthe same relationship already exists in the workspace flat-map cache.\n\nWith 15 guards using this service, each guarded mutation could add an\nunnecessary database round trip.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the five workspace-scoped repositories with\n`WorkspaceManyOrAllFlatEntityMapsCacheService`\n- Load only the flat map matching the requested child kind\n- Resolve view fields, filters, filter groups, groups, and sorts by ID\n- Preserve the existing `null` behavior for missing entities\n\nEach lookup is keyed by entity ID, no workspace-wide filtering is\nintroduced.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nOn a warm workspace cache, permission guards resolve the parent `viewId`\nwithout querying PostgreSQL. Cold caches retain the normal workspace\ncache recomputation behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Typecheck reports no errors in the changed file\n- Existing lookup semantics are preserved for all supported entity kinds\nand missing IDs\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23384?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"935b3dd0c762c0605ea817e1b052db280afc5bd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/935b3dd0c762c0605ea817e1b052db280afc5bd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 935b3dd0c762c0605ea817e1b052db280afc5bd6\nparent 19903f89e5ac21a191f64c6837f520ce8cf89364\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1785225264 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785225264 +0000\n\nperf: use cache for view entity lookups (#23384)\n\n## Context\n\nView child mutation guards resolve a parent view before checking access.\nThe lookup service queried PostgreSQL for a single `viewId`, even though\nthe same relationship already exists in the workspace flat-map cache.\n\nWith 15 guards using this service, each guarded mutation could add an\nunnecessary database round trip.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the five workspace-scoped repositories with\n`WorkspaceManyOrAllFlatEntityMapsCacheService`\n- Load only the flat map matching the requested child kind\n- Resolve view fields, filters, filter groups, groups, and sorts by ID\n- Preserve the existing `null` behavior for missing entities\n\nEach lookup is keyed by entity ID, no workspace-wide filtering is\nintroduced.\n\n## Expected impact\n\nOn a warm workspace cache, permission guards resolve the parent `viewId`\nwithout querying PostgreSQL. Cold caches retain the normal workspace\ncache recomputation behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Typecheck reports no errors in the changed file\n- Existing lookup semantics are preserved for all supported entity kinds\nand missing IDs\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23384?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaGBiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADLEQALD9HGTF9ok8ViDBbcA+oXwH\n7kNb5Vt3HnsJATPkUeaWewSuTOkdqoVjLfLLsWRfbBwTQ034MG69pqpjdBIcyXSA\nkX0xFbILnRGZhuTMFM7Gtl8JmCHFFHVplJndG7XgCYQiKRt1SsahFqpyLC1WfeZb\ne0+/Q2tBUBFVjJv9nlmDQtm+6g79Dnz6zZB7iFPSTR4cgiOl/VsJ2SgKXt+kD58I\nkZWyPz7JJo5JORimnY6ZdQNgpGD8hPPNAMphMvHL98oWgP4mUdSNNgyL79ehx5Xl\n7aruaTFH6M5wr6KmLaCaf9g3t5czRuVR7J52Al2cIb/bfqfyfFvw5zP5RYiWG264\nVvk50RjeBxmk/z7dn6XbzfCp//pFEvb+7ekV1IrQVGDXZlUZod0BAiMO6gQ415Gf\n6oAEicOlk1rqEK/Ikd1fyiosguu8/qHPmlUEC68VNcX93SjISjwrWwaQm+1jBlFM\naGcw6dD+3h8UKWsi3nXcwbnsnn2B92rK6wYZgsYb+x4MVHvoMSAul2Z33G32UsTe\nhxcVsCB3Gxae9pCeyv7vtI6BzGBuxd+h3MYJR5HVrONQpIOzgYGjqnHEz6LdMU0c\nL72F+F7E2ygxVJ5l9BYqF5oWKKro5Jy0PRwSihqhQzZxHGnwVbLcAxWwwyjVEbcz\nRJ73dt7EJKbQWxTMsstO\n=Dc7A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGFlMGZmYjEzNzNjYTkyMzQ5ZGI4NmVjZTJhYWNmNmRhNWVjY2MyZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/19903f89e5ac21a191f64c6837f520ce8cf89364","sha":"19903f89e5ac21a191f64c6837f520ce8cf89364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/19903f89e5ac21a191f64c6837f520ce8cf89364"}],"sha":"ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/ae0ffb1373ca92349db86ece2aacf6da5eccc2f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/19903f89e5ac21a191f64c6837f520ce8cf89364/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:54:15Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T07:54:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add indexes for channel webhook subscription external IDs (#23386)\n\n## Context\n\nIncoming Microsoft messaging, Microsoft calendar, and Google calendar\nwebhook notifications resolve their channel through\n`webhookSubscriptionExternalId`.\n\nThe column was added without an index, so PostgreSQL has to scan the\ncorresponding channel table for every notification. Under sustained\nwebhook traffic, these repeated scans add unnecessary database work and\nkeep core database connections occupied longer.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a partial B-tree index on\n`messageChannel.webhookSubscriptionExternalId`\n- Add the equivalent index on\n`calendarChannel.webhookSubscriptionExternalId`\n- Register both indexes in the TypeORM entity metadata\n- Add an idempotent 2.25 fast instance upgrade command to create and\nremove them\n\nThe webhook handlers and their queries remain unchanged.\n\n## Why this design\n\n- The indexes contain only non-null subscription IDs, channels without\nan active subscription do not add index entries\n- A single-column index supports both the equality lookup used by Google\nand the `IN` lookup used by Microsoft\n- The indexes are intentionally non-unique, this preserves existing\nbehavior and avoids making the upgrade fail if historical duplicate\nvalues exist\n- Subscription IDs are read much more often than they are updated, so\nindex maintenance overhead should be negligible\n\n## Expected impact\n\nWebhook channel resolution should require a targeted index lookup\ninstead of a table scan. This reduces database work, shortens connection\noccupancy, and improves latency on webhook notification paths.\n\nThis is a targeted database optimization. It complements the database\npool changes, but is not expected to resolve every source of API tail\nlatency by itself.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Server typecheck passes\n- Oxlint and formatting checks pass\n- Upgrade command uses idempotent `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` and `DROP\nINDEX IF EXISTS` statements\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23386?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"9f5dd8cfc07922d42aa7742320e186a17683690a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/9f5dd8cfc07922d42aa7742320e186a17683690a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/19903f89e5ac21a191f64c6837f520ce8cf89364","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f5dd8cfc07922d42aa7742320e186a17683690a\nparent cc5ff4869dd98b07c07625e064d4f8ef278d1db5\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1785225255 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785225255 +0000\n\nAdd indexes for channel webhook subscription external IDs (#23386)\n\n## Context\n\nIncoming Microsoft messaging, Microsoft calendar, and Google calendar\nwebhook notifications resolve their channel through\n`webhookSubscriptionExternalId`.\n\nThe column was added without an index, so PostgreSQL has to scan the\ncorresponding channel table for every notification. Under sustained\nwebhook traffic, these repeated scans add unnecessary database work and\nkeep core database connections occupied longer.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a partial B-tree index on\n`messageChannel.webhookSubscriptionExternalId`\n- Add the equivalent index on\n`calendarChannel.webhookSubscriptionExternalId`\n- Register both indexes in the TypeORM entity metadata\n- Add an idempotent 2.25 fast instance upgrade command to create and\nremove them\n\nThe webhook handlers and their queries remain unchanged.\n\n## Why this design\n\n- The indexes contain only non-null subscription IDs, channels without\nan active subscription do not add index entries\n- A single-column index supports both the equality lookup used by Google\nand the `IN` lookup used by Microsoft\n- The indexes are intentionally non-unique, this preserves existing\nbehavior and avoids making the upgrade fail if historical duplicate\nvalues exist\n- Subscription IDs are read much more often than they are updated, so\nindex maintenance overhead should be negligible\n\n## Expected impact\n\nWebhook channel resolution should require a targeted index lookup\ninstead of a table scan. This reduces database work, shortens connection\noccupancy, and improves latency on webhook notification paths.\n\nThis is a targeted database optimization. It complements the database\npool changes, but is not expected to resolve every source of API tail\nlatency by itself.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Server typecheck passes\n- Oxlint and formatting checks pass\n- Upgrade command uses idempotent `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` and `DROP\nINDEX IF EXISTS` statements\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23386?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\