w/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/ab3d9212186c1180e1a1090b841dcda5ceeaefe0","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGFiM2Q5MjEyMTg2YzExODBlMWExMDkwYjg0MWRjZGE1Y2VlYWVmZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3","sha":"4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3"}],"sha":"ab3d9212186c1180e1a1090b841dcda5ceeaefe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/ab3d9212186c1180e1a1090b841dcda5ceeaefe0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T16:57:35Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T16:57:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai-chat) fix AI chat tool-output spill leaks: spill learn_tools, cap navigation tools, truncate on spill failure (#23286)\n\n## Context\n\nAI chat spills tool outputs larger than `MAX_INLINE_TOOL_OUTPUT_BYTES`\n(16 kB) to a file and lets\nthe model page them back with `search_output` / `extract_json_paths`.\nThree paths bypass this and\nlet unbounded payloads into conversation history:\n\n1. **`learn_tools` is never spilled.** Tool schemas go inline whatever\ntheir size.\n2. **Navigation tools have no inline cap.** They are exempt from\nspilling by design (they page\n   spilled files), but nothing bounds their own output.\n3. **Spill failure falls back to full inline.** On any spill error the\nservice returns the complete\n   payload with only a warning appended.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`learn_tools` now spills.** `createLearnToolsTool` takes `{\nexcludeTools?, spillLargeOutput? }`\n(same shape as `createExecuteToolTool`); chat execution enables it. Only\nthe bulky `tools`\nschemas are spilled; `message` / `notFound` / `suggestions` stay inline\nand the response carries\na `spilledTools` envelope (fileId, preview, hint) pageable via\n`extract_json_paths`. MCP is\n  unchanged.\n- **Navigation tools get a hard inline cap.** Still never spilled, but\noutput above 16 kB is\nhead+tail truncated with a marker telling the model to narrow the query\nor page with `offset`.\n- **Spill failure truncates instead of inlining.** The fallback returns\nhead+tail within the 16 kB\n  budget with the original byte size in the marker, keeping the warning.\n- New `truncateHeadTail` util: byte-budgeted, marker-aware, UTF-8\ncodepoint-safe.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `tool-output-spill.service.spec.ts`: spill envelope unchanged,\nunder-budget passthrough,\nnavigation cap for both tools (budget respected, marker mentions\n`offset`, no file written),\n  truncated fallback on spill failure with warnings preserved.\n- `learn-tools.tool.spec.ts`: no spill without the option, inline under\nbudget,\n`message`/`notFound`/`suggestions` intact when spilled, spill-failure\nwarnings surfaced.\n- `truncate-head-tail.util.spec.ts`: budget, head+tail+marker,\nmultibyte-safe cuts.\n- 63 tests across 6 suites; `lint:diff-with-main` and `typecheck` green.\n\n## Post-deploy\n\nWatch the `AiChatToolOutputTokens` histogram (p95 should collapse to ~4k\ntokens) and the\n`AiChatInputTokens` / `AiChatCacheReadTokens` ratio on GPT-5-class\nmodels.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23286?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"5517800432a4bd3aca42454d708b437ced0d2672","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/5517800432a4bd3aca42454d708b437ced0d2672"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3","verification":{"payload":"tree 5517800432a4bd3aca42454d708b437ced0d2672\nparent 3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784912255 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784912255 +0000\n\nfix(ai-chat) fix AI chat tool-output spill leaks: spill learn_tools, cap navigation tools, truncate on spill failure (#23286)\n\n## Context\n\nAI chat spills tool outputs larger than `MAX_INLINE_TOOL_OUTPUT_BYTES`\n(16 kB) to a file and lets\nthe model page them back with `search_output` / `extract_json_paths`.\nThree paths bypass this and\nlet unbounded payloads into conversation history:\n\n1. **`learn_tools` is never spilled.** Tool schemas go inline whatever\ntheir size.\n2. **Navigation tools have no inline cap.** They are exempt from\nspilling by design (they page\n   spilled files), but nothing bounds their own output.\n3. **Spill failure falls back to full inline.** On any spill error the\nservice returns the complete\n   payload with only a warning appended.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`learn_tools` now spills.** `createLearnToolsTool` takes `{\nexcludeTools?, spillLargeOutput? }`\n(same shape as `createExecuteToolTool`); chat execution enables it. Only\nthe bulky `tools`\nschemas are spilled; `message` / `notFound` / `suggestions` stay inline\nand the response carries\na `spilledTools` envelope (fileId, preview, hint) pageable via\n`extract_json_paths`. MCP is\n  unchanged.\n- **Navigation tools get a hard inline cap.** Still never spilled, but\noutput above 16 kB is\nhead+tail truncated with a marker telling the model to narrow the query\nor page with `offset`.\n- **Spill failure truncates instead of inlining.** The fallback returns\nhead+tail within the 16 kB\n  budget with the original byte size in the marker, keeping the warning.\n- New `truncateHeadTail` util: byte-budgeted, marker-aware, UTF-8\ncodepoint-safe.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `tool-output-spill.service.spec.ts`: spill envelope unchanged,\nunder-budget passthrough,\nnavigation cap for both tools (budget respected, marker mentions\n`offset`, no file written),\n  truncated fallback on spill failure with warnings preserved.\n- `learn-tools.tool.spec.ts`: no spill without the option, inline under\nbudget,\n`message`/`notFound`/`suggestions` intact when spilled, spill-failure\nwarnings surfaced.\n- `truncate-head-tail.util.spec.ts`: budget, head+tail+marker,\nmultibyte-safe cuts.\n- 63 tests across 6 suites; `lint:diff-with-main` and `typecheck` green.\n\n## Post-deploy\n\nWatch the `AiChatToolOutputTokens` histogram (p95 should collapse to ~4k\ntokens) and the\n`AiChatInputTokens` / `AiChatCacheReadTokens` ratio on GPT-5-class\nmodels.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23286?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY5mRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA95QQAH7pwcXzaSYWFIXX4eF5D3r8\n8jChs+ZJClkGSu3Y6yW4Ung/TTpUJbwn2/ymV3QY3ppEC7Xvzb39WnKWzqJ3SaAM\nrzxHHcirOeQIanIlglW1V1EYn4QRjfnGYXjL5TgyiMlh4XnVo8XRzaoFosiw/xXg\nXSmCqx3HhzIrk6q688ByGOHEA73NpIuyS7IIWZw+y8d/BAzooltvrnpYKYBx74dP\niLyhRuiI72G2Ymgc6MKL6x1xIvzq/Sm/J7pm592p63jeIfq+5UNKQucCZrdaAX/H\nC61rbYEaTsL9My/W0H/dnjGg+5qzJtw8slJ+mnQTd7peYFxxayzYDs7hqlSK5rTj\nz8E7TLtfn/R74Qv1PFv3U53+VRaNh/SpYCVZWBa0uI30iEyL5Dw/2COs7Z1bWoYw\nVQwsgzRY/squ4p6boYnWxItkYDL4G6TzNc02/AnecCfalIhzrQ5iw895dx0qnYJv\nfd71rt73KKN6oF9yNTz7RWCCiYTP03rRui4a+jh9uSE8t8L9/E1n2vffUxeRK/lF\nsp+Ph+WUCO7xVkTb5arZ7Jp+IBXRdxF8vTAAjTrEcosjoKIBTgNlTHIj+KGjJvTZ\nYPtpz2aeUpOU4Zmdvo+8tX2uDryOqyPabtymELur6C6GUXqCZIBk2VkqHY9WWgLc\nKU37a44W+nZKwv0f7df5\n=Bdl4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDQ4NTE0ODllYmNmMzVmNWUzN2M0ODhkZTU5ZTcyMjNmZTU5ZjU4YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b","sha":"3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b"}],"sha":"4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/4851489ebcf35f5e37c488de59e7223fe59f58a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T16:50:57Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T16:50:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): index page-layout FKs to fix workspace cleanup timeout (#23289)\n\nThe cleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob cron timed out every run (Sentry monitor\n\"a timeout check-in was detected\"): hard-deleting soft-deleted\nworkspaces hung on `DELETE FROM core.pageLayout`, hit the 10s query\ntimeout, rolled back, so those workspaces were never destroyed and got\nretried hourly.\n\nRoot cause: the FKs in the pageLayout -> pageLayoutTab ->\npageLayoutWidget tree had no usable index on the referencing column. The\nexisting indexes lead with workspaceId and are partial (\"deletedAt\" IS\nNULL), so ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL fell back to full sequential\nscans of the shared core tables per deleted row; on layout-heavy\nworkspaces this exceeded 10s.\n\n- Add non-partial FK-column indexes on pageLayoutTab(pageLayoutId) and\npageLayoutWidget(pageLayoutTabId)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23289?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"09ea79d848a0ad89b9257154e23410ae9a0cf94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/09ea79d848a0ad89b9257154e23410ae9a0cf94f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b","verification":{"payload":"tree 09ea79d848a0ad89b9257154e23410ae9a0cf94f\nparent 45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784911857 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784911857 +0000\n\nfix(server): index page-layout FKs to fix workspace cleanup timeout (#23289)\n\nThe cleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob cron timed out every run (Sentry monitor\n\"a timeout check-in was detected\"): hard-deleting soft-deleted\nworkspaces hung on `DELETE FROM core.pageLayout`, hit the 10s query\ntimeout, rolled back, so those workspaces were never destroyed and got\nretried hourly.\n\nRoot cause: the FKs in the pageLayout -> pageLayoutTab ->\npageLayoutWidget tree had no usable index on the referencing column. The\nexisting indexes lead with workspaceId and are partial (\"deletedAt\" IS\nNULL), so ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL fell back to full sequential\nscans of the shared core tables per deleted row; on layout-heavy\nworkspaces this exceeded 10s.\n\n- Add non-partial FK-column indexes on pageLayoutTab(pageLayoutId) and\npageLayoutWidget(pageLayoutTabId)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23289?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY5gBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAstYQAHcdqyicu5beS9qgHLjYq04W\nz4Yk9rGIDAjsf4K3qwYFxHCCkdqnYBS1i0Q6zb4DILoYIqDJkrd9IkE1O7rfxUGL\n4Rx0JLf4b2/D2j7GH20b9bkJWNTwej9gV8iF0wNWcqdPhUjAYDZxUxbx+TK1iuTu\nS8XrCHWt0V2HT4d93b8hOb/SNXw4k4HVCG29P4bkJ/sVId91DjYMZ2c0Oa0avQ+6\nrlmZ1JeHlt+EX3hae/pszmb00NzN2bmImbn87y6IkLeT/1+X0i44J19vjNEZC7j4\n5aOoIK6b3Pf48SY/vH2QJTtrEjQpt6jwudcphly2XyQ0xifnWPIWQtvtfa5xSKPl\neCJdU5Ks2a/ZlUXwbEONI4zR3nmzvO3dUp1WJl/c30HqtAvoBjnKMME5gmIS949O\njC0ZrTmQ91DocK7c241NeYRvEcQFSyIL//QvzP/msWJ+TDTwsATuC3jp9nf6hWf3\nyqGowae4uyRO8JUrERARMkxsjI8dHHn8J/dvUyRIil3Se/9cx98HYijBYLJ25vFb\nesesEf/9Z1zPnodMUPvCmIa+vB8r8xEWhaMKdOvSHax+iIoWKLSUERveslFV7JWR\nlTiPWtxTxqQ+euicMiTcV6L+sTavtFtmxlvx0eCAUF0yFe0Zggd7KChHwq3m9/uW\nXZTEFRwQPtacA6+PB12Y\n=q+MJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDNhMTA2N2VjNmRiNjY0NzM3ZTNhMTBkNWIzNjQzYjljNzNiOWEwOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131","sha":"45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131"}],"sha":"3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/3a1067ec6db664737e3a10d5b3643b9c73b9a08b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T16:23:17Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T16:23:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(billing): make logic function executions free for exempt apps (#23255)\n\n## Problem\n\nWorkspaces get 5 free credits/month to run logic functions, AI and\nworkflows. When a user imports their mailbox with the\nonboarding-suggested **Call Recorder** and **Last contact** apps, each\nimported message/calendar event fires those apps''\ndatabase-event-triggered logic functions, and each execution bills a\nflat 100 micro-credits. A single import can fire tens of thousands of\nexecutions and drain the entire monthly allowance before the user has\ndone anything else.\n\nThe trigger pipeline has no notion of \"this came from sync\", and logic\nfunction executions are metered per record (one job per imported\nrecord), so the burn is unavoidable today.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep a static list of billing-exempt app identifiers\n(`MARKETPLACE_BILLING_EXEMPT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS` — Call Recorder and\nLast contact) and check it in the logic-function executor''s billing step\nvia a small `isBillingExemptApplication(universalIdentifier)` utility.\nWhen the running app is exempt, the per-invocation meter records\n`creditsUsedMicro: 0` and skips the credit decrement.\n\nScope is deliberately narrow: only the automatic per-invocation meter is\nexempted. Anything the function itself charges via `chargeCredits` (the\nseparate `/app/billing/charge` endpoint) and any AI token usage keep\nbilling and keep their enforcement, so a free app can still charge for\nreal paid work (e.g. Call Recorder''s per-recording charge, People Data\nLabs enrichment) and AI usage still throws on credit exhaustion.\n\nThere is no DB column, migration, cache, admin UI, or per-registration\nstate — the exemption is derived entirely from the app''s\n`universalIdentifier` against the in-memory list, so it applies\nuniformly to fresh and existing installations.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `isBillingExemptApplication` utility over the exempt-apps constant,\nwith a unit test.\n- Logic-function executor consults the utility to decide\n`creditsUsedMicro` (0 for exempt apps, 100 otherwise) and only\ndecrements credits for non-exempt invocations.\n\n## Notes / follow-ups\n\n- This fixes the billing drain but not the execution burst: an import\nstill fires the real isolate executions for zero user-visible benefit\nover the apps'' existing batch backfill. Suppressing database-event\ntriggers during historical import is a complementary follow-up worth\ndoing for infra cost and rate-limit reasons.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `nx typecheck twenty-server` / `nx typecheck twenty-front`\n- [x] Server unit tests (`isBillingExemptApplication`) pass\n- [ ] Manual: install Call Recorder / Last contact, import a mailbox,\nconfirm credits are not consumed by their logic function executions\nwhile AI usage and in-app charges still bill","tree":{"sha":"5504509cea45047c3d25b07e07ea4ba9ffa03575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/5504509cea45047c3d25b07e07ea4ba9ffa03575"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131","verification":{"payload":"tree 5504509cea45047c3d25b07e07ea4ba9ffa03575\nparent d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1784910197 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784910197 +0200\n\nfeat(billing): make logic function executions free for exempt apps (#23255)\n\n## Problem\n\nWorkspaces get 5 free credits/month to run logic functions, AI and\nworkflows. When a user imports their mailbox with the\nonboarding-suggested **Call Recorder** and **Last contact** apps, each\nimported message/calendar event fires those apps''\ndatabase-event-triggered logic functions, and each execution bills a\nflat 100 micro-credits. A single import can fire tens of thousands of\nexecutions and drain the entire monthly allowance before the user has\ndone anything else.\n\nThe trigger pipeline has no notion of \"this came from sync\", and logic\nfunction executions are metered per record (one job per imported\nrecord), so the burn is unavoidable today.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep a static list of billing-exempt app identifiers\n(`MARKETPLACE_BILLING_EXEMPT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS` — Call Recorder and\nLast contact) and check it in the logic-function executor''s billing step\nvia a small `isBillingExemptApplication(universalIdentifier)` utility.\nWhen the running app is exempt, the per-invocation meter records\n`creditsUsedMicro: 0` and skips the credit decrement.\n\nScope is deliberately narrow: only the automatic per-invocation meter is\nexempted. Anything the function itself charges via `chargeCredits` (the\nseparate `/app/billing/charge` endpoint) and any AI token usage keep\nbilling and keep their enforcement, so a free app can still charge for\nreal paid work (e.g. Call Recorder''s per-recording charge, People Data\nLabs enrichment) and AI usage still throws on credit exhaustion.\n\nThere is no DB column, migration, cache, admin UI, or per-registration\nstate — the exemption is derived entirely from the app''s\n`universalIdentifier` against the in-memory list, so it applies\nuniformly to fresh and existing installations.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `isBillingExemptApplication` utility over the exempt-apps constant,\nwith a unit test.\n- Logic-function executor consults the utility to decide\n`creditsUsedMicro` (0 for exempt apps, 100 otherwise) and only\ndecrements credits for non-exempt invocations.\n\n## Notes / follow-ups\n\n- This fixes the billing drain but not the execution burst: an import\nstill fires the real isolate executions for zero user-visible benefit\nover the apps'' existing batch backfill. Suppressing database-event\ntriggers during historical import is a complementary follow-up worth\ndoing for infra cost and rate-limit reasons.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `nx typecheck twenty-server` / `nx typecheck twenty-front`\n- [x] Server unit tests (`isBillingExemptApplication`) pass\n- [ ] Manual: install Call Recorder / Last contact, import a mailbox,\nconfirm credits are not consumed by their logic function executions\nwhile AI usage and in-app charges still bill","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY5F1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtL8QAAM5nnQ+pFenTf00oGeagQev\nG8J8TFDgmQgsdhv08ScDt3VGYjBOGvX8g3vgPMPR4WXiRZrdybvxbscUTUv3LT29\nSICOrZfGeRlYH1uM6FARqacKeYty7p3Yv822EFI2vcfmbWLtW5eVO2t2BtmiaNVx\ndGbzf3omnQDugTG7V0F9E1sdxYwzv9fPV4ptNkYJ1zScLyjPvHYdE0O+1Qoyn+7W\nTw249y09K8/4u2OmJG7fWz+wh3LwbVViAZW81k/mMaN4yiEonXGeAN+aHB99ilVL\nOq/e59pN8YcjJVED92SUqQEds+uZ+/wN9bE5P04DsMMYriy9OOm1Irz0TFtsT7Kz\nm54VQKx2YBU8Qg4v92n14GqqmhoRXCUjKPSZJ7UR0yG9mKjFhhVcHNO88z13smdj\nWv139sIgIB3BPHrTrj5XiyBZV0Th0iKfZG0lX1Nj4qoexuJNaGN7LnVNTBHlWshP\ngD9qsbcPnGeocUw4Eluk9DAtaS0lS43R1OY2VSelzRU124jJbe8MjLfqSBgmnLyw\n6TdYwE2DK1Bo8rib2FTfUUScGdy19b1rm2Kn1qVhiYR/tovwVnrh1lU7FyUooOAt\nVRqzImY1gL1VYVx2ALlsurY5wDa99QQWZuTPalni3zVMldH4PZcw+N/BJPg0sVbQ\nr766N3PJ4tmP+hoZziJO\n=uiEH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKDQ1ZjkyYjY3NjM3OTFkY2MwNWE3MGQ4MGIxYjVlMDI2MmNkZTcxMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52","sha":"d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52"}],"sha":"45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/45f92b6763791dcc05a70d80b1b5e0262cde7131"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T15:49:52Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T15:49:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix system objects bypassing role object permission overrides (#23280)\n\n## Bug\n\nFixes #23062 (security). A workspace member whose role denies all object\naccess could still read/mutate system-object records (messages, calendar\nevents, and related system objects). System objects bypassed explicit\nrole-level object permissions.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `workspace-roles-permissions-cache.service.ts`, the per-object\npermission helper resolved values as:\n\n```ts\n(isSystem ? true : (overrideValue ?? defaultValue))\n```\n\nFor every non-workflow, non-workspace-member system object this forced\n`read`/`update`/`softDelete`/`destroy` to `true`, so an explicit deny\noverride on the role was never consulted.\n\n## Fix\n\nFlip the precedence so an explicit role override wins, and the\n`isSystem` default only applies when the role provides no override:\n\n```ts\noverrideValue ?? (isSystem ? true : defaultValue)\n```\n\nBecause the override fields are `boolean | undefined`, `??` correctly\nhonors an explicit `false` while still falling back to the system\ndefault (`true`) when the role has no override row for that object.\n\nWorkflow objects (settings-gated via the `WORKFLOWS` flag) and\nworkspace-member objects (settings-gated, always readable) are handled\nin separate branches and are unchanged, so their intended defaults do\nnot regress.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-server` passes.\n- Typecheck: no new errors from this change (pre-existing unrelated\nfailures in `twenty-shared` date-filter utils only).\n- Manually verified on a local instance that a deny-all role no longer\nhas read access to system objects.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23280?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"0b04ba9e364c81856e8cd8e2c83e74c5db26e506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/0b04ba9e364c81856e8cd8e2c83e74c5db26e506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b04ba9e364c81856e8cd8e2c83e74c5db26e506\nparent bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1784908192 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784908192 +0000\n\nFix system objects bypassing role object permission overrides (#23280)\n\n## Bug\n\nFixes #23062 (security). A workspace member whose role denies all object\naccess could still read/mutate system-object records (messages, calendar\nevents, and related system objects). System objects bypassed explicit\nrole-level object permissions.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `workspace-roles-permissions-cache.service.ts`, the per-object\npermission helper resolved values as:\n\n```ts\n(isSystem ? true : (overrideValue ?? defaultValue))\n```\n\nFor every non-workflow, non-workspace-member system object this forced\n`read`/`update`/`softDelete`/`destroy` to `true`, so an explicit deny\noverride on the role was never consulted.\n\n## Fix\n\nFlip the precedence so an explicit role override wins, and the\n`isSystem` default only applies when the role provides no override:\n\n```ts\noverrideValue ?? (isSystem ? true : defaultValue)\n```\n\nBecause the override fields are `boolean | undefined`, `??` correctly\nhonors an explicit `false` while still falling back to the system\ndefault (`true`) when the role has no override row for that object.\n\nWorkflow objects (settings-gated via the `WORKFLOWS` flag) and\nworkspace-member objects (settings-gated, always readable) are handled\nin separate branches and are unchanged, so their intended defaults do\nnot regress.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-server` passes.\n- Typecheck: no new errors from this change (pre-existing unrelated\nfailures in `twenty-shared` date-filter utils only).\n- Manually verified on a local instance that a deny-all role no longer\nhas read access to system objects.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23280?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY4mvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3h8QAEsTIxmoAog40y5oOgSunfpl\nuEUI8YQ+fAnK5Fxx0pRB5B2BU/0erXiKztPrzBLWjKo9VqRdfFwxpSoqekL/Twvi\nLQA/aF8K50bxIfcpbgCNq9x65Fj2rRVvWteDgZUzZWWl8WNlxWi6IfVjbAtxQiHB\nzhn26l+U5V0vPRVeUDV6ztfYbrm8NJh2tFhL3toxHCl0lvz9ubsl+b45uSTv/4Zf\nVr41IJtuy8d1P6OGuvYdB8X04UaIo7F+yJ6IF8iUzY2HUFMwXWFg4+FvPIlq5Qkq\n2HArTXx+rl5ry7BrbJyVj7bh8oxnS9AyRuC1bZaU1MNBb4smFBbUUn6fE1ygxm1w\ndPeys4xWTU1YoiCPWuZGMD5oraSrzgzTXNkp4el4t85Jo04jXMgy4VyCbjW59Zjk\nlgAYk8w6Rs8IIdDeZ+60/zhxigY59HnpDigod9E+VaNjaJ+nDo1QCfNbICgtrTCC\njzGllTeoFUEStWTwZiGZrbGQV6uY9PuPX/cFJ7TX8mBZFuLXlQtTL98/CLpe0mgA\nL2GZuLgu4Qscka6a+auxnrOlOOO3rsV+PDYTC0Gg9OpQka4yCFG9Jvl81A/bH/R4\n3oCRWxdTwP2cVMC4aUliKCyjU/ScJCDi7aTtTajlIbOhAINbfKd4/1ZQW92uFv9P\ntqXBNls6YlbBuI+X+58O\n=qu/I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGQ2YzE4NmE3MWUzZTdlNjI3Mjc5ZWE0ZThmYmNmYWVhMzZiMWRhNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118","sha":"bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118"}],"sha":"d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/d6c186a71e3e7e627279ea4e8fbcfaea36b1da52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T15:32:33Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T15:32:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: move add-agent-foreign-key-to-role-target instance command to 2.25 (#23285)\n\n## What\n\nMoves the `add-agent-foreign-key-to-role-target` fast instance command\nfrom `2.24.0` to `2.25.0`.\n\nIntroduced in #23206, the command was registered under version `2.24.0`.\nSince `TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION` is now `2.25.0`, `2.24.0` is an\nalready-released version, so its instance commands do not re-run on\nupgrade and the foreign-key migration would never execute.\n\nThis is the same issue #23271 fixed for the message-list-members\nbackfill workspace command.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Moved the command file from `upgrade-version-command/2-24/` to `2-25/`\n(renamed the file prefix).\n- Updated the decorator from `@RegisteredInstanceCommand(''2.24.0'', ...)`\nto `(''2.25.0'', ...)`.\n- Updated the import in `instance-commands.constant.ts` to the new\nrelative path and reordered both the import and the array entry to sit\nafter the 2-24 commands.\n\nThe timestamp (`1784820332810`) and command logic (`up`/`down`) are\nunchanged.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01KpCb9BK1eoM1WWXJU6g95e)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23285?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"212dfacdaafef9e1d7c61e83593c0606feb58b69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/212dfacdaafef9e1d7c61e83593c0606feb58b69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118","verification":{"payload":"tree 212dfacdaafef9e1d7c61e83593c0606feb58b69\nparent 0d876eb714b5917edcb8517dd29e7ec4796d0bff\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1784907153 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784907153 +0000\n\nfix: move add-agent-foreign-key-to-role-target instance command to 2.25 (#23285)\n\n## What\n\nMoves the `add-agent-foreign-key-to-role-target` fast instance command\nfrom `2.24.0` to `2.25.0`.\n\nIntroduced in #23206, the command was registered under version `2.24.0`.\nSince `TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION` is now `2.25.0`, `2.24.0` is an\nalready-released version, so its instance commands do not re-run on\nupgrade and the foreign-key migration would never execute.\n\nThis is the same issue #23271 fixed for the message-list-members\nbackfill workspace command.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Moved the command file from `upgrade-version-command/2-24/` to `2-25/`\n(renamed the file prefix).\n- Updated the decorator from `@RegisteredInstanceCommand(''2.24.0'', ...)`\nto `(''2.25.0'', ...)`.\n- Updated the import in `instance-commands.constant.ts` to the new\nrelative path and reordered both the import and the array entry to sit\nafter the 2-24 commands.\n\nThe timestamp (`1784820332810`) and command logic (`up`/`down`) are\nunchanged.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01KpCb9BK1eoM1WWXJU6g95e)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23285?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY4WiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXGMQAJkSX4WnPz3LsNcvt6tQf2c3\nkDEfiIQ7bGYkO3zPbsjD5cxtOHCeILq3jpy94EBtrlG2MgJrFYvlBGC870JNW0IS\neTzMHEwfhreCby47N0c9NlipmjpF0jDoDbV8WJzq9v6I+S2hQJHJ18Jmr8YHeOQI\nBvQCeH3lbfDrv6Fq361YRtu2bg5HHeI7IZA1vNA9gQwUnpu8r8AqBMjK0Ue0jV2O\ntpK88X45+g6xYso3MVmks23DGe5YRtxrwuK4evv/CuPU8laQ0q2/vI9GYBiMr6ru\nVdDcu7jjTSdwAglMYlKl0zhpKdHv74IdaARYW1rEYRo+1Id1icepiEBAqMzAtNE5\n7BWy9zIREnGd7m9A3rh1xCcsLFrh1PgFFrszI22C5m/6XlCvwtY/GoIWO/aJYMYA\nNXWWdjV/Xy1AQzYKjN+iTIvkh3l5KlccnWLlJDxubp6WMor87z0PTm8DCjXLQL4u\n9U3ZXGmwx+I4l7sv50OfVfE1JKBO9GugC6YPwszf+bQ37hboLitUmo3LH6T1P1Sm\nDK3lurIns2M3QvnREoX3UGF/zz0qulofTlO8T5gGXtYWuGn9et+X1gTz0MfniFEc\nA5sV+ZRmb/2NTHVF6yNblGOSp8pnI/AXYD/03E3M4EtLPmXkPWX0UUarD2lROosi\n1yP6Kww0uBPINdmjksl+\n=s9Qx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118","node_id":"C_kwDOTn4gOtoAKGJjNzkyMmRhN2Q4ZTlhMzc0YTZjMTA4Njk3NDdmZTFhNzg0N2ExMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commit/0d876eb714b5917edcb8517dd29e7ec4796d0bff","sha":"0d876eb714b5917edcb8517dd29e7ec4796d0bff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/0d876eb714b5917edcb8517dd29e7ec4796d0bff"}],"sha":"bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/bc7922da7d8e9a374a6c10869747fe1a7847a118"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125115953?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mabdullahabaid","id":125115953,"login":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/commits/0d876eb714b5917edcb8517dd29e7ec4796d0bff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T15:21:32Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T15:21:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: lift axios/tar/brace-expansion/body-parser across app lockfiles (Dependabot) (#23267)\n\n## Summary\n\nSweeps the **twenty-apps lockfiles** for this week''s advisory wave:\nrecursive `yarn up` for **axios, tar, brace-expansion, body-parser** in\neach of the 12 apps with open Dependabot alerts (hello-world, postcard,\nself-hosting, twenty-partners, call-recorder, people-data-labs,\ntwenty-discord, twenty-exa, twenty-fireflies, twenty-last-contact,\ntwenty-linear, twenty-slack).\n\nAll moves fit the declared ranges (apps carry these transitively via\n`twenty-sdk`, whose `axios ^1.16.0` and deep tar/brace chains are\ncarets), so the diff is **lockfile-only** across all 12 manifests - no\nresolutions, no `package.json` changes. axios -> 1.18.x, tar -> 7.5.20\n(critical GHSA-23hp-3jrh-7fpw chain), brace-expansion -> 1.1.16 / 2.1.2\n/ 5.0.7, body-parser -> 1.20.6 / 2.3.0.\n\nThe second commit narrows scope to apps only: the twenty-server fixture\nprojects (seed-dependencies, common-layer-dependencies) move to a\ndedicated PR because seed-dependencies'' yarn.lock is checksum-coupled to\n`DEFAULT_YARN_LOCK_CHECKSUM` in\n`get-default-application-package-fields.util.ts`; it also drops\naccidentally committed `.yarn/install-state.gz` artifacts.\n\n## Deliberately not covered\n\n- **sharp**: every path is minor-locked at `^0.34.5` (including\ntwenty-sdk latest) - separate PR bumping twenty-sdk''s range.\n- **react-router / react-router-dom**: no fixed release on the 6.x line\n(fix is the v7 major); tracked separately.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Vulnerable-version scan across all 12 lockfiles: no axios <1.18, tar\n<7.5.19, brace-expansion below 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.7, or body-parser below\n1.20.6/2.3.0 remains.\n- `yarn install --immutable` passes in each app.\n- All fix versions clear the 3-day npm age gate.","tree":{"sha":"34c6b198562e937dfef871197406be606318f158","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/34c6b198562e937dfef871197406be606318f158"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/0d876eb714b5917edcb8517dd29e7ec4796d0bff","verification":{"payload":"tree 34c6b198562e937dfef871197406be606318f158\nparent 7067f6ef88762ec1aba131e36a434aa2298ca23a\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1784906492 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784906492 +0000\n\nfix: lift axios/tar/brace-expansion/body-parser across app lockfiles (Dependabot) (#23267)\n\n## Summary\n\nSweeps the **twenty-apps lockfiles** for this week''s advisory wave:\nrecursive `yarn up` for **axios, tar, brace-expansion, body-parser** in\neach of the 12 apps with open Dependabot alerts (hello-world, postcard,\nself-hosting, twenty-partners, call-recorder, people-data-labs,\ntwenty-discord, twenty-exa, twenty-fireflies, twenty-last-contact,\ntwenty-linear, twenty-slack).\n\nAll moves fit the declared ranges (apps carry these transitively via\n`twenty-sdk`, whose `axios ^1.16.0` and deep tar/brace chains are\ncarets), so the diff is **lockfile-only** across all 12 manifests - no\nresolutions, no `package.json` changes. axios -> 1.18.x, tar -> 7.5.20\n(critical GHSA-23hp-3jrh-7fpw chain), brace-expansion -> 1.1.16 / 2.1.2\n/ 5.0.7, body-parser -> 1.20.6 / 2.3.0.\n\nThe second commit narrows scope to apps only: the twenty-server fixture\nprojects (seed-dependencies, common-layer-dependencies) move to a\ndedicated PR because seed-dependencies'' yarn.lock is checksum-coupled to\n`DEFAULT_YARN_LOCK_CHECKSUM` in\n`get-default-application-package-fields.util.ts`; it also drops\naccidentally committed `.yarn/install-state.gz` artifacts.\n\n## Deliberately not covered\n\n- **sharp**: every path is minor-locked at `^0.34.5` (including\ntwenty-sdk latest) - separate PR bumping twenty-sdk''s range.\n- **react-router / react-router-dom**: no fixed release on the 6.x line\n(fix is the v7 major); tracked separately.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Vulnerable-version scan across all 12 lockfiles: no axios <1.18, tar\n<7.5.19, brace-expansion below 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.7, or body-parser below\n1.20.6/2.3.0 remains.\n- `yarn install --immutable` passes in each app.\n- All fix versions clear the 3-day npm age gate.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY4MrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADY8QAIoZ5lmtdNqFskmflAv0a9N2\njbB4WK3WM/7Ep3MwUORJpdkR0kho4NMqKjxLSHQrDRTxGo4VP8+o3aK9UIORz0xr\nhDU4W6v5h3m/Xe3FH/4b2uJlhVAEQEUTEIOsPu07wR5TXnjce0m0Jbg8IPZYnyQ6\n8A6ZKPUg7w8uoWFWXF+jCOUD8roe+PBG73/KLsxip1+W/tXfJ+TdlegwhT1t7Wa9\nEuFeUuU0JHF5NjXiGEvIj5y5uo2VOkj/ddOubepI6Fo90BeG6/eaQHUOJDu8VeG8\nSWVg73Twiu4qaM8xT6Yx+AZjR8kdCC1DEw8H9fww7IAUADlHseWuzor6ag6/T1Zz\nAuvJaR0d/7hOc0n3KxwZu4+xM2DQIMi2OfjeCCUaQy0AIjv1dCMjzlhnSUJf9SIc\n/UMnGVlhyAusu4I+A+cE6z/O9pDRKY5XL/Jwvw1JF8sPpMzO2QGn2dXMqk3awnBI\nVw1mJjlvGSftEfrJptdBAymj28NnKZtrH8Io1XKQ6R9FprpC8F/M7pT/+ML89jT4\n7Cn+awGONbGejnaAlcOhbgizG8XdYj/CmVnYJL87frsMHaUm+mhl/shjWfVGjpkL\nlitRdJ6qDDpxHHzmUWzU3UFlaDaKfoWnzCFGaCc+djZQzJAa8j7pe4w10zzIl6Om\n9fstj39z24/RHibNZV++\n=mUn0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T06:28:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/