","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/trees/fc1dd82dec3fc717aa9f8ad63ec5f9ff696afacf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nextpagetech/twentycrm-npt/git/commits/7067f6ef88762ec1aba131e36a434aa2298ca23a","verification":{"payload":"tree fc1dd82dec3fc717aa9f8ad63ec5f9ff696afacf\nparent 70e1e94e55cdd6932d6360a47c8eff82ad8b5498\nauthor Abdul Rahman <81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1784906487 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784906487 +0000\n\nfix: honor agent rolePermissionConfig in record CRUD (#23248)\n\n## Summary\n- Agent tools were built with the agent’s `rolePermissionConfig`, but\nrecord CRUD ignored it and re-resolved permissions from `authContext`\n(app `defaultRoleId`)\n- CRUD services now pass `rolePermissionConfig` through\n`CommonApiContextBuilder` and the common query runner, so repository\naccess matches the agent role\n- Workflow/chat paths already use the same role for auth and\n`rolePermissionConfig`, so their behavior should be unchanged\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/23248?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY4MHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATuUQAKhyCbxYChTfzW10wjd8FdVw\njGyaGWyxVjIqlKdpy8yC0brkNI1D//i15ygPvK9S5kHOAf1p0pX4LhBOtY8PaCcj\no30YZws/suHgYdU8X2nFpVNNn81XVYODRLII/VOnzvN82BfL+2vxim1vvbbMLpsR\nKRvEB6hcWGEkFR3w4xTroiFH1YMiHKvCfn8eo+4l0t+XOQMUYfAUfhlH0GhUVsAU\nupvySiQvCB+CSbt7qTH